{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm resuming after the interruption. So far I have collected the following:\n\n- The r7 rationale document (read in full).\n- Design documents: header (:13-47), §2.4(iv) (:255-286), §3.1 table including the two new H0 discovery rows (:437-456), §3.2 three scopes (:466-504), §3.3, §8 H0/H1/H2 rows, §8.1 table including the new dialect-arms row and reconciled rows (:822-913), §8.3 (:940-964), §9.1 (:988-1025), §9.3 (:1041-1047), §10 (:1056-1089).\n- Code verification (9 of 16 sites): index.cljc:78 ✓ (numeric fastpath), vm.cljc:404-408 ✓ (bytes->str branching: JVM UTF-8 vs fromCharCode/fromCharCodes), php.cljc:95-101 ✓ (double/parse, Double/parseDouble, js/parseFloat; int/parse, Long/parseLong, js/parseInt), query.cljc:808 ✓ (runtimeType/type), ringbuffer.cljc:167-169 ✓ (IAtom/Atom test), rpc.cljc:114-116 ✓ (rand), adapter.cljc:58-60 ✓ (edn/read-string vs cljs.reader), packet.cljc:67-69 ✓ (runes/codePoints/codePointAt), engine.cljc:929-930 ✓ (runtimeType/type).\n\nThat gives me 9 sites. Cross-host branching claims:\n1. bytes->str: verified precisely — JVM `(String. b \"UTF-8\")`, JS fromCharCode (byte = char code), Dart fromCharCodes. ✓ Doc claim is accurate, and includes \"drop the JVM-only encoding arity unless H2's audit finds callers\" — the arity exists at :406 ✓.\n2. js/parseInt >2^53: JS parseInt returns a Number (float64) — loses precision above 2^53; JVM's Long/parseLong is exact up to int64. ✓ Claim is correct. (cljd's int/parse is also exact.)\n\nStill to verify:\n- Six dropped names: four out-of-closure (dao/jing/content/async.cljc, dao/stream/udp.cljc, dao/space/schema.cljc, dao/jing/stream.cljc), two exempt-catch-only (remote_channel.cljc:399,440,920; ws_project.cljc:376,435). Verify: (i) not in closure-clj.edn; (ii) the arms in remote_channel/ws_project are catch-only. Grep the closure edn for these names, and grep the two files for #?.\n- F4: the 13 print calls in main.cljc — hard to verify exactly without running the resolver; can grep-count the print calls in main.cljc textually (approximate). The doc claims r3's 19 counted text lines including docstrings. Can grep-count println/print/prn/pr/printf/newline/flush/js/console in main.cljc — textual count is approximate (locals may be excluded). Let me grep.\n- antlr/repl.cljc:71 quoted println ✓ (verified by the author in round H0; can be checked immediately).\n- Consistency checks: em-dashes (grep —), long lines >170 (grep .{171,}), duplicate headings, counts: 76 profile entries (table A's N column: 28+5+10+10+6 = 59 for H1… wait, table A includes hash/sign rows for H3. 28+5+10+10+6=59; plus hash+sign rows (unverified) — the claim is 76 total entries. I only read up to line 590 (text row). Remaining rows: dao.host.hash, dao.host.sign, possibly arrays. The total should be 76; can't fully verify without reading the rest of table A. The task says verify \"76 profile entries, seven profile files, five test namespaces, closure totals, random-uuid 27/26/21 don't disagree across sections.\" Seven profile files: integer,float,number,bytes,text,hash,sign = 7 ✓ (mentioned at §8.1 and §10 \"7 dao.host.* files added (5 in H1, 2 in H3)\" ✓ consistent). Five test namespaces: §10 says \"at least 5 test namespaces added (gate-test at H0, conformance/bytes/text at H1, hash-test at H3)\" — that's 5 ✓; H1 slice row names conformance-test, bytes-test, text-test (3) + gate-test + hash-test = 5 ✓. Closure totals 142/140/141/133 consistent at §3.1 and H0 row ✓. random-uuid 27/26/21 at §3.2 ✓, §3.1 entropy row says \"21 random-uuid sites in closure (§3.2)\" ✓, §9.1 mentions five out-of-closure sites ✓.\n- 76 entries: need to check table A rows. Grep the N column of table A… or grep \"76\" in the doc: §4.2 says \"table A is the profile (76 entries)\". Sum the N values: grep the rows. Let me read lines 590-680 to see the rest of table A and count.\n- Cost table: 24 edits = r5's 16 + 8 profile consumers ✓ (:1058-1064), 3 deletions ✓, and \"dao.space.index and UCF rows files no longer 'unchanged'\" — fixed false claims ✓. Consistency with slice list: H2 row says \"all consumers migrate\" and §8.3 adds 8 files ✓; are all 8 named in H2? §8.1 first row lists 9 sites (vm.cljc:404, index:78, repl/query:460, linker/closure:32, ucf/rows:282, php:95,98, register_code:439, register_effects:130, packet:67) = 9 files — but the 8 in cost excludes yin/vm.cljc? r5's 16 already included yin/vm.cljc (H2 consumers list at :784 includes yin/vm.cljc:32). So 8 new = index, repl/query, linker/closure, ucf/rows, php, register_code, register_effects, packet ✓ consistent (vm.cljc already counted). Good.\n- Header review status: says r5 revision?? Line 13: \"Status: design only; nothing commissioned. **Revision r5**, 2026-10-20\" then the r7 row was appended at :22-26. Header says \"Revision r5\" but the doc is r7 — inconsistency! The r7 row exists (:22) and r6 row (:27), but the bolded \"Revision r5\" label was not updated. This is a defect (minor). Verify: line 13 \"**Revision r5**, 2026-10-20, by the Architect\". Yes — the revision label is stale. Finding.\n- Review status accuracy: astra's SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES is against r4's reduced scope; r5 applied M1-M4 \"to be confirmed by non-Claude reviewer before H0 dispatch\" — per the task, cmd confirmed only mechanical fixes in r5/r6; the r7 row says \"non-Claude reviewer must confirm this r7 before H1 dispatch\" ✓. Question asked: is r7's categorization more than mechanical? Yes — the categorization of 16 files into profile-consumer/dialect-arms/deferred, plus two named behavior changes and scope decisions (gate uses transitive closure), are substantive architectural judgments, not mechanical fixes. Therefore my confirmation as non-Claude reviewer is… The header asks \"non-Claude reviewer must confirm this r7\" — not necessarily astra. The task asks me to say whether r7 deserves astra. My view: r7's changes are substantive but a reconciliation of measurement against existing doctrine; the doc's own rule requires non-Claude confirmation (which this review provides); astra's sign-off scope was §2+H0-H4 of r4 — r7 changes §3.1/§3.2/§8.1/§10 within that scope. Recommendation: substantive categorization decisions (especially the two named behavior changes and gate-scope decisions) warrant an astra pass, or at minimum owner approval; my confirmation covers code-vs-doc accuracy, not doctrinal re-review. I'll say this: more than mechanical → worth an astra pass on categorization; this confirmation covers factual accuracy.\n- Is H0 required-change vs not-required unambiguous? §8.1 reconciliation paragraph (:894-913): \"What H0 must change: retag those 16 entries… data change… no tool change; drop nothing\" and \"What H0 does not need to change: totals… unaffected; lanes do not need to rerun beyond gate-test\". Unambiguous ✓. One ambiguity check: retag names \":migration-source, :dialect-arm, :deferred-scope\" — but gate_test's list-1 uses keyword :migration-source etc., and closure.clj's classes don't include :dialect-arm or :h0-unlisted… the closure's class tags come from closure.clj's class-rows (:h0-unlisted is in gate's list-1 only; closure.edn's tags are classes like :profile-internal-pure). Retag says \"the 16 entries in the gate's list 1 and in the committed closure class tags\" — the closure class tags for those 16 are currently mostly :none or something else (e.g., yin.vm has :consumer; rpc has :deferred-entropy). Adding a :dialect-arm class requires modifying closure.clj's class-rows (tool data change — the doc says \"no tool change\", but class tags come from class-rows in closure.clj!). Hmm: \"data change to test and edn output, no tool change\" — but the edn output is generated by the tool; retagging classes requires editing closure.clj's class-rows (which is data within the tool file, arguably). Minor ambiguity: closure.clj's class-rows is exactly where classes are defined, and \"no tool change\" could be misread. Worth an info-level finding: clarify that class-rows in closure.clj (data within the tool file) will be edited, and the edn will be regenerated.\n\nRemaining verifications to run:\n1. Grep closure-clj.edn for async/udp/schema/jing.stream (should be absent) and remote_channel/ws_project (present).\n2. Grep remote_channel.cljc and ws_project.cljc for #? — verify catch arms only.\n3. Count prints in main.cljc.\n4. Confirm quoted println at antlr/repl.cljc:71.\n5. Read rest of table A and sum to 76 (lines 590-680).\n6. Consistency greps: em-dashes \"—\", lines >170, duplicate headings.\n\nThen write the review, <600 words. Let me run these checks in a batch.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Resuming. I have 9 of the 16 sites verified; now the dropped names, table A's entry count, the print"}]}}
