er (build/toolchain implementation)\n7: Implementers:\n8: - Model: claude-opus-5-5 | Assigned: 2026-10-20 07:51:04 +07 | Status: done (round 1, macOS arm64) | Rationale: owner routing 2026-10-20: opus-5.5 implements; resumes the spike session\n9: \n10: ## Verdict\n11: \n12: | Baseline item (§7.8 W8 start criterion) | Verdict |\n13: |---|---|\n14: | 1. Pinned jolt + Chez bootstrapped from a tracked declaration | **DONE** (macOS arm64) |\n15: | 2. `:jolt` alias + `src/jolt` root, no overlays/stubs; spike overlays folded | **PARTIAL**: the alias and root are done. The overlay fold was NOT done because it conflicts with the brief (see 2b). |\n16: | 3. `:jolt` loads `yang.antlr.export` and `yang.antlr.packet` without overlays | **DONE** |\n17: | 4. One `jolt.ffi` defcfn `:blocking` smoke call passes | **DONE**. Collect-safety is NOT established (see 4). |\n18: \n19: **What this means for J0c:** the §7.8 start criterion asks for three things: pinned bootstrap, the alias loading both namespaces, and the `:blocking` smoke. **All three are met on macOS arm64.** The overlay fold is not part of that criterion.\n20: \n21: **Linux x86_64 (shiva): NOT RUN.** shiva also needs Chez 10.4.1 and CMake 4.4.4 provisioned through mise.\n22: \n23: - Worktree: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a`, branch `jolt-j0a` from master `212c45dd9`. Changes are uncommitted and nothing is staged.\n24: - Logs: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/j0a-logs/` (untracked `build/`).\n25: \n26: ## Environment\n27: - Darwin arm64, macOS 26.6.2, Apple clang 21.0.0, babashka v1.13.223.\n28: - Chez 10.4.1 (threaded `#t`) at `~/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme`.\n29: - CMake 4.4.4: `mise install cmake` was run this round. It went into the shared mise install dir at `~/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake`. This is the only thing installed outside the worktree.\n30: \n31: ## 1. Pinned jolt and Chez from a tracked declaration: DONE\n32: \n33: - **`jolt-toolchain.edn`** (new, tracked, repo root) records:\n34:   - the jolt origin `https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt`, full SHA `96d7b8662d7c491722445bf976b2e25e36ce5d63`, and commit date;\n35:   - `:tag :none`, nearest release tag `v0.8.23` (`a0ac71c3f638fe55158bd01b4ecbb0dd3d7545e5`), describe string `vnightly-16-g96d7b866` (ruling 4);\n36:   - all 7 recursive submodule SHAs (`git submodule status --recursive` on the pinned tree);\n37:   - `:patches []` (default 2: none);\n38:   - Chez `10.4.1` via mise, required threaded;\n39:   - CMake `4.4.4` via mise;\n40:   - the observed macOS paths and compiler.\n41:   - Linux is `nil` (not run). `:native {}` (libblake3, ANTLR4 C++ and libcrypto are later rounds).\n42: - **`mise.toml`** (worktree copy): `chezscheme = \"10.4.1\"` and `cmake = \"4.4.4\"`, exact pins. CMake 4.4.4 is what `mise latest cmake` resolved. The main tree's uncommitted `chezscheme = \"latest\"` was not touched.\n43:   - The brief states the owner confirmed the exact-Chez default. §13.2 W6 also asks for that acceptance to be **recorded in §13.2 of the design doc**. I did not edit docs, so the orchestrator should record it there.\n44: - **`bb bootstrap:jolt`** (new `bb.edn` task, running `src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj`):\n45:   - **Toolchain check:** checks Chez and CMake through `mise exec <tool>@<pinned> -- which`. It verifies the exact versions and that Chez is threaded, and never installs anything.\n46:   - **Clone:** if `build/tools/jolt` is absent, it clones the origin, checks out the full SHA detached, and initializes submodules recursively.\n47:   - **Verify:** the HEAD SHA, a clean tree, and all submodule SHAs against the declaration.\n48:   - **Env file:** writes `build/tools/jolt-env.sh` with `JOLT_CHEZ` set explicitly (plus `JOLT_HOME`).\n49:   - **Smoke:** runs `jolt -e '(+ 1 2)'` and expects 3.\n50:   - **Never pulls:** an existing checkout is only verified.\n51:   - Nothing