d nothing.\n78: - Two of the overlays must not be folded as they are anyway:\n79:   - The `dao.jing` overlay stubs SHA-256 with a throw, and the brief allows no stubs.\n80:   - The `integer/host` overlay's bigint `bit-and`/`bit-or`/`bit-xor` are knowingly wrong (§4.4, §5.1).\n81: - None of the four is needed for the baseline closure (item 3).\n82: - **The orchestrator must decide which slice may edit `dao.jing`/`yin.vm` for the fold (J0a round 2 or J1).** Attribution for that fold: the spike session (claude-opus-5-5, 2026-10-19), `collab/1792412960461-engineer-jolt-yin-repl-spike.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md` section 5.\n83: \n84: ## 3. `yang.antlr.export` and `yang.antlr.packet` load without overlays: DONE\n85: \n86: - `bb smoke:jolt` runs `build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj` with the env file sourced. Every run exited 0 with `SUMMARY ok` (`smoke-1.log`, `smoke-2.log`).\n87: - **Closure:** loading `yang.antlr.export` adds exactly `(yang.antlr.export yang.antlr.packet)` to `loaded-libs`. That is asserted.\n88: - **Transit:** none. Nothing from `dao.data`, `dao.stream.transit` or `cognitect.transit` is reached. A separate check found no loaded lib matching `transit|cognitect`. So there is nothing to record as a runtime-loaded transit dependency for this closure.\n89: - **Values:**\n90:   - `packet/code-points \"aé😀\"` = `[97 233 128512]`. This runs the `:clj` branch, `.codePoints` via jolt's String shim, and passes unchanged.\n91:   - `packet/utf8-bytes` gives 7.\n92:   - `export/byte-offsets [97 233 128512]` gives `[0 1 3 7]`.\n93: \n94: ## 4. defcfn `:blocking` smoke: DONE (collect-safety not established)\n95: \n96: - **Assertions** in `src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj`:\n97:   - `usleep` bound `:blocking` returns 0 after at least 200 ms (observed 201 and 204 ms).\n98:   - `strlen` bound `:blocking` on the UTF-8 C string \"aé😀\" returns 7.\n99:   - Both PASS.\n100: - **Collect timing, RECORD only (not asserted).** A full collection (`jolt.host/gc-full!`) ran on the main thread while another thread was inside `usleep(400 ms)`:\n101: \n102: | Call binding | collect start | collect end | call end |\n103: |---|---|---|---|\n104: | `:blocking` | 50 ms | 118 ms | 400 ms |\n105: | plain (no `:blocking`) | 57 ms | 212 ms | 410 ms |\n106: \n107: - **Anomaly:** jolt's own documentation (`stdlib/jolt/ffi.clj:1502-1510`) says a thread in a non-`:blocking` call stays active and the collector waits until the call returns. The plain control did not wait for the call to return. I reproduced this with a raw `Thread` as well as `future`.\n108: - So this observation cannot yet show that `:blocking` is what makes a call collect-safe. I removed my first version of the check, which asserted it, after the control falsified it.\n109: - Possible explanations, none verified: the rendezvous path in `sa-gc-collect` (`host/chez/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss:61-80`), or Chez handling of a thread in `usleep`.\n110: - The long-hash collect-safety gate (§6.3) is later J0a work and will need a mechanism that discriminates.\n111: \n112: ## Commands run (foreground, in the worktree)\n113: ```\n114: git worktree add /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a -b jolt-j0a master   # from the repo root\n115: mise trust\n116: mise latest cmake            # 4.4.4\n117: mise install cmake\n118: bb bootstrap:jolt            # cold, warm, two negatives, restored (logs above)\n119: bb smoke:jolt                # x2 (first with a fresh JOLT_CACHE_DIR; source mode keeps JOLT_AOT_CACHE=0, so no cache was written)\n120: . build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \"$JOLT_HOME\"/bin/jolt -Srepro -Spath -A:jolt\n121: \"$JOLT_HOME\"/bin/jolt -Srepro -Stree -A:jolt\n122: mise exec -- cljstyle check/fix src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj jolt-toolchain.edn deps.edn\n123: ```\n124: - **Wall clock:** bootstrap cold 153.71 s, warm 7.12 s; smoke 7.77 s and then 7.45 s. jolt runs from source, so there is no AOT cache and cold and warm are similar.\n125: - **cljstyle:** my new files pass. `deps.edn` and `bb.edn` already fail `cljstyle check` on master (I checked `git show master:deps.edn`), and none of the reported lines are mine.\n126: - **npm ci:** not needed.\n127: \n128: ## J0a acceptance items NOT done this round (not started)\n129: - Recording the owner's acceptance of the exact-Chez default in §13.2. The value is applied in `mise.toml` and the toolchain file, but this is a doc edit for the orchestrator.\n130: - Folding the spike overlays (2b, blocked by the brief) and the rest of the §4.4 fold/audit sites, including the machine-readable branch inventory and the reached-`src/clj` guard list (`yin.repl.host`, `dao.space.dht`).\n131: - Clean-cache core require of `yin.repl` without overlays. The standard/main dependency audit naming runtime-unexercised dependencies (`cognitect.transit` via `dao.data` and others).\n132: - Reproducing the S arithmetic and the six hashes.\n133: - Vendored native sources: libblake3 and ANTLR4 C++ revisions and hashes, `bb build:jolt-native`, output digests.\n134: - Source/`:jolt/provides`/binary precedence probes.\n135: - `.jolt` in `.cljstyle` `:extensions`, and the kondo `:jolt` feature lane.\n136: - The jolt test runner (`test:jolt` family).\n137: - libcrypto provenance and negative tests, and long-hash collect-safety (see the anomaly in 4).\n138: - The Linux x86_64 platform record on shiva, including provisioning Chez and CMake there.\n139: - Removing overlay paths from classpaths. They were never added here, but the main-tree spike scripts still reference them.\n140: \n141: ## Files changed (worktree, uncommitted)\n142: - Modified: `bb.edn` (tasks `bootstrap:jolt`, `smoke:jolt`), `deps.edn` (alias `:jolt`), `mise.toml` (chezscheme 10.4.1, cmake 4.4.4).\n143: - Added: `jolt-toolchain.edn`, `src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj`, `src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj`, `src/jolt/README.md`.\n144: - Untracked build outputs, not for commit: `build/tools/jolt/` (the pinned clone), `build/tools/jolt-env.sh`