imit":95}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1792458383514,"messageId":"91abdbdd-6cfa-44a4-b327-022b0c7b7b38"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_add538de83cf42b7bd0c3fee","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 125 lines\nNote: showing lines 225-349. More of the file remains. Use offset=350 to continue.\n225: ### 4.2 Source roots: `src/jolt` first\n226: \n227: V: roots are searched outermost-first, and `.jolt`, `.clj`, `.cljc` are tried\n228: within each root (`host/chez/loader.ss:389-395,467-481`;\n229: `jolt-core/jolt/deps.clj:1744-1746,1776-1782`). A later-root `.jolt` does not\n230: beat an earlier-root `.cljc`. So `src/jolt` (a new tracked host source root, not\n231: an overlay) goes before `src/cljc` and `src/clj` in the `:jolt` alias. Verify\n232: the resolved order with `-Spath`, record which file supplies each host override,\n233: and audit aliases whose `:extra-paths` precede `:replace-paths`. J0a keeps a\n234: precedence probe for `:jolt/provides` / `ldr-ns-replaced-rel?` and for built\n235: binaries, whose embedded sources otherwise probe first.\n236: \n237: Listing `src/clj` on the classpath must not load JVM implementations. V:\n238: `yin.repl.host` selects `yin.repl.host.jvm` under `:clj`\n239: (`src/cljc/yin/repl/host.cljc:15-17`), which reaches `dao.stream.ws.jvm`;\n240: `dao.space.dht` selects `dao.stream.datagram.jvm` under `:clj`\n241: (`src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:53-57`). Each selecting branch gets a `:jolt`\n242: guard before `:clj`. The portable `dao.stream.ws` and `dao.stream.datagram` do\n243: not themselves select these JVM namespaces, but they have other host operations\n244: to audit; `dao.stream.ws` also requires `dao.stream.transit` unconditionally\n245: today; removing that is the codec track's work\n246: ([dao.stream.codec.md](./dao.stream.codec.md)), on which J6 depends (§9.4).\n247: \n248: ### 4.3 Build declaration and tasks\n249: \n250: V: root `deps.edn:1-23` supplies dependencies and paths, `:test` (`:30`) uses\n251: Cognitect's runner, `:clj-yin-repl` (`:66`) runs `yin.repl.main`; `bb.edn:34-90`\n252: defines the fast/all/slow lanes and `:96-170` changed/subsystem selection. These\n253: are implementations for other runtimes, not scripts to run unchanged under jolt.\n254: \n255: P: a `:jolt` **host configuration alias**, not a dependency coordinate.\n256: `:replace-paths` selects `src/jolt` before `src/cljc` and audited `src/clj`\n257: content (including the demo), excluding generated Java parser classes and\n258: JS/Dart roots. `:replace-deps` holds the portable source dependencies this lane\n259: needs, versioned from the root; it does not fetch Datomic, http-kit or boring\n260: JVM classes. The resolved closure is verified, not assumed empty. `:jolt-test`\n261: adds test and runner paths; `:jolt-yin-repl` adds `:main-opts`. The alias\n262: mechanisms exist in jolt (`jolt-core/jolt/deps.clj:8-9,1737-1792`, V). The\n263: supported launch is always through the explicit alias so dependencies and native\n264: libraries are reproducible.\n265: \n266: Proposed tasks (P):\n267: \n268: - `bb bootstrap:jolt`: materialize the recorded jolt SHA, submodules and\n269:   declared native dependencies. Explicit update mode advances to a reviewed full\n270:   SHA through `qualify:jolt-upgrade`; ordinary runs never pull.\n271: - `bb build:jolt-native`: mise-driven, pinned-CMake vendored C/C++ builds into\n272:   `build/native/<platform>/`, checked system/Homebrew libcrypto loading, feature\n273:   and loader smoke checks. No download during namespace loading.\n274: - `bb test:jolt`, `test:all:jolt`, `test:slow:jolt`: same `^:slow` and\n275:   `dao.test-slow/guard` semantics. Start with a small tracked `clojure.test`\n276:   runner (explicit namespace discovery, nonzero exit on load/test/error\n277:   failures); prove Cognitect runner compatibility before reusing it. The runner\n278:   is a launcher, not an oracle.\n279: - `test:changed:jolt`, `test:sub:jolt`: extend `src/dev/affected.clj` and the\n280:   existing require-closure mechanism; discover `.jolt` sources; treat\n281:   toolchain/native/alias changes as wide changes. `src/dev/subsystems.edn` stays\n282:   the taxonomy.\n283: - At J8, jolt joins `bb test`, `test:all`, `test:slow` and the changed/subsystem\n284:   dispatch and list output. Before then it is an explicit experimental task; no\n285:   aggregate claims a lane it omits.\n286: \n287: `gen:antlr` remains the JVM build step for generated parsers and gains the\n288: pinned C++ target (§7). Node shadow builds and Dart compilation remain\n289: prerequisites for oracle and cross-host peer tests only. Missing dependencies\n290: fail prerequisites: jolt's README (`:110-115,160-164`) says fetch failures and\n291: unknown aliases may otherwise be skipped or warned.\n292: \n293: ### 4.4 Fold and audit sites\n294: \n295: J0a produces an exhaustive, machine-readable inventory of selected interop\n296: branches and their tests, including every reached `src/clj` namespace and its\n297: planned `:jolt` guard, and every runtime-unexercised dependency the closure\n298: loads. `cognitect.transit` (W2; reached today through `dao.data`,\n299: `dao.stream.cbor`, `dao.jing.stream` and `dao.stream.ws` -> `dao.stream.transit`,\n300: V) must be **absent** from the jolt closure once the codec track has landed\n301: C0-C4 (§9.4), after which no shared namespace requires `dao.stream.transit`;\n302: the inventory then proves the absence rather than listing it as unexercised. If\n303: J0a runs first, the inventory lists `cognitect.transit` as a runtime-unexercised\n304: dependency and names the codec track as what removes it. The sites below are a\n305: verified starting set, not a claim that the 91-namespace closure is portable.\n306: \n307: +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n308: | Site (r7 coordinates)                                                 | Required work                                                                                  |\n309: +=======================================================================+================================================================================================+\n310: | `src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:112-250`                                 | The spike overlay fixed `big`, `b+`, `b-`, `b*`, `bquot`, `bcmp`, `bgcd`; also audit `bsign`,  |\n311: |                                                                       | `bpow`, `b->int:223`, `magnitude-bytes:235`. Chez exact arithmetic; no BigInteger              |\n312: |                                                                       | constructor/valueOf/toByteArray.                                                               |\n313: +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n314: | `cbor.cljc:462-658,993-1012`                                          | Predicates, float carriers and bits, decimal/ratio accessors and exact numeric comparison      |\n315: |                                                                       | still carry JVM representation. Gate the whole scalar surface (§5.2).                          |\n316: +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n317: | `src/cljc/yin/vm/integer/host.cljc:27-28,41-108,115-298`              | Import, carrier predicates, promotion/demotion, truncation, arithmetic, compare, three big bit |\n318: |                                                                       | operations, shifts, magnitude length, radix output. The overlay's bit operations are knowingly |\n319: |                                                                       | wrong; do not copy them (§5.1).                                                                |\n320: +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n321: | `src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:59-85,114-136`                                | SHA and BLAKE3 string/bytes sites branch to one jolt crypto facade; preserve UTF-8, byte-array |\n322: |                                                                       | semantics and lowercase digest text.                                                           |\n323: +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n324: | `src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc:32-40,46-132`                     | Replace the Java boring dependency, for jolt only, with a narrow `.jolt` wire-node writer      |\n325: |                                                                       | (§5.2).                                                                                        |\n326: +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n327: | `src/cljc/dao/data/arrays.cljc:92,138-148`                            | `asort` calls `parallelSort` (`:145`, V); replace for jolt. Audit arraycopy, overlapping       |\n328: |                                                                       | copies and clone.                                                                              |\n329: +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n330: | `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:275-279`                                      | Jolt banner branch before the JVM arm, with recorded jolt/Chez identity; never print `JVM      |\n331: |                                                                       | nil`. Audit rendering at `:364-395`.                                                           |\n332: +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n333: | `src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:11-17,54-85`                        | Remove the unconditional host-parser dependency for jolt; keep the complete catalog and        |\n334: |                                                                       | primitive injection.                                                                           |\n335: +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n336: | `src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:11-30,199-239,873-880,951-959,1212-1364` | Eager storage/network/sign requires, file helpers, exits, JVM cadence/stdin. Port host         |\n337: |                                                                       | mechanisms without duplicating `step-all` or driver semantics.                                 |\n338: +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n339: | `src/cljc/yin/repl/host.cljc:15-17,20-37`                             | Select a jolt WebSocket adapter without requiring `host.jvm`/http-kit. An unsupported          |\n340: |                                                                       | capability is explicit and does not block local startup.                                       |\n341: +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n342: \n343: J0a also adds `.jolt` to `.cljstyle`'s `:files :extensions` (V: absent,\n344: `.cljstyle:14`) and checks that the formatter keeps branch order; runs the\n345: clj-kondo lane over representative `:jolt` arms and `.jolt` files with explicit\n346: feature analysis (V: `.clj-kondo/config.edn` has no `:jolt` setting;\n347: unknown-feature skipping is not linting); and removes all four spike overlay\n348: paths and helper sources from production and test classpaths.\n349: "}]},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_6ac9b720fb17497796c24e11","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 42 lines\nNote: showing lines 496-537. More of the file remains. Use offset=538 to continue.\n496: ### 6.1 The toolchain file and mise-driven builds\n497: \n498: Owner Q4 policy (settled): mise-driven vendored builds of the upstream **BLAKE3\n499: C reference sources** and the **ANTLR4 C++ runtime**, each with license, pinned\n500: source revision and hash in a tracked toolchain file (proposed\n501: `jolt-toolchain.edn`), built with a mise-pinned CMake into\n502: `build/native/<platform>/` by `bb build:jolt-native`, for macOS arm64 and Linux\n503: x86_64. System/Homebrew OpenSSL libcrypto stays external, with a pre-digest path\n504: and version check.\n505: \n506: `jolt-toolchain.edn` (P) records:\n507: \n508: - the full jolt SHA (initially `96d7b8662d7c491722445bf976b2e25e36ce5d63`), the\n509:   GitHub main origin and recursive submodule SHAs;\n510: - the Chez version actually resolved, and `JOLT_CHEZ` set explicitly;\n511: - libblake3 and ANTLR4 C++ runtime source revisions and hashes; ANTLR tool and\n512:   runtime both 4.13.2;\n513: - the exact mise CMake pin (V: `mise.toml` has no CMake today), compiler\n514:   versions and flags, and build output digests per platform;\n515: - the expected libcrypto path and version per platform;\n516: - any local jolt patches, only if proposed default 2 is accepted (§13.2).\n517: \n518: Mise provisions Chez and CMake; the repo task compiles the vendored libraries\n519: (there is no presumed mise libblake3 package). A mise git plugin for jolt is\n520: unnecessary until proved: the repo task owns the jolt CLI clone under\n521: `build/tools/jolt`. No namespace load searches arbitrary system libraries or\n522: downloads anything, and the production gate never falls back silently. J0a\n523: records the exact CMake version, revisions, hashes and output locations; this\n524: document invents none.\n525: \n526: V (r7): jolt's README (`:95-115`) documents threaded Chez 10.x, `JOLT_CHEZ`\n527: precedence and OpenSSL/git prerequisites, and (`:130-164`) the deps aliases,\n528: `-Srepro`, `-Spath`, `-Stree`. `bin/jolt` runs from the checked-in seed; `make\n529: devboot` is optional (`Makefile:1901-1902`), and the Makefile references a\n530: provisioned GCC bundle (`:111-113`). Assumption to verify at J0: the xPack\n531: download/compiler selection; inventory its scripts before enabling it. Devboot\n532: and `jolt build` record compiler/provisioning checksums, use the same Chez and\n533: discard caches on runtime/source change. Source-mode execution is the baseline;\n534: AOT packaging is an additional gate, never the fix for a semantic failure.\n535: \n536: ### 6.2 BLAKE3 over FFI\n537: "}]},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_b648d9385e1347cbb2553251","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 42 lines\nNote: showing lines 596-637. More of the file remains. Use offset=638 to continue.\n596: ### 6.4 Pins and the upgrade gate (owner Q5)\n597: \n598: Owner: \"record the mob's answer\", then \"opus when needed\". Jolt is pinned by\n599: full SHA in `jolt-toolchain.edn`; a suitable release-tagged SHA is preferred;\n600: main remains the upstream development source; nothing updates silently. The\n601: owner or orchestrator triggers the proposed `bb qualify:jolt-upgrade` when an\n602: upstream fix we need lands, when the resolved Chez version changes, or when the\n603: pin is older than about 30 days. Age triggers evaluation, not promotion; a\n604: failing candidate leaves the last passing pin.\n605: \n606: The gate runs on macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64: clean tracked load and resolved\n607: paths; relevant fast/all/slow tests with counts; J1 integer/CBOR/hash fixtures;\n608: shared VM boundary traces; J0b UDP and J0c parser/GC/cache/lifetime regressions;\n609: native-library provenance; J6/J7 peers once they exist. It records candidate,\n610: base and submodule SHAs, exact Chez, patches, native versions, commands, results\n611: and rollback coordinates. No unavailable test passes silently. Early pins\n612: qualify only for the implemented milestone; J8 promotion needs every parity\n613: gate. No numeric JVM-ratio budget exists before J8 evidence.\n614: \n615: Pin and tag (W7; ruled, §13.4 ruling 4). V (read-only git in the local\n616: checkout, 2026-10-20): `96d7b866` is the checkout's `main`/`origin/main` head,\n617: committed 2026-10-19, carries **no tag**, and `git describe --tags` answers\n618: `vnightly-16-g96d7b866`; the nearest release tag the checkout knows is\n619: `v0.8.23` (`a0ac71c3`, 2026-10-17), with `vnightly` (`5ae108e5`, 2026-10-18) a\n620: moving nightly tag. The checkout's tag list is only what it has fetched. All S\n621: and J0b evidence describes `96d7b866`. **J0a keeps `96d7b866`** and records it\n622: in `jolt-toolchain.edn` with \"tag: none; nearest release tag v0.8.23\n623: (a0ac71c3); describe vnightly-16-g96d7b866\". No S claim is re-established.\n624: From the first run of `qualify:jolt-upgrade` onward, Q5 governs as the owner\n625: stated it: a **suitable** release-tagged SHA is preferred, and an untagged SHA\n626: is admissible when it carries a needed upstream fix and is explicitly qualified\n627: through the gate (astra A5). No rule here mandates the newest release. A re-pin\n628: before that first gate run happens only under the reversal condition in §13.4.\n629: \n630: Chez status (R): `mise.toml:8` reads `chezscheme = \"latest\"` (V; the change is\n631: uncommitted per r7); the spike observed 10.4.1. Replacing `latest` with an exact\n632: pin is proposed default 3 (§13.2), not a decision. Until it is disposed of,\n633: nobody changes the selector or claims a repository pin exists; every result\n634: records the resolved version and path, and any resolved Chez change goes through\n635: the upgrade gate.\n636: \n637: ### 6.5 Commands"}]},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_7f59cc55279e40e2a8a2b8dd","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 58 lines\nNote: showing lines 841-898. More of the file remains. Use offset=899 to continue.\n841: ### 7.8 J0c probe and J5 gate\n842: \n843: J0c (P, required, both platforms):\n844: \n845: - generate the actual pinned Python grammar with Cpp, build and load wrapper and\n846:   runtime;\n847: - parse a fixed set: arithmetic, nested indentation/dedent, empty input/EOF,\n848:   non-ASCII and astral characters, malformed syntax, incomplete multiline input;\n849: - marshal into the jolt adapter, run the shared exporter, and require canonical\n850:   CST/diagnostic packet equality with the JVM/Node/Dart oracle for identical\n851:   source/unit/profile, then identical completeness-probe results;\n852: - lowering comparison restricted to a fixed corpus with no integer beyond 64\n853:   bits and no floats, so a J1 numeric gap cannot masquerade as parser\n854:   infeasibility (W8); any J1-attributable diff is reported separately from\n855:   parser feasibility;\n856: - observe C++ token-buffer behaviour rather than assume Java equivalence (JVM\n857:   lazy-buffer NoViableAlt handling differs from JS/Dart, `cst.clj:168-221`);\n858:   require identical first-failure (`:end`/`:early`/nil) and probe results for\n859:   open blocks, brackets, triple quotes and an early error under an open bracket;\n860: - embedded NUL and invalid input policy, bounded-response failure, injected C++\n861:   exceptions, repeated parse/free cycles, sanitizer leak/lifetime checks; no\n862:   exception or pointer escapes, no failed parse publishes a partial successful\n863:   packet;\n864: - two-worker/cache isolation (§7.4), collect-safety and thread/stack evidence\n865:   (§7.5, §7.6), helper provenance and generated digests;\n866: - record library versions, target/helper hashes, commands, result diffs, whether\n867:   unrelated jolt work progresses during a parse, and how limits are enforced.\n868:   Unsupported interruption is disclosed, not passed as cancellation. A toy\n869:   grammar does not count.\n870: \n871: J0c start criterion (W8): J0c starts once the minimum J0a baseline exists,\n872: namely the pinned jolt and Chez are bootstrapped, the `:jolt` alias loads\n873: `yang.antlr.export` and `yang.antlr.packet` without overlays, and one `defcfn\n874: :blocking` smoke call passes. It need not wait for unrelated UDP or codec work.\n875: J0c compares exporter packet values only; J1 owns broad Jing byte/hash parity\n876: and J5 full integration.\n877: \n878: J5 (P, required): extend the probe to the full existing ANTLR/frontend corpus\n879: and standard `(lang :yang/python)` acceptance: byte-span, diagnostic and profile\n880: parity; complete/incomplete/error probes; reset/session behaviour and\n881: malformed-input limits; worker-cache and reset isolation; local-built package\n882: loading from a clean deployment with no JVM/Node process;\n883: missing/incompatible-library refusals; deterministic repeats; lifetime and\n884: exception fault injection from an external harness so a crash fails the test\n885: rather than erasing its report. Acceptance: `1 + 2`, definitions across\n886: submissions, multiline functions, `print`, exceptions, arbitrary integer shifts,\n887: floats and reset match the existing Python REPL suite; PHP and Clojure keep\n888: working; syntax-error spans and profile identities match the oracle. A missing\n889: or incompatible library fails prerequisites for the declared lane and yields the\n890: existing qualified unavailable-parser result at the API seam, never another\n891: parser. Any failure blocks the gate and goes to the owner; no fallback.\n892: \n893: The parser interpreter composes over in-memory source/CST streams with canonical\n894: data and identity correlation; the C wrapper is private linkage behind it, and\n895: no native pointer or callback enters those media. Python lowering, prelude,\n896: primitives and evaluation stay in jolt.\n897: \n898: ## 8. UDP"}]},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_c2ebcd2cc65044f1a743c34d","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 95 lines\nNote: showing lines 1208-1302. More of the file remains. Use offset=1303 to continue.\n1208: ### 10.1 Slice table\n1209: \n1210: +---------------------------------------------+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1211: | Slice                                       | Boundary          | Falsifiable acceptance                                                                              |\n1212: +=============================================+===================+=====================================================================================================+\n1213: | External dependency: the codec track        | Not this track    | [dao.stream.codec.md](./dao.stream.codec.md) must have landed its slices C0-C4 on master before J6  |\n1214: |                                             |                   | is commissioned; jolt requires nothing else of it (§9.4). Not jolt work; not restated here.          |\n1215: +---------------------------------------------+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n1216: | J0a: tracked load and toolchain             | Manifest and      | Precondition: the owner's disposition of the §13.2 defaults that J0a would apply is recorded.       |\n1217: |                                