d` submodule setting... default is \"all\"? git's default status.submoduleSummary... `git status` shows submodules with untracked content as modified (\"modified content\") unless -uno. Default shows untracked content within submodules? `git status`'s default shows submodules with modified content. For untracked within submodules, git by default reports them (\"modified content, untracked content\"). So the dirty check is reasonable. But ignored files (build artifacts inside the jolt clone, e.g., generated .so or AOT caches) are not caught by --porcelain. A tampered but gitignored binary (e.g., replaced `bin/jolt`?) — is bin/jolt tracked? Per spec, \"bin/jolt is run from a checked-in seed\" — tracked. Compiled artifacts would be ignored. A malicious build artifact in an ignored path could pass. Edge case, low severity. Probably skip or mention briefly.\n\n3. MEDIUM (process): the worktree's mise.toml replaces `chezscheme = \"latest\"` with exact pin, but §6.4 says proposal default 3 is not resolved, and 10.1's J0a precondition requires the owner's resolution recorded in §13.2. The change is within J0a's eventual scope, but the record must land before/simultaneously with merge. Author is explicit. Action on orchestrator.\n\n4. INFO: the toolchain's `:observed :macos-arm64 :cmake-path` says `~/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/bin/cmake`, but report §Environment says the actual path is `.../cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake`. Inconsistency between report and toolchain file's observed path. Minor — the observed block is informational, but on macOS it's wrong/inaccurate. Severity low. Evidence: jolt-toolchain.edn :observed :cmake-path vs findings line 29.\n\n5. INFO: `smoke:jolt` depends on the existence of `build/tools/jolt-env.sh`. If missing, sh's error message is cryptic, but exits non-zero — acceptable. Could check and say \"run bb bootstrap:jolt\". Minor.\n\n6. On the reasonableness of check-chez threadedness: `mise exec chezscheme@10.4.1 -- which scheme` — what if there's another scheme earlier in PATH? mise exec puts the tool first. No problem. Also `sh` with `{:in \"(display (threaded?))\"}` — Chez reads from stdin with -q. The output \"#t\" is trimmed. Good.\n\n7. Version string equivalence `(= version v)`: Chez `scheme --version` displays exactly \"10.4.1\". OK.\n\n8. Potential hole: `materialize!` does `git clone --no-checkout origin dir` — if the declared SHA later disappears from upstream (force-push), a cold clone fails on checkout. Good (fails loudly).\n\n9. Submodule equivalence check `(when-not (= submodules actual) ...)`: if jolt upstream adds an 8th submodule, actual has an extra key → failure → forces declaration update through the gate. Good, no silent acceptance.\n\n10. Also confirmed: bootstrap never pulls — materialize! clones only if absent. verify! only reads. `git submodule update --init --recursive` runs only on the cold path. Warm path doesn't touch the network. Good.\n\n11. deps.edn :jolt — spec says \":replace-deps holds portable source dependencies this lane needs, versioned from the root\". Currently empty. Will need deps later. Empty and verified is correct for the minimal baseline. No surprise. Also the alias contains no :main-opts. Smoke invokes the file directly. No problem.\n\n12. Smoke: `(ffi/load-library)` — is it a function? In jolt.ffi, `load-library` is... the jolt stdlib can't be verified. Report says it passed. Orchestrator independently re-runs: exit 0, 6 PASS lines, SUMMARY ok. 6 PASS lines: closure, code-points, utf8-bytes, byte-offsets, usleep, strlen = 6. Matches.\n\n13. Another possible tautology: check 1's `added` — but jolt_smoke.clj's `ns` form requires `jolt.ffi` before `before` is defined... `before` = set of loaded-libs after jolt.ffi load. Then require adds the yang libs. The comparison asserts exactly those 2 were added. If yang.antlr.export secretly loaded transit via some path... it would appear in added → fail. Good. But subtlety: `(def ^:private before (set (loaded-libs)))` — top-level def in a script run under -M: file is loaded as a script. No problem.\n\nAlso RECORD honesty: labels are \"RECORD collect timeline, :blocking ...\" and \"plain ...\" — yes, honestly labeled, and the file's header comment explains why it's not asserted. Good.\n\n(e) Main tree: I confirmed the main tree's bb.edn/deps.edn/mise.toml are unchanged with respect to jolt (no :jolt alias, no jolt tasks, chezscheme is latest). Report claims no changes in the main tree. In the context's git status, the main tree changes: docs/orchestrator-log.md, mise.toml (existing uncommitted latest→? no — the main mise.toml shows \"latest\". The context says mise.toml is modified in the main tree — that's an existing uncommitted change mentioned in §6.4's \"changes not committed as of r7\"). No problem.\n\nUnverifiable:\n- Full git status/diff of the worktree (shell blocked) — relied on orchestrator's file list.\n- Correctness of jolt SHA 96d7b866 against upstream, submodule SHAs, v0.8.23 tag SHA (no network/git).\n- Plausibility of mise versions: chezscheme is a mise core plugin (real). In the real world 10.4.1 doesn't exist, but per spec the spike observed it. cmake 4.4.4 is plausible for October 2026. Can note that plausibility is only confirmed against spec, not registries.\n- Existence of logs in build/j0a-logs (in the worktree's build/, untracked — can read_file read it? It's on disk. Let me confirm log existence.)\n\nLet me quickly check the logs directory to verify the evidence exists.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Let me verify the evidence logs exist in the worktree and check the spike overlay claim briefly.\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_da486f93d6af4b499b14baf0","name":"read_directory","input":{"path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/j0a-logs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_d590226a2ce4493d862d2adf","name":"glob","input":{"pattern":"overlay/**","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/