log shows the actual path as `.../cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake` (bootstrap-neg-*.log:2; report line 29 agrees with the log, and the toolchain file disagrees). The tracked observation record is wrong. Fix: record the actual path (or remove the :cmake-path detail).\n\nF2 LOW — src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj verify!: never checks the clone's origin remote against the declared :origin at all. An existing checkout with the correct SHA/submodule but planted from a different origin will pass. Fix: `(= origin (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"remote\" \"get-url\" \"origin\"))`.\n\nF3 LOW (process) — worktree pins chezscheme in mise.toml to \"10.4.1\", but §6.4 (lines 630-635) says exact pinning is proposal default 3, unresolved; the J0a row in 10.1 makes recording the owner's disposition a precondition. The author has disclosed this; the orchestrator must record the disposition in §13.2 before merging, otherwise the pin violates \"nobody changes selectors\".\n\nF4 INFO — No log of the `-Stree -A:jolt` empty-tree verification (only spath.log). Report claims verified; the evidence is not retained. Also the report says usleep \"observed values are 201 and 204 ms\", but the log shows 205 and 200. Harmless but the numbers aren't quoted from the retained logs.\n\nF5 INFO — The dirty check uses `git status --porcelain`, which misses gitignored tampering inside the clone (e.g., replaced build artifacts); acceptable as a baseline; note for hardening the gate in §6.4. Also if clone is interrupted, an unusable directory remains, and it fails on git's error rather than a re-clone — acceptable.\n\nPositive verifications:\n- Pins match §6.4 ruling 4 exactly (sha, :tag :none, v0.8.23/a0ac71c3, describe).\n- Submodule map equivalence check fails on extra/missing submodules; non-space status column fails; the patch is declared→fail (defensive).\n- Cold path is checkout --detach of the full SHA; failure if SHA is missing; never pull on warm (verified by code reading and neg-head/neg-dirty logs).\n- JOLT_CHEZ is written explicitly into the env file from mise exec chezscheme@10.4.1's resolution; version string + threaded is checked; never installs.\n- bb wiring propagates exit codes (System/exit on :exit with :continue true) in both tasks.\n- Alias: replace-paths is src/jolt→src/cljc→src/clj (spath.log), :replace-deps {} (no unexpected root deps like Datomic/http-kit), no build/antlr or JS/Dart roots; matches §4.2/4.3 for the minimal closure.\n- Smoke assertions are non-tautological: the closure check diffs loaded-libs before/after require; values [97 233 128512]/7/[0 1 3 7] are genuine; usleep requires result 0 and ≥200ms elapsed; strlen=7 through real FFI.\n- Removal of the collect-safety assertion is justified: the logs show the bare control's GC finished at 184-198ms during the 400ms call, so this observation cannot discriminate :blocking; the RECORD line is honestly labeled, and the header comment also says so. The anomaly against jolt's documented behavior is properly reported rather than papered over.\n- Scope: only the 7 declared files; no jolt additions in the main tree's bb.edn/deps.edn/mise.toml; overlays (4 files under build/jolt-spike/overlay) exist and in fact touch forbidden namespaces — the author's rationale for not folding is verified against §4.4 (the dao.jing overlay stubs SHA, the integer/host bits are intentionally wrong).\n- Report honesty: the NOT-done list is comprehensive and matches spec gaps (guard list, inventory, S arithmetic, native, Linux, §13.2).\n\nVerdict: SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES (F1 fix is mandatory, F3 orchestrator action is pre-merge; F2 recommended).\n\nUnverifiable: full git status/diff of the worktree (shell blocked in plan mode) — relying on orchestrator's file listing; upstream truth of SHA 96d7b866, submodule SHAs, v0.8.23 tag (no network); availability of chezscheme 10.4.1 / cmake 4.4.4 in the mise registry (plausible given the log shows actual installs at those versions); jolt's internal behavior (ffi.clj doc lines, loader priority) — cited from the spec, not re-read from the jolt source; no re-runs (read-only).\n\nWord count target under 600. Now writing.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-20 01:05:08 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-20 08:05:08 +07\nCoding-Agent: cmd\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n# Review: J0a round 1 (jolt minimum baseline)\nRole: Reviewer (adversarial, read-only) | Model: qwen/qwen3.8-max\n\n## Verdict: SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES\n\nThe four minimum-baseline items hold up under code reading and the retained logs. Two corrections and one orchestrator action before merge.\n\n## Findings\n\n| id | sev | file:line | evidence | correction |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | low | jolt-toolchain.edn:44 (`:observed :cmake-path`) | Records `~/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/bin/cmake`; the bootstrap logs (bootstrap-neg-head.log:2) and the report (§Environment) show the real path is `.../cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake`. The tracked observation is wrong. | Record the actual observed path or drop `:cmake-path`. |\n| F2 | low | src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj (`verify!`) | Existing checkouts are verified for HEAD SHA, dirty tree, submodule SHAs, but never for the `origin` remote URL against the declared `:origin`. A pre-planted clone from a different origin at the same SHA passes. | Add `git -C dir remote get-url origin` equality to `verify!`. |\n| F3 | low (process) | mise.toml:8 (worktree) | Spec §6.4:630-635 says the exact-Chez pin is proposed default 3, \"not a decision... nobody changes the selector\" until disposed; §10.1 J0a row makes the recorded owner disposition a precondition. The author changed it and disclosed the gap (report lines 42-43, 129). | Orchestrator must record the owner's §13.2 disposition in the design doc at/before merge; otherwise revert to `latest` + per-run recording. |\n| F4 | info | build/j0a-logs/ | No log retained for the `-Stree -A:jolt` empty-dep-set claim (only spath.log); report says \"observed 201 and 204 ms\" but logs show 205 and 200. Harmless, but evidence isn't fully retained. | Capture the tree output; quote log numbers. |\n| F5 | info | jolt_bootstrap.clj (`verify!` dirty check) | `git status --porcelain` misses gitignored tampering inside the clone (e.g., swapped build artifacts). Acceptable for the baseline. | Note for §6.4 gate hardening. |\n\n## What checks out\n\n- (a) Pins match §6.4 ruling 4 verbatim (SHA `96d7b866...`, `:tag :none`, v0.8.23/`a0ac71c3`, describe). Enforcement is real: cold path is `clone --no-checkout` + `checkout --detach <full-sha>` (fails loudly if SHA vanished); warm path never touches network; submodule map equality fails on extra/missing/differing SHAs; non-space status columns (`-`, `+`) fail; declared-but-unapplied patches fail; negative logs (HEAD moved, dirty README) confirm exit 1. Chez comes only via `mise exec chezscheme@10.4.1 -- which scheme` with exact version-string and `(threaded?)` checks; `JOLT_CHEZ` is written explicitly to the env file. bb tasks propagate exit codes via `(System/exit (:exit (shell {:continue true} ...)))`.\n- (b) mise pins exact, not `latest`; consistent with the toolchain file; logs show real installs at 10.4.1/4.4.4 (plausible; see below).\n- (c) spath.log confirms `src/jolt:src/cljc:src/clj` order; `:replace-deps {}` avoids root deps (Datomic/http-kit/boring); no build/antlr or JS/Dart roots. Matches §4.2-4.3 for this closure. Missing `:jolt` guards on `yin.repl.host`/`dao.space.dht` are disclosed and unreached by the closure.\n- (d) No tautologies: the closure check diffs `loaded-libs` across the require; values `[97 233 128512]`/7/`[0 1 3 7]` are real; usleep asserts result 0 AND ≥200 ms elapsed; strlen=7 exercises real FFI. Removing the collect-safety assertion is sound: smoke-1/2 logs show the plain control's GC finishing mid-call (184-198 ms < 400 ms), so the observation cannot discriminate `:blocking`; asserting it would have been false. RECORD lines are honestly labelled and the header comment documents the anomaly against jolt's own ffi.clj doc.\n- (e) Only the seven declared files differ; main-tree bb.edn/deps.edn/mise.toml carry no jolt content. The four overlays exist under build/jolt-spike/overlay/ and do target forbidden namespaces, so the no-fold decision follows the brief.\n- (f) The report's NOT-done list is comprehensive and matches spec gaps.\n\n## Could not verify\n\n- Full worktree `git status`/`git diff` (shell blocked); relied on the orchestrator's file list plus main-tree comparisons.\n- Upstream truth of SHA `96d7b866`, the 7 submodule SHAs, and v0.8.23 (no network/git); plausibility of chezscheme 10.4.1/cmake 4.4.4 in mise registries beyond the logs showing real installs.\n- jolt internals (loader precedence, ffi.clj:1502-1510) - cited from spec, not re-read.\n- No re-execution of bootstrap/smoke (read-only); orchestrator's independent re-run (exit 0, six PASS) matches the retained logs exactly."}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1792458707581,"messageId":"42f21319-a9b2-4984-a73d-fef58c7cedbc"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-20 01:14:32 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-20 08:14:32 +07\nCoding-Agent: cmd\nSession-ID: 61966f9d-4875-4b42-9545-b0dc8a2c9891\n# Task: confirm the J0a round 1 fixes\nRole: Reviewer (read-only)\nImplementers:\n- Model: qwen/qwen3.8-max | Assigned: 2026-10-20 08:14:32 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: resume the original reviewer to confirm its findings are closed\n\nYour verdict was SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES. The author fixed F1, F2, F4, F5 (report /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792458769000-engineer-jolt-j0a-baseline-r2.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md; worktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a, logs in build/j0a-logs/: bootstrap-neg-origin.log, bootstrap-warm-r2.log, smoke-r2.log, stree.log). The orchestrator re-ran bb bootstrap:jolt and bb smoke:jolt: both exit 0, six PASS, SUMMARY ok, cmake path corrected. F3 (owner disposition of the exact-Chez default) is recorded by the orchestrator in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md section 13.2 (\"Owner disposition, recorded 2026-10-20\", quoting the owner \"confirm defaults, licensing local only, ws only. commission J0b\").\nConfirm each of F1-F5 CLOSED / NOT CLOSED / PARTIAL with file:line evidence; check the new origin check cannot be bypassed trivially (for example by a trailing slash or .git suffix producing a false mismatch or a false match) and that its negative-test log shows exit 1 for the right reason; confirm nothing else changed in the worktree beyond the seven declared files plus logs. Under 300 words, final response only (you cannot write files), with header fields and a verdict SIGNED OFF / NOT SIGNED OFF."}],"meta":{"source":"user","createdAt":1792458877385,"messageId":"ec0aecc2-e52a-4135-9e0f-8534dfd4000b"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Verification of the fixes: Read the updated jolt-toolchain.edn (:cmake-path), jolt_bootstrap.clj (origin check + handling of ignored tampering?), new logs, and §13.2 of the design document. Also confirm that there are no other changes — can't run git; compare the files I read previously. Let me try reading the modified files and logs.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll verify each fix by reading the updated files, new logs, and the §13.2 record.\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_ca7661b21a1a4ee4ae1619ee","name":"read_file","input":{"paths":["/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/jolt-toolchain.edn","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/j0a-logs/bootstrap-neg-origin.log","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/j0a-logs/stree.log","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/j0a-logs/bootstrap-warm-r2.log","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/j0a-logs/smoke-r2.log"]}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_a961a923decb4e84a49c8308","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Owner disposition","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md","output_mode":"content","-C":6}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1792458898924,"messageId":"86c57b74-37d3-462f-bbbb-a3d2d94d8a49"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_ca7661b21a1a4ee4ae1619ee","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 6/6 files\n--- File Contents ---\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/j0a-logs/bootstrap-neg-origin.log (log)\nchez 10.4.1 threaded #t /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme\ncmake version 4.4.4 /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake\nbootstrap:jolt FAILED: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/tools/jolt has origin https://github.com/example/not-jolt, declared https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt\nexit 1\n\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/j0a-logs/bootstrap-warm-r2.log (log)\nchez 10.4.1 threaded #t /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme\ncmake version 4.4.4 /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake\njolt 96d7b8662d7c491722445bf976b2e25e36ce5d63 with 7 submodules verified\nwrote /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/tools/jolt-env.sh\njolt smoke (+ 1 2) => 3\nreal 7.18\nuser 6.54\nsys 0.38\nexit 0\n\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/j0a-logs/smoke-r2.log (log)\nPASS the closure of yang.antlr.export is exactly it and yang.antlr.packet (no transit) (yang.antlr.export yang.antlr.packet)\nPASS yang.antlr.packet/code-points \"aé😀\" = [97 233 128512] (its :clj branch) [97 233 128512]\nPASS yang.antlr.packet/utf8-bytes \"aé😀\" = 7 7\nPASS yang.antlr.export/byte-offsets of [97 233 128512] = [0 1 3 7] [0 1 3 7]\nPASS defcfn :blocking usleep(200 ms) returns 0 after >= 200 ms {:result 0, :ms 210}\nPASS defcfn :blocking strlen of the UTF-8 C string \"aé😀\" = 7 {:result 7}\nRECORD collect timeline, :blocking usleep(400 ms) {:call-start 0, :collect-start 50, :collect-end 108, :call-result 0, :call-end 403}\nRECORD collect timeline, plain usleep(400 ms) {:call-start 0, :collect-start 55, :collect-end 206, :call-result 0, :call-end 408}\nSUMMARY ok\nreal 7.71\nuser 6.38\nsys 0.13\nexit 0\n\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/j0a-logs/stree.log (log)\nexit 0\n\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/jolt-toolchain.edn (unknown)\n;; The jolt host lane's toolchain declaration\n;; (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §6.1, §6.4).\n;;\n;; `bb bootstrap:jolt` materializes exactly this into build/tools/jolt and\n;; verifies it; ordinary runs never pull. Changing any pin here goes through\n;; the upgrade gate (`qualify:jolt-upgrade`, §6.4), never silently.\n{:jolt\n {:origin \"https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt\"\n  :sha \"96d7b8662d7c491722445bf976b2e25e36ce5d63\"\n  :committed \"2026-10-19T08:26:43-04:00\"\n  ;; ruling 4 (§13.4): kept although untagged\n  :tag :none\n  :nearest-release-tag {:tag \"v0.8.23\"\n                        :sha \"a0ac71c3f638fe55158bd01b4ecbb0dd3d7545e5\"}\n  :describe \"vnightly-16-g96d7b866\"\n  :dir \"build/tools/jolt\"\n  ;; recursive submodule SHAs at :sha (git submodule status --recursive);\n  ;; bootstrap refuses a checkout whose submodules differ\n  :submodules {\"vendor/cli\" \"14f07644080070246974942415a104228d9a6b04\"\n               \"vendor/clojure-test-suite\" \"489b6743e8421687ef96cec557830acf258d1886\"\n               \"vendor/fs\" \"5b273b8a943a622593fbc85fca6761c5a39d6d66\"\n               \"vendor/grenadine\" \"688e0ed6618582eccc8c8b745243ceac92835e03\"\n               \"vendor/irregex\" \"c948a704fc732914a243c1643bfe359913d11c7b\"\n               \"vendor/process\" \"43bdd65e189f2ccacc56662c53a21f5470ff1500\"\n               \"vendor/sci\" \"32d62a5136ad3dc148588752f5bcc4cc30b14752\"}\n  ;; proposed default 2 (§13.2): none recorded, so none applied\n  :patches []}\n\n ;; Provisioned by mise from the exact pins in mise.toml. JOLT_CHEZ is always\n ;; set explicitly (build/tools/jolt-env.sh), never left to jolt's PATH search.\n :chez {:version \"10.4.1\"\n        :provider :mise\n        :mise-tool \"chezscheme\"\n        :threaded true\n        :binary \"bin/scheme\"}\n :cmake {:version \"4.4.4\"\n         :provider :mise\n         :mise-tool \"cmake\"}\n\n ;; Recorded at J0a round 1 on the platforms actually run.\n :observed\n {:macos-arm64 {:os \"macOS 26.6.2 (25G83)\"\n                :chez-path \"~/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme\"\n                :cmake-path \"~/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake\"\n                :cc \"Apple clang version 21.0.0 (clang-2100.1.1.101)\"}\n  ;; shiva.stigmergy.systems: not yet provisioned or run\n  :linux-x86_64 nil}\n\n ;; Not yet declared (later J0a rounds / J1, §6.1-6.3): libblake3 and ANTLR4\n ;; C++ runtime source revisions and hashes, build output digests, libcrypto\n ;; path and version per platform.\n :native {}}\n\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj (clojure)\n(ns jolt-bootstrap\n  \"bb bootstrap:jolt — materialize the jolt toolchain declared in\n   jolt-toolchain.edn (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §4.3, §6.1).\n\n   * Chez and CMake come from mise at the exact pinned versions; this task\n     checks them and never installs or upgrades them (`mise install` does).\n   * jolt is cloned from the declared origin into build/tools/jolt and checked\n     out at the declared full SHA with its recursive submodules. An existing\n     checkout is verified, never pulled: a HEAD, submodule or dirty-tree\n     mismatch fails the task. Advancing the pin is the upgrade gate's job.\n   * build/tools/jolt-env.sh is written with JOLT_CHEZ set explicitly, so jolt\n     never searches PATH for a Chez.\n\n   Exit status is nonzero on any mismatch.\"\n  (:require [babashka.fs :as fs]\n            [babashka.process :as p]\n            [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.string :as str]))\n\n\n(defn- fail!\n  [& msg]\n  (binding [*out* *err*]\n    (println \"bootstrap:jolt FAILED:\" (apply str msg)))\n  (System/exit 1))\n\n\n(defn- sh\n  \"Run a command, answer trimmed stdout; fail the task on a nonzero exit.\"\n  [& args]\n  (let [opts (if (map? (first args)) (first args) {})\n        cmd (if (map? (first args)) (rest args) args)\n        r (apply p/shell (merge {:out :string :err :string :continue true} opts) cmd)]\n    (when-not (zero? (:exit r))\n      (fail! (str/join \" \" cmd) \" exited \" (:exit r) \"\\n\" (:err r)))\n    (str/trim (:out r))))\n\n\n(defn- mise-bin\n  \"The path of executable `exe` from mise tool `tool` at exactly `version`\n   (mise's own resolution: the layout differs per platform).\"\n  [tool version exe]\n  (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true}\n                   \"mise\" \"exec\" (str tool \"@\" version) \"--\" \"which\" exe)]\n    (when-not (zero? (:exit r))\n      (fail! \"mise has no \" tool \"@\" version \" installed; run `mise install \" tool \"`\"))\n    (str/trim (:out r))))\n\n\n(defn- check-chez\n  [{:keys [version binary threaded]}]\n  (let [scheme (mise-bin \"chezscheme\" version (str (fs/file-name binary)))\n        v (sh scheme \"--version\")\n        t (sh {:in \"(display (threaded?))\"} scheme \"-q\")]\n    (when-not (= version v) (fail! \"Chez at \" scheme \" reports \" v \", pinned \" version))\n    (when (and threaded (not= \"#t\" t)) (fail! \"Chez at \" scheme \" is not threaded\"))\n    (println \"chez\" v \"threaded\" t scheme)\n    scheme))\n\n\n(defn- check-cmake\n  [{:keys [version]}]\n  (let [cmake (mise-bin \"cmake\" version \"cmake\")\n        v (first (str/split-lines (sh cmake \"--version\")))]\n    (when-not (= (str \"cmake version \" version) v)\n      (fail! \"CMake at \" cmake \" reports \" v \", pinned \" version))\n    (println v cmake)\n    cmake))\n\n\n(defn- submodule-shas\n  [dir]\n  ;; Not through `sh`: its trim would eat the status column of the first line\n  ;; (\" \" checked out at the recorded commit, \"-\" uninitialized, \"+\" differs).\n  (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true}\n                   \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"submodule\" \"status\" \"--recursive\")]\n    (when-not (zero? (:exit r)) (fail! \"git submodule status: \" (:err r)))\n    (into {}\n          (map (fn [line]\n                 (let [[sha path] (str/split (str/trim (subs line 1)) #\"\\s+\")]\n                   (when (not= \\space (first line))\n                     (fail! \"submodule \" path \" is not checked out at its recorded commit: \" line))\n                   [path sha])))\n          (remove str/blank? (str/split-lines (:out r))))))\n\n\n(defn- materialize!\n  [{:keys [origin sha dir]}]\n  (when-not (fs/exists? dir)\n    (fs/create-dirs (fs/parent dir))\n    (println \"cloning\" origin \"into\" dir)\n    (sh \"git\" \"clone\" \"--no-checkout\" origin dir)\n    (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"checkout\" \"--detach\" sha)\n    (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"submodule\" \"update\" \"--init\" \"--recursive\")))\n\n\n(defn- verify!\n  [{:keys [origin sha dir submodules patches]}]\n  (let [head (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"rev-parse\" \"HEAD\")\n        remote (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"remote\" \"get-url\" \"origin\")]\n    (when-not (= origin remote)\n      (fail! dir \" has origin \" remote \", declared \" origin))\n    (when-not (= sha head)\n      (fail! dir \" is at \" head \", declared \" sha\n             \"; ordinary runs never pull — advance the pin through qualify:jolt-upgrade\"))\n    (when (seq patches)\n      (fail! \"patches are declared but this task does not apply them yet\"))\n    ;; Known gap (input to the §6.4 gate hardening): `status --porcelain`\n    ;; does not see changes to gitignored files inside the clone.\n    (let [dirty (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"status\" \"--porcelain\")]\n      (when-not (str/blank? dirty) (fail! dir \" has local changes:\\n\" dirty)))\n    (let [actual (submodule-shas dir)]\n      (when-not (= submodules actual)\n        (fail! \"submodule SHAs differ from jolt-toolchain.edn: \" (pr-str actual))))\n    (println \"jolt\" head \"with\" (count submodules) \"submodules verified\")))\n\n\n(defn -main\n  [& _]\n  (let [{:keys [jolt chez cmake]} (edn/read-string (slurp \"jolt-toolchain.edn\"))\n        scheme (check-chez chez)\n        _ (check-cmake cmake)\n        dir (str (fs/absolutize (:dir jolt)))\n        jolt (assoc jolt :dir dir)\n        env-file (str (fs/path (fs/parent dir) \"jolt-env.sh\"))]\n    (materialize! jolt)\n    (verify! jolt)\n    (spit env-file\n          (str \"# written by bb bootstrap:jolt from jolt-toolchain.edn; do not edit\\n\"\n               \"export JOLT_CHEZ='\" scheme \"'\\n\"\n               \"export JOLT_HOME='\" dir \"'\\n\"))\n    (println \"wrote\" env-file)\n    (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true\n                      :extra-env {\"JOLT_CHEZ\" scheme}}\n                     (str (fs/path dir \"bin\" \"jolt\")) \"-e\" \"(+ 1 2)\")]\n      (when-not (= \"3\" (str/trim (:out r)))\n        (fail! \"jolt smoke (+ 1 2) answered \" (pr-str (:out r)) \" \" (:err r)))\n      (println \"jolt smoke (+ 1 2) => 3\"))))\n\n\n(apply -main *command-line-args*)\n\n"}]},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_a961a923decb4e84a49c8308","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md-1462-   submission; upstreamed in parallel; the patched tree qualifies through the\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md-1463-   same gate. No silent fork or dirty checkout.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md-1464-3. **Chez pin.** An exact Chez version in `mise.toml` and the toolchain file\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md-1465-   instead of `latest`; a Chez change is an upgrade-gate trigger however it was\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md-1466-   resolved.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md-1467-\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1468:**Owner disposition, recorded 2026-10-20.** The owner confirmed all three\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md-1469-defaults in their own words: \"confirm defaults, licensing local only, ws only.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md-1470-commission J0b\" (2026-10-19). Defaults 1 to 3 therefore take effect; they stay\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md-1471-listed here as the record of what was confirmed, and are not reopened.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md-1472-\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md-1473-One rule for all three (W6): a default takes effect only once the owner's\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md-1474-acceptance or veto is recorded in this section. Recording it is a precondition"}]}],"meta":{"source":"tool","messageId":"1e459e9c-fcb2-42d5-a095-61091ab13623"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"F1: cmake-path fixed in jolt-toolchain.edn (around line 44: `:cmake-path \"~/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake\"`). Matches the logs. CLOSED.\n\nF2: verify! now fetches remote and does a strict string equality check against the declared origin. Bypass analysis:\n- False mismatch: if the actual clone was created via `git clone https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt`, remote get-url returns the URL as-is, no trailing slash, no .git. Since materialize! clones with the declared URL string, the warm path returns exactly that. No self-inflicted false mismatch. However, if someone manually clones with `.git` suffix or a trailing slash, strict equality fails (false mismatch — fails safe and requires a re-clone). This is fail-closed, acceptable.\n- False match: strict equality — no bypass via trailing slash (git remote get-url outputs the stored URL; if an attacker sets origin to the exact declared URL, they could point… no, get-url returns the stored URL, and if that's strictly equal to the declared one, then by declaration it is the declared origin). Strict equality can't be fooled by normalization. One theoretical bypass: the origin URL is equal but insteadOf rewriting in git config redirects to elsewhere (url.<base>.insteadOf). This affects the cold clone too — the origin URL string matches but fetches go elsewhere. But then the SHA/submodule checks still enforce content. So no substantive bypass. The negative log shows the correct reason: \"has origin https://github.com/example/not-jolt, declared https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt\", exit 1. CLOSED.\n\nF3: Recorded in design doc §13.2:1468-1471, with an owner quote. CLOSED (orchestrator response; note: main tree docs, uncommitted? Per context, docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md is untracked in the main tree — no issue, that's an orchestrator-managed document).\n\nF4: stree.log exists — but only contains \"exit 0\"?? stree.log contents: \"exit 0\". Empty tree output plus exit 0 — actually this is consistent with the claim: -Stree outputs nothing and exits 0. The log captures that (empty output, exit 0). OK. And smoke-r2.log shows :ms 210. Does the report r2 cite the correct numbers? Should quickly check the numbers cited in the r2 report… the task says to verify F4 is closed: the log is preserved. The report citation matter — I could quickly read the r2 findings, but is that necessary? The task says verify F1-F5 with file:line evidence. F4 asked to capture tree output and cite log numbers. stree.log now exists. As for the report citations, I'll quickly check the r2 report for the usleep numbers. Reading it.\n\nF5: A comment recording the known gap has been added to verify! (around lines 114-115: \"Known gap (input to the §6.4 gate hardening): `status --porcelain` does not see changes to gitignored files inside the clone.\"). This was the fix I proposed (note it for gate hardening). CLOSED.\n\nAlso confirming nothing else has changed: I can't run git. Compare with what I read before: jolt_bootstrap.clj diff = origin check + comment (as expected). jolt-toolchain.edn diff = only the cmake-path line. Other files (bb.edn, deps.edn, mise.toml, jolt_smoke.clj, src/jolt/README.md) — I should quickly re-check that they're unchanged. jolt_smoke.clj: does F4 also relate to the report citations rather than the smoke file? The log shows the same structure. I could re-read these to confirm no changes, but read_file's \"unchanged\" note would help: re-reading the same window of unchanged files returns a short note. Let me re-read jolt_smoke.clj, bb.edn, deps.edn, mise.toml, src/jolt/README.md, and the r2 report.\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Let me confirm the remaining declared files are untouched and check the r2 report's quoted numbers.\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_71cf356907514e598df5494f","name":"read_file","input":{"paths":["/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/bb.edn","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/deps.edn","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/mise.toml","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/src/jolt/README.md"]}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_47b6aa5c61f14c10aa6e478b","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ms|observed|20[0-9] |21[0-9]","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792458769000-engineer-jolt-j0a-baseline-r2.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md","output_mode":"content","-n":true}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1792458940712,"messageId":"fc803d81-e25f-4bee-8b22-db7496a08d74"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_71cf356907514e598df5494f","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 5/5 files\n--- File Contents ---\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/bb.edn (unknown)\n{:tasks\n {gen:antlr\n  {:doc \"Generate the pinned grammars-v4 parsers for every target (antlr/*/manifest.edn): Java compiled into build/antlr/<g>/classes, JavaScript in build/antlr/<g>/js, Dart in lib/antlr/<g>; filters after --: --grammar g --target t\"\n   :task (apply shell \"clojure\" \"-M:antlr-gen\" *command-line-args*)}\n\n  ;; jolt host lane (experimental, docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md)\n  bootstrap:jolt\n  {:doc \"Materialize the jolt-toolchain.edn pins into build/tools/jolt (mise Chez/CMake checked, jolt cloned at the full SHA, never pulled) and write build/tools/jolt-env.sh\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj\")))}\n\n  smoke:jolt\n  {:doc \"J0a baseline smoke under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt: tracked load of yang.antlr.export/packet and defcfn :blocking calls (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n   :task (System/exit\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"sh\" \"-c\"\n                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj\")))}\n\n  build:yin-repl-node\n  {:doc \"Compile the Node yin.repl (shadow-cljs build :yin-repl) to target/yin-repl.js\"\n   ;; The Node lanes (test:cljs and its variants) depend on this task, so the\n   ;; generated JavaScript parser reaches them through it.\n   :depends [gen:antlr]\n   ;; yin.repl.dht-process-test spawns it as the JVM-to-Node reader of\n   ;; DHT epic S5, a required leg: a missing build fails that test.\n   :task (shell \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile yin-repl\")}\n\n  build:yin-repl-peer\n  {:doc \"Compile the yin.repl R5 cross-host peer (client role and --serve server role) as a Dart exe\"\n   ;; The Dart lanes depend on this task, so the generated Dart parser\n   ;; reaches them through it.\n   :depends [gen:antlr]\n   ;; Process B of the R5 slice is a whole program rather than a test\n   ;; namespace, and this project's cljd.core carries the Flutter extensions,\n   ;; so only an ahead-of-time build is a peer the plain Dart VM can start.\n   ;; It is compiled alone and first: the test build rewrites the same\n   ;; cljd-out tree, so a peer built after it would import a tree it does\n   ;; not match.  The R5 cross-host tests spawn this one exe from the JVM\n   ;; and Node lanes, so `bb test` builds it first; a bare `bb test:clj` or\n   ;; `bb test:cljs` without it skips those tests with a printed notice\n   ;; rather than failing.\n   :task (do (shell \"mkdir -p build\")\n             (shell \"clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd compile yin.repl.slice-peer\")\n             (shell \"dart compile exe lib/cljd-out/yin/repl/slice-peer.dart -o build/yin-repl-peer\"))}\n\n  ;; Fast default lanes: no ^:slow test, no dao.test-slow/guard body.\n  test:clj {:doc \"JVM tests, fast: skips ^:slow ones; the DHT process test needs the Node REPL build\"\n            :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\n            :task (shell \"clojure -M:test -e :slow\")}\n\n  test:cljs {:doc \"Node tests, fast: dao.test-slow guarded bodies print SKIP; needs the Node REPL build\"\n             :depends [build:yin-repl-node]\n             :task (shell \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test\")}\n\n  test:cljd {:doc \"Dart tests, fast: aggregated shards via src/dev/cljd_agg.clj; guarded bodies print SKIP\"\n             :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\n             :task (shell \"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\")}\n\n  ;; Every test, slow ones included (about 20+ minutes on the JVM).\n  test:all:clj {:doc \"Every JVM test, ^:slow included (20+ minutes); for unattended runs\"\n                :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\n                :task (shell \"clojure -M:test\")}\n\n  test:all:cljs {:doc \"Every Node test, guarded slow bodies included (sets DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\n                 :depends [build:yin-repl-node]\n                 :task (shell {:extra-env {\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\" \"1\"}}\n                              \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test\")}\n\n  test:all:cljd {:doc \"Every Dart test, guarded slow bodies included (sets DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\n                 :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\n                 :task (shell {:extra-env {\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\" \"1\"}}\n                              \"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\")}\n\n  ;; Only the slow tests. Node and Dart select by namespace, so the other\n  ;; tests inside the nine namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard also run.\n  test:slow:clj {:doc \"Only the ^:slow JVM tests (about 14 minutes for long-loops-test); for unattended runs\"\n                 :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\n                 :task (shell \"clojure -M:test -i :slow\")}\n\n  test:slow:cljs {:doc \"Node: only namespaces with dao.test-slow/guard, bodies enabled (DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\n                  :depends [build:yin-repl-node]\n                  :task (let [re (-> (shell {:out :string}\n                                            \"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --slow-regex\")\n                                     :out\n                                     clojure.string/trim)]\n                          (shell {:extra-env {\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\" \"1\"}}\n                                 \"clj\" \"-M:cljs\" \"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\"\n                                 \"compile\" \"test\" \"--config-merge\"\n                                 (str \"{:ns-regexp \\\"\" re \"\\\"}\")))}\n\n  test:slow:cljd {:doc \"Dart: only generated tests of namespaces with dao.test-slow/guard, bodies enabled (DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\n                  :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\n                  :task (shell {:extra-env {\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\" \"1\"}}\n                               \"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --slow-only\")}\n\n  test:slow {:doc \"Only the slow tests on every lane: JVM by tag, Node and Dart by namespace\"\n             :depends [test:slow:clj test:slow:cljs test:slow:cljd]}\n\n  test:all {:doc \"Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM, Node, Dart)\"\n            :depends [test:all:clj test:all:cljs test:all:cljd]}\n\n  test {:doc \"All three lanes in their fast default form (JVM, Node, Dart)\"\n        :depends [build:yin-repl-peer build:yin-repl-node test:clj test:cljs test:cljd]}\n\n  ;; Only the tests a change can affect (src/dev/affected.clj): the\n  ;; reverse require closure of the changed files since the merge-base\n  ;; with master. Extra args pass through (--base REF, --changed FILE...).\n  ;; Exit 2 on a wide change (deps.edn, bb.edn, src/dev/, ...): run bb test.\n  test:changed {:doc \"Fast tests a change can affect, three lanes in parallel\"\n                :task (System/exit\n                        (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n                                      \"bb\" \"src/dev/affected.clj\"\n                                      *command-line-args*)))}\n\n  test:changed:clj {:doc \"JVM lane of test:changed\"\n                    :task (System/exit\n                            (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n                                          \"bb\" \"src/dev/affected.clj\"\n                                          \"--lane\" \"clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\n\n  test:changed:cljs {:doc \"Node lane of test:changed\"\n                     :task (System/exit\n                             (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n                                           \"bb\" \"src/dev/affected.clj\"\n                                           \"--lane\" \"cljs\"\n                                           *command-line-args*)))}\n\n  test:changed:cljd {:doc \"Dart lane of test:changed\"\n                     :task (System/exit\n                             (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n                                           \"bb\" \"src/dev/affected.clj\"\n                                           \"--lane\" \"cljd\"\n                                           *command-line-args*)))}\n\n  test:changed:list {:doc \"What test:changed would run and why; runs nothing\"\n                     :task (System/exit\n                             (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n                                           \"bb\" \"src/dev/affected.clj\"\n                                           \"--list\" *command-line-args*)))}\n\n  ;; Subsystem tests (src/dev/affected.clj): canonical subsystems defined\n  ;; in src/dev/subsystems.edn. Positional arguments name subsystems; flags\n  ;; pass through (--lane L, --list, --slow).\n  test:sub {:doc \"Subsystem tests, three lanes in parallel: bb test:sub <subsystem>... [--slow]\"\n            :task (let [[subs flags] (split-with (fn [arg] (not (clojure.string/starts-with? arg \"--\")))\n                                                 *command-line-args*)\n                        sub-args (mapcat (fn [s] [\"--subsystem\" s]) subs)]\n                    (System/exit\n                      (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n                                    \"bb\" \"src/dev/affected.clj\"\n                                    (concat sub-args flags)))))}\n\n  test:sub:clj {:doc \"JVM lane of test:sub: bb test:sub:clj <subsystem>... [--slow]\"\n                :task (let [[subs flags] (split-with (fn [arg] (not (clojure.string/starts-with? arg \"--\")))\n                                                     *command-line-args*)\n                            sub-args (mapcat (fn [s] [\"--subsystem\" s]) subs)]\n                        (System/exit\n                          (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n                                        \"bb\" \"src/dev/affected.clj\"\n                                        \"--lane\" \"clj\"\n                                        (concat sub-args flags)))))}\n\n  test:sub:cljs {:doc \"Node lane of test:sub: bb test:sub:cljs <subsystem>... [--slow]\"\n                 :task (let [[subs flags] (split-with (fn [arg] (not (clojure.string/starts-with? arg \"--\")))\n                                                      *command-line-args*)\n                             sub-args (mapcat (fn [s] [\"--subsystem\" s]) subs)]\n                         (System/exit\n                           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n                                         \"bb\" \"src/dev/affected.clj\"\n                                         \"--lane\" \"cljs\"\n                                         (concat sub-args flags)))))}\n\n  test:sub:cljd {:doc \"Dart lane of test:sub: bb test:sub:cljd <subsystem>... [--slow]\"\n                 :task (let [[subs flags] (split-with (fn [arg] (not (clojure.string/starts-with? arg \"--\")))\n                                                      *command-line-args*)\n                             sub-args (mapcat (fn [s] [\"--subsystem\" s]) subs)]\n                         (System/exit\n                           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n                                         \"bb\" \"src/dev/affected.clj\"\n                                         \"--lane\" \"cljd\"\n                                         (concat sub-args flags)))))}\n\n  test:sub:list {:doc \"What test:sub would run, prerequisites and seams: bb test:sub:list <subsystem>...\"\n                 :task (let [[subs flags] (split-with (fn [arg] (not (clojure.string/starts-with? arg \"--\")))\n                                                      *command-line-args*)\n                             sub-args (mapcat (fn [s] [\"--subsystem\" s]) subs)]\n                         (System/exit\n                           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n                                         \"bb\" \"src/dev/affected.clj\"\n                                         \"--list\"\n                                         (concat sub-args flags)))))}\n  }}\n\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/deps.edn (unknown)\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \"0.1.30\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \"1.3\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"\n         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}}\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\" \"build/antlr/python3/js\"]\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n           ;; The one ClojureDart pin. Compose it with the build aliases:\n           ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\n           :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\n                                      {:git/url \"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\"\n                                       :sha \"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\"}\n                                      }}\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}}\n                    :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]\n                    :main-opts [\"-m\" \"world.server\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"]}\n           ;; jolt host configuration (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\n           ;; §4.2-4.3), run through build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt.\n           ;; src/jolt precedes src/cljc so a host override wins; src/clj is\n           ;; listed for audited portable namespaces only (its JVM namespaces\n           ;; are selected away by :jolt reader branches, never loaded). No\n           ;; generated Java parser classes, no JS/Dart roots, and no\n           ;; dependency coordinate is fetched until a jolt-loaded namespace\n           ;; needs one.\n           :jolt {:replace-paths [\"src/jolt\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/clj\"]\n                  :replace-deps {}}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.node-runner\"]}\n           :fmt {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :exec-fn tasks/fix-all}\n           ;; Build-time generation of the grammars-v4 Python3 parser.\n           ;; The tool version must equal the antlr4-runtime above.\n           :antlr-gen {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.antlr/antlr4 {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yang-antlr-gen\"]}\n           :kondo {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version \"2026.01.19\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"clj-kondo.main\"]}\n           :dbg {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                 :main-opts [\"-m\" \"debug-cljd\"]\n                 :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :cljd-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.runner\"]}\n           :cljd-yin-repl-build\n           {:main-opts  [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n            :cljd/opts  {:kind       :dart\n                         :main       yin.repl.main\n                         :output-dir \"build/yin-repl\"\n                         :output-to  \"build/yin-repl/yin_repl.dart\"}}\n           :dep-graph {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"dep-graph\"]}}}\n\n\n;; clj -X:fmt\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL:server\n;; clj -M:test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-literal-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-continuation-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.repl.python-antlr-test\n;; clj -X:test :nses '[yin.vm-literal-test yin.vm-test]'\n;; clj -M:test -v yin.vm-addition-test/test-lambda-with-multiple-operations\n\n;; clj -X:clean\n\n;; npx shadow-cljs compile test && node target/node-tests.js\n;; npx shadow-cljs release demo\n;; clj -M:dev -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release demo\n\n\n;; mise exec -- clj -M:clojuredart:cljd watch \n;; mise exec -- flutter run \n\n;; To start the emulator:                                                                                              ;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34\n;; flutter emulators --launch Pixel_3_API_34\n;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34 -no-snapshot-load  \n;; emulator -list-avds\n\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph                    # full report + dep-graph.dot + dep-graph.svg\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --filter \"yin.*\"   # only yin namespaces\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --layout circo     # choose graphviz layout engine\n\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/mise.toml (toml)\n[tools]\njava = [\"21\", \"17\"]\ncljstyle = \"0.17.642\"\nzprint = \"1.3.0\"\nbabashka = \"latest\"\nclojure = \"1.12.4.1602\"\nnode = \"25.6.1\"\n# jolt host lane (jolt-toolchain.edn): exact pins, never \"latest\"; a change of\n# either goes through the jolt upgrade gate\nchezscheme = \"10.4.1\"\ncmake = \"4.4.4\"\nandroid-sdk = \"latest\"\nflutter = { version = \"latest\", platforms = \"\"\"\n[linux-x64]\nurl = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/linux/flutter_linux_{{ version }}-beta.tar.xz\"\n\n[macos-arm64]\nurl = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/macos/flutter_macos_arm64_{{ version }}-beta.zip\"\n\n[macos-x64]\nurl = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/macos/flutter_macos_{{ version }}-beta.zip\"\n\n[windows-x64]\nurl = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/windows/flutter_windows_{{ version }}-beta.zip\"\n\"\"\", version_json_path = \".releases[?channel=beta].version\", version_list_url = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/releases_macos.json\" }\n\n[env._]\npath = [\n  \"{{env.HOME}}/.local/share/mise/installs/android-sdk/1.0/platform-tools\",\n  \"{{env.HOME}}/.local/share/mise/installs/android-sdk/1.0/emulator\",\n]\n\n[env]\n#FLUTTER_STORAGE_BASE_URL = \"https://storage.flutter-io.cn\"\n#PUB_HOSTED_URL = \"https://pub.flutter-io.cn\"\n\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj (clojure)\n;; bb smoke:jolt — the J0a minimum-baseline smoke, run UNDER jolt with the\n;; :jolt alias (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §7.8, W8):\n;;\n;;   1. the :jolt alias loads yang.antlr.export and yang.antlr.packet from the\n;;      tracked roots, with no overlay, and both answer a known value;\n;;   2. jolt.ffi defcfn :blocking calls pass (libc usleep and strlen).\n;;\n;; Collect-safety is NOT asserted here: the RECORD lines show when a full\n;; collection finishes relative to a 400 ms call in each mode, but the plain\n;; (non-:blocking) control did not wait for its call to return on jolt\n;; 96d7b866 (J0a round-1 report), so the observation does not yet separate\n;; the two modes. The long-hash collect-safety gate is later J0a work.\n;;\n;; Prints PASS/FAIL per check and RECORD per observation; exits nonzero on any\n;; FAIL.\n(ns jolt-smoke\n  (:require [jolt.ffi :as ffi]))\n\n\n;; Loaded here rather than in the ns form, so the libs they add are observable.\n(def ^:private before (set (loaded-libs)))\n(require '[yang.antlr.export :as export] '[yang.antlr.packet :as packet])\n(def ^:private added (sort (remove before (loaded-libs))))\n\n(def failures (atom 0))\n\n\n(defn- check\n  [label ok? detail]\n  (when-not ok? (swap! failures inc))\n  (println (if ok? \"PASS\" \"FAIL\") label (pr-str detail)))\n\n\n;; 1. tracked load\n(check \"the closure of yang.antlr.export is exactly it and yang.antlr.packet (no transit)\"\n       (= '(yang.antlr.export yang.antlr.packet) added)\n       added)\n\n\n(check \"yang.antlr.packet/code-points \\\"aé😀\\\" = [97 233 128512] (its :clj branch)\"\n       (= [97 233 128512] (packet/code-points \"aé😀\"))\n       (packet/code-points \"aé😀\"))\n\n\n(check \"yang.antlr.packet/utf8-bytes \\\"aé😀\\\" = 7\"\n       (= 7 (packet/utf8-bytes \"aé😀\"))\n       (packet/utf8-bytes \"aé😀\"))\n\n\n(check \"yang.antlr.export/byte-offsets of [97 233 128512] = [0 1 3 7]\"\n       (= [0 1 3 7] (vec (export/byte-offsets [97 233 128512])))\n       (export/byte-offsets [97 233 128512]))\n\n\n;; 2. defcfn :blocking\n(ffi/load-library)\n(ffi/defcfn c-usleep-blocking \"usleep\" [:uint] :int :blocking)\n(ffi/defcfn c-strlen-blocking \"strlen\" [:pointer] :size_t :blocking)\n(ffi/defcfn c-usleep \"usleep\" [:uint] :int)\n\n\n(defn- ms\n  [t0]\n  (long (/ (- (System/nanoTime) t0) 1e6)))\n\n\n(let [t0 (System/nanoTime) r (c-usleep-blocking 200000) dt (ms t0)]\n  (check \"defcfn :blocking usleep(200 ms) returns 0 after >= 200 ms\"\n         (and (= 0 r) (>= dt 200)) {:result r :ms dt}))\n\n\n(let [p (ffi/string->ptr \"a\\u00e9\\ud83d\\ude00\")\n      r (try (c-strlen-blocking p) (finally (ffi/free p)))]\n  (check \"defcfn :blocking strlen of the UTF-8 C string \\\"aé😀\\\" = 7\"\n         (= 7 r) {:result r}))\n\n\n(defn- collect-during\n  \"On another thread run (call 400000); 50 ms in, run a full collection here.\n   Answers the timeline in ms from the thread's start.\"\n  [call]\n  (let [t0 (System/nanoTime)\n        log (atom [])\n        th (Thread. (fn []\n                      (swap! log conj [:call-start (ms t0)])\n                      (swap! log conj [:call-result (call 400000)])\n                      (swap! log conj [:call-end (ms t0)])))]\n    (.start th)\n    (Thread/sleep 50)\n    (swap! log conj [:collect-start (ms t0)])\n    (jolt.host/gc-full!)\n    (swap! log conj [:collect-end (ms t0)])\n    (.join th)\n    (into {} @log)))\n\n\n(println \"RECORD collect timeline, :blocking usleep(400 ms)\" (pr-str (collect-during c-usleep-blocking)))\n(println \"RECORD collect timeline, plain usleep(400 ms)\" (pr-str (collect-during c-usleep)))\n\n(println \"SUMMARY\" (if (zero? @failures) \"ok\" (str @failures \" failed\")))\n(System/exit (if (zero? @failures) 0 1))\n\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/src/jolt/README.md (markdown)\n# src/jolt\n\nThe jolt host source root (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §4.1-4.2).\nThe `:jolt` alias in `deps.edn` puts it before `src/cljc`, so a namespace here\noverrides the portable one on jolt only.\n\nOnly complete, narrow host implementations live here, as `.jolt` files with the\nsame public surface and contract tests as the portable namespace they replace.\nSmall representation differences go in `#?(:jolt ...)` branches of the shared\n`.cljc` source instead (`:cljd` first, then `:jolt`, then `:clj`/`:default`).\nNever a copy of `yin.repl`, `yin.vm.engine` or `dao.jing.cbor`.\n\nEmpty at J0a round 1: the baseline closure (`yang.antlr.export`,\n`yang.antlr.packet`) needs no host override.\n\n"}]},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_47b6aa5c61f14c10aa6e478b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"collab/1792458769000-engineer-jolt-j0a-baseline-r2.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:18:| F1: wrong `:cmake-path` | `jolt-toolchain.edn:44` now records the observed path `~/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake`. This matches `bootstrap-warm-r2.log:2` and the round-1 report's Environment section. |\ncollab/1792458769000-engineer-jolt-j0a-baseline-r2.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:20:| F4: missing `-Stree` log; latency quotes | `stree.log` holds the output of `jolt -Srepro -Stree -A:jolt`: nothing printed, exit 0 (the file is just `exit 0`), so the dependency tree is empty. The round-1 latencies come from the logs: `usleep(200 ms)` measured **205 ms** (`smoke-1.log`) and **200 ms** (`smoke-2.log`). I had reported 201/204, which came from runs whose output I did not save. This round's run measured 210 ms (`smoke-r2.log`). |"}]}],"meta":{"source":"tool","messageId":"dd9fdf1a-8117-4c88-8960-7f1de1151226"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 5 files other than the bootstrap/toolchain are unchanged (bb.edn, deps.edn, mise.toml, jolt_smoke.clj, README.md are identical to what I read previously — the contents match). The report r2 honestly corrects the misquotation.\n\nF2 bypass analysis:\n- Exact string equality `(= origin remote)`. The cold clone uses the declared URL string as-is, so `git remote get-url origin` returns exactly that → no false mismatches on the bootstrap-created checkout (confirmed with warm-r2 exit 0).\n- If manually cloned with `.git` suffix or trailing slash, it will mismatch → fails closed (safe, requires re-clone). No false positives from normalization: equality only holds when the stored URL matches the declaration byte-for-byte.\n- Residual issue: redirection via `url.insteadOf` may cause the declared URL to fetch from elsewhere — however the SHA + submodule + dirty checks still constrain the contents, so it's not a substantive bypass.\n- The negative log shows the correct reason and exit 1: \"has origin https://github.com/example/not-jolt, declared https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt\".\n\nF3: Recorded in the design doc §13.2:1468-1471, with a quote from the owner.\n\nF5: Comment inside verify! (\"Known gap (input to §6.4 gate hardening)...\").\n\nF4: stree.log exists (exit 0, output empty), and the r2 report corrects the latency quote with log-derived numbers (205/200/210).\n\nVerdict: SIGNED OFF. Under 300 words.\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-20 01:14:32 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-20 08:14:32 +07\nCoding-Agent: cmd\nSession-ID: 61966f9d-4875-4b42-9545-b0dc8a2c9891\n# Review: J0a round 2 - confirmation of fixes\nRole: Reviewer (read-only) | Model: qwen/qwen3.8-max\n\n## Verdict: SIGNED OFF\n\n| id | status | evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| F1 | CLOSED | jolt-toolchain.edn:44 now records `.../cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake`, matching bootstrap-warm-r2.log:2 and bootstrap-neg-origin.log:2. |\n| F2 | CLOSED | jolt_bootstrap.clj `verify!` (~:107-111): `git -C dir remote get-url origin` compared by exact string equality against the declared `:origin`, failing before the SHA check. bootstrap-neg-origin.log:3-4 shows exit 1 for the right reason: `has origin https://github.com/example/not-jolt, declared https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt`. |\n| F3 | CLOSED | docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1468-1471: \"Owner disposition, recorded 2026-10-20\" quoting the owner (\"confirm defaults, licensing local only, ws only. commission J0b\"); defaults 1-3 take effect, satisfying the §6.4/§10.1 precondition for the exact-Chez pin in worktree mise.toml:10. |\n| F4 | CLOSED | stree.log retains the empty `-Stree -A:jolt` output (file is just `exit 0`). The r2 report:20 also corrects the round-1 latency quotes to the log-backed numbers (205/200; r2 run 210, smoke-r2.log:5) and admits 201/204 came from unsaved runs. |\n| F5 | CLOSED | jolt_bootstrap.clj `verify!` (~:118-119) carries the comment \"Known gap (input to the §6.4 gate hardening): `status --porcelain` does not see changes to gitignored files inside the clone.\" |\n\n**Origin-check bypass analysis:** equality is byte-exact, so no normalization false-match. A `.git` suffix or trailing slash on a hand-made clone yields a false *mismatch*, which fails closed (re-clone needed), not a false pass; bootstrap's own cold clone stores the declared URL verbatim, so warm runs pass (bootstrap-warm-r2.log, exit 0). Residual: `url.insteadOf` rewriting could redirect fetches behind a matching origin string, but the full-SHA, submodule-map and dirty-tree checks still bind content, so it is not a practical bypass.\n\n**No other changes:** bb.edn, deps.edn, mise.toml, jolt_smoke.clj, src/jolt/README.md are byte-identical to round 1 on re-read; the only diffs are the two F1/F2/F5 edits plus the four new logs. Caveat: still no worktree `git status` (shell blocked); scope confirmation rests on file-level comparison and the orchestrator's re-run."}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1792458972797,"messageId":"18ef587c-b352-431e-9eeb-8bb2010459bd"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-20 01:31:53 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-20 08:31:53 +07\nCoding-Agent: cmd\nSession-ID: 61966f9d-4875-4b42-9545-b0dc8a2c9891\n# Task: independent review of J0c round 1 (ANTLR4 C++ parser feasibility ladder)\nRole: Reviewer (adversarial, read-only)\nImplementers:\n- Model: qwen/qwen3.8-max | Assigned: 2026-10-20 08:31:53 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: owner routing \"cmd for review\"; author is claude-opus-5-5; resume the J0a reviewer\n\nReview READ-ONLY the uncommitted change in the worktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c (branch jolt-j0c, base jolt-j0a 9f1f9144): modified antlr/python3/manifest.edn, bb.edn, jolt-toolchain.edn, src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj; new native/jolt-parser/CMakeLists.txt, native/jolt-parser/jolt_parser.cpp, src/dev/jolt_native.clj, src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj. Author report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792459030000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r1.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md. Spec: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md sections 6.1, 7 (7.2-7.8), 10.1 J0c row. The orchestrator re-ran the probe on macOS arm64: exit 0, six PASS lines and SUMMARY ok (tree of \"1 + 2\\n\" decoded in jolt; malformed \"1 +\\n\" returns syntax-error records, no exception).\nScope is the FEASIBILITY LADDER only (R1 pinned runtime build, R2 real Python3 grammar generated for C++ plus helpers, R3 extern \"C\" wrapper called from jolt). Check: (a) R1: are the runtime source revision and SHA-256 really pinned and enforced (fetch only by hash, tamper case), is the build reproducible enough as claimed, are CMake/compiler flags recorded; (b) R2: the generator edit in src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj and the manifest edit touch SHARED tooling used by the existing Java/JavaScript/Dart targets: do they leave those three targets' behaviour, recorded digests and helper handling byte-for-byte unchanged? Look for any path where the existing targets' output or digests could change; check the exact-text patches for the C++ target are sound; check :license/:redistribution blocks survived the brace mistake the author reports; (c) R3: read jolt_parser.cpp adversarially: exception containment (every entry point catches everything including std::bad_alloc), buffer ownership and free path, embedded NUL and invalid UTF-8 handling, size bounds, any pointer or C++ object visible to the guest, thread/static state (ANTLR C++ shares static caches; is anything unsafe even for one worker), UB, integer overflow in length fields; (d) probe assertions: can any PASS pass while the thing is broken; (e) does the change touch anything forbidden (shared dao.stream / dao.data / dao.jing / yin.vm source, the main tree)? (f) is the report honest about what is NOT done and about unresolved helper provenance?\nUnder 700 words, final response only (you cannot write files), header fields on top, verdict SIGNED OFF / SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES / NOT SIGNED OFF, findings table (id, severity, file:line, evidence, correction), and what you could not verify."}],"meta":{"source":"user","createdAt":1792459918060,"messageId":"35aee565-cf45-4a2d-9a62-92414437a15a"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let's gather the files. Things to read:\n\n1. Author's report: collab/1792459030000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r1.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md\n2. Worktree files:\n   - antlr/python3/manifest.edn (has changes) — compare with the main tree / jolt-j0a base\n   - bb.edn (has changes)\n   - jolt-toolchain.edn (has changes)\n   - src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj (has changes) — compare with the base\n   - native/jolt-parser/CMakeLists.txt (new)\n   - native/jolt-parser/jolt_parser.cpp (new)\n   - src/dev/jolt_native.clj (new)\n   - src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj (new)\n3. Spec sections 7.2-7.7 (lines 696-841), 6.1 already read.\n\nBase for comparison: worktree jolt-j0a (currently committed as 9f1f9144?) or the main tree. The main tree has antlr/python3/manifest.edn and src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj.\n\nLet's start reading in parallel.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll review J0c round 1. First the author's report and the new/changed worktree files.\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_c77840dc3d8a45359aaecd05","name":"read_file","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792459030000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r1.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_1dc3f0f36d50455b861ed997","name":"read_file","input":{"paths":["/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/native/jolt-parser/jolt_parser.cpp","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/native/jolt-parser/CMakeLists.txt","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/antlr/python3/manifest.edn","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/antlr/python3/manifest.edn"]}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1792459937960,"messageId":"bc2fa8f2-6a5e-45d3-a882-3312606aafd9"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_c77840dc3d8a45359aaecd05","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 187 lines\n1: Created-GMT: 2026-10-20 01:17:10 GMT\n2: Created-Local: 2026-10-20 08:17:10 +07\n3: Coding-Agent: claude\n4: Session-ID: 8f45af4f-0557-4cfa-a375-78525ee6a40e\n5: # Findings: J0c round 1 - the ANTLR4 C++ parser built and called from jolt (feasibility ladder)\n6: Role: Compiler & AST / Stream engineer (native build and FFI probe)\n7: Implementers:\n8: - Model: claude-opus-5-5 | Assigned: 2026-10-20 08:17:10 +07 | Status: done (round 1, macOS arm64) | Rationale: owner routing \"opus-5.5 for implementation, cmd for review\"\n9: \n10: ## Verdict\n11: \n12: | Rung | Result | Evidence |\n13: |---|---|---|\n14: | R1 pinned ANTLR4 C++ runtime 4.13.2, hash-checked, built with mise CMake | **DONE** | `r1-build.log` (exit 0, 39.67 s); negative tamper test `r1-neg-sha.log` (exit 1) |\n15: | R2 real pinned Python3 grammar generated with `-Dlanguage=Cpp`, helpers identified | **DONE** | `r2-gen.log` (exit 0); deterministic re-run against recorded digests `r2-gen-verify.log`, `r2-gen-verify2.log` (exit 0) |\n16: | R3 extern \"C\" wrapper, `:blocking` defcfn call from jolt, bytes decoded in jolt | **DONE** | `r3-build.log` (exit 0); `r3-probe-1.log`, `r3-probe-2.log`, `final-probe.log` (7/7 PASS, exit 0) |\n17: \n18: No rung failed. **macOS arm64 only; Linux x86_64 (shiva) NOT RUN.**\n19: \n20: - Worktree: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c`, branch `jolt-j0c` from `jolt-j0a` @ `9f1f9144`. Changes are uncommitted and nothing is staged.\n21: - Logs: `…/jolt-j0c/build/j0c/logs/`.\n22: - Baseline: `bb bootstrap:jolt` (cold) exit 0 in 81.71 s (`bootstrap.log`). A final `bb smoke:jolt` exit 0 (`final-smoke.log`).\n23: \n24: ## R1: the C++ runtime (DONE)\n25: \n26: - **Declaration**, in `jolt-toolchain.edn :native :antlr4-cpp-runtime`:\n27:   - Version 4.13.2, BSD-3-Clause.\n28:   - Source `https://www.antlr.org/download/antlr4-cpp-runtime-4.13.2-source.zip`. That is the official C++ runtime distribution; the GitHub 4.13.2 release has no C++ asset.\n29:   - SHA-256 `0ed13668906e86dbc0dcddf30fdee68c10203dea4e83852b4edb810821bee3c4`.\n30:   - Upstream: `antlr/antlr4` tag `4.13.2`, tag object `2ac185af855ff39b4b8c41854b756767099c356f`, commit `cc82115a4e7f53d71d9d905caa2c2dfa4da58899`, path `runtime/Cpp`.\n31: - **Not verified:** that the zip's contents equal `runtime/Cpp` at that commit. I compared no file-level digests. This is a provenance gap for review.\n32: - **`bb build:jolt-native`** (new; runs `src/dev/jolt_native.clj`):\n33:   - Fetches into `build/native/src/` only when the archive is absent, and accepts it only at the declared SHA-256. A mismatch deletes the file and fails.\n34:   - Extracts fresh and builds with the mise CMake into `build/native/darwin-arm64/`.\n35:   - Writes `build/native/darwin-arm64/build-record.edn` with tool versions, flags and output SHA-256s.\n36:   - Nothing downloads at namespace load.\n37: - **Flags:** `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DANTLR_BUILD_CPP_TESTS=OFF -DANTLR_BUILD_SHARED=OFF -DANTLR_BUILD_STATIC=ON -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON -DCMAKE_CXX_STANDARD=17`.\n38:   - **Static linking**, so the runtime is linked into the single wrapper dylib that jolt loads. There is no second library or rpath to resolve at load time (§7.2 asks for this choice to be explicit).\n39:   - **Tests are OFF** because the runtime's `ANTLR_BUILD_CPP_TESTS=ON` default makes CMake download googletest during the build.\n40: - **Toolchain:** CMake 4.4.4 (mise, `…/cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake`); compiler Apple clang 21.0.0 (clang-2100.1.1.101). The build has 2 harmless upstream warnings.\n41: - **Output:** `build/native/darwin-arm64/antlr4-runtime/lib/libantlr4-runtime.a`.\n42:   - **Finding:** its SHA-256 differs on every identical rebuild: `e086b10d…`, `94bcda41…`, `28ce9a67…` across three builds. The archive is not reproducible, presumably because `ar` embeds timestamps (not investigated).\n43:   - The linked dylib was byte-identical across all three builds (see R3), so gates should digest the dylib, not the archive.\n44: - **Negative test:** I appended one byte to the cached zip. The task answered `has SHA-256 9bc059e7…, declared 0ed13668…; deleted` and exited 1 (`r1-neg-sha.log`). I restored the original zip and confirmed its SHA-256.\n45: \n46: ## R2: generating the C++ parser (DONE)\n47: \n48: **Helpers exist at the pinned grammar revision.** grammars-v4 `8af0d4c26c796ea27c15c3d85418f2d0f77c3adb`, `python/python3/Cpp/`, has:\n49: - `Python3LexerBase.h` (890 bytes)\n50: - `Python3LexerBase.cpp` (3784 bytes)\n51: - `Python3ParserBase.h` (233 bytes)\n52: - `Python3ParserBase.cpp` (182 bytes)\n53: - `transformGrammar.py`\n54: \n55: The four helpers are now in `manifest.edn :files` with their BLAKE3 digests, fetched by the existing generator at the pinned revision:\n56: \n57: | file | BLAKE3 |\n58: |---|---|\n59: | `Cpp/Python3LexerBase.h` | `393ff86d…817a` |\n60: | `Cpp/Python3LexerBase.cpp` | `cd598ca5…a5b3` |\n61: | `Cpp/Python3ParserBase.h` | `59afaba9…3349` |\n62: | `Cpp/Python3ParserBase.cpp` | `38a2790b…c28b` |\n63: \n64: - **License and provenance:** no notice in any file, so they are recorded **UNRESOLVED** exactly like the Java/JS/Dart helpers. `:redistribution :blocked-until` now names C++ too, and generated output stays under `build/` (local build only, never staged).\n65: - **The C++ target needs more than `-Dlanguage=Cpp`:**\n66:   1. **A grammar transform.** The pinned `.g4` files carry Java-syntax actions (`this.onNewLine()` and similar) and two `// Insert here @header for C++ …` placeholders. Upstream's own `Cpp/transformGrammar.py` (BLAKE3 `7600aaee…50ec`) rewrites `this.`→`this->` and fills the headers. I recorded the identical edits as 13 exact-text `:patches` on `Python3Lexer.g4`/`Python3Parser.g4` under the `:cpp` target, rather than running the Python script. The two identical `{ this.CannotBePlusMinus() }?` lines are disambiguated by their rule names `literal_pattern`/`literal_expr`.\n67:   2. **The positioned NEWLINE/DEDENT patch.** The other three targets all carry it, and I ported it to the C++ token factory as 5 exact-text patches on `Cpp/Python3LexerBase.{h,cpp}`:\n68:      - a new `positionedToken(type, start, stop)`;\n69:      - NEWLINE placed on its newline characters (`tokenStartCharIndex .. +newLine.size()-1`);\n70:      - DEDENT and the end-of-input NEWLINE zero-width at `getCharIndex()`.\n71: \n72:      **This is a helper patch port I wrote, disclosed here for review against the Java patch.** It is not a hand-written parser. It is not yet checked against the JVM oracle (span parity is later J0c work).\n73: - **Generator change** (`src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj`): a target may now declare `:exts`. C++ keeps and digests both `.h` and `.cpp`, where previously only the first helper's extension was kept, which would have deleted every header. The Java, JavaScript and Dart targets are unchanged: no `:exts` means the old behaviour.\n74: - **Command:** `clojure -M:antlr-gen --target cpp` (ANTLR tool 4.13.2 from the existing `:antlr-gen` alias).\n75:   - First run: exit 0, 16.75 s. It generated 8 files in `build/antlr/python3/cpp/`, all ASCII (the generator enforces this).\n76:   - I recorded their BLAKE3 digests as `:cpp :generated`. Re-runs exited 0 with matching digests, so generation is deterministic and the drift check is live.\n77:   - Digests: `Python3Lexer.cpp a8be1b51…`, `Python3Lexer.h a1cb6339…`, `Python3LexerBase.cpp 65027edf…`, `Python3LexerBase.h 8548fd2c…`, `Python3Parser.cpp d30cc4df…`, `Python3Parser.h 5e62a9c3…`, `Python3ParserBase.cpp 38a2790b…` (unpatched), `Python3ParserBase.h 59afaba9…` (unpatched).\n78: - **Defect I introduced and then fixed:** my first manifest edit had one extra `}`. That made the top-level map close early. `clojure.edn/read-string` then silently ignored the rest, dropping `:license` and `:redistribution`, while generation still worked because it doesn't read them. cljstyle exposed it. After the fix, all five top-level keys read back with nothing trailing, matching HEAD. **Worth a guard in the generator:** read with a `PushbackReader` and reject trailing forms.\n79: - **Divergences in the C++ helper, noted and not fixed:**\n80:   - Its `commonToken` takes line/column from `lastToken` (Java takes them from the lexer).\n81:   - Its `getIndentationCount` iterates UTF-8 bytes, not code points.\n82: \n83:   Both are candidates for the later JVM-oracle parity comparison.\n84: \n85: ## R3: the wrapper and the jolt call (DONE)\n86: \n87: - **Location:** `native/jolt-parser/` (`CMakeLists.txt`, `jolt_parser.cpp`). It is a new top-level directory for hand-written native sources:\n88:   - not `src/`, whose roots are Clojure source roots on jolt's classpath;\n89:   - not `antlr/`, which holds only pinned grammar inputs and manifests;\n90:   - not `build/`, which is for generated and untracked output.\n91: - **ABI** (`extern \"C\"`, C types only):\n92:   - `int32_t jolt_parser_parse(const uint8_t* src, size_t len, uint8_t** out, size_t* out_len)`\n93:   - `void jolt_parser_free(uint8_t*)`\n94:   - `int32_t jolt_parser_layout_version(void)`\n95: - **Error handling:** every entry catches `std::exception` and `(...)` and returns −2/−3 with a message buffer. −1 means invalid arguments, −4 means over the 64 MiB output bound.\n96: - **Buffer layout:** private, fixed-width, little-endian: magic `JPT1`, layout version, status, rule-name table, symbolic-name table, preorder records, collected listener errors. The full layout is documented in the source header.\n97:   - Each rule record carries its index and child count. Each token record carries type, code-point start/stop and UTF-8 text.\n98:   - This is raw marshalling only: no Jing encoder, no `toStringTree`, no packet. It is a subset of the §7.3 field list (first-failure evidence and context start are later).\n99: - **Build:** `bb build:jolt-native` links `libjolt_parser.dylib` against the pinned static runtime and the generated sources (`r3-build.log`, exit 0, 49.95 s).\n100:   - SHA-256 `fd8ac980a123ac9610743d36c12930bc539de1b40edb2e649f40f9e4b8f9df76`, **identical across three builds**. Mach-O arm64, 1,356,232 bytes, depends only on `libc++` and `libSystem`.\n101:   - **Finding:** `CXX_VISIBILITY_PRESET hidden` applies only to my own translation units. The three `jolt_parser_*` entries plus about 1,556 `antlr4::` C++ symbols from the static archive are exported (`nm -gU`). A later round should use an exported-symbols list (`-exported_symbols_list` / a version script) so the runtime cannot interpose or be interposed.\n102: - **jolt side** (`src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj`, run with `\"$JOLT_HOME\"/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj`):\n103:   - **Load and bind:** `ffi/load-library` loads the dylib by absolute path. `(ffi/defcfn c-parse \"jolt_parser_parse\" [:pointer :size_t :pointer :pointer] :int :blocking)`, plus free and version.\n104:   - **Call:** `parse-bytes` copies the UTF-8 source into an `ffi/alloc` buffer and calls the parser. It copies the result with `ffi/read-array` into a jolt byte array, frees it through `jolt_parser_free` in a `finally`, and frees its own cells. No pointer leaves the function.\n105:   - **Decode:** the decoding is plain Clojure over the byte array.\n106: - **Result for `\"1 + 2\\n\"`:** status 0, a 3196-byte buffer consumed exactly, parse call 2.7–3.6 ms. The decoded tree:\n107: \n108: ```\n109: file_input\n110:   stmt\n111:     simple_stmts\n112:       simple_stmt\n113:         expr_stmt\n114:           testlist_star_expr\n115:             test\n116:               or_test\n117:                 and_test\n118:                   not_test\n119:                     comparison\n120:                       expr\n121:                         expr\n122:                           atom_expr\n123:                             atom\n124:                               NUMBER \"1\" [0,0]\n125:                         ADD \"+\" [2,2]\n126:                         expr\n127:                           atom_expr\n128:                             atom\n129:                               NUMBER \"2\" [4,4]\n130:       NEWLINE \"\\n\" [5,5]\n131:   EOF \"<EOF>\" [6,5]\n132: ```\n133: \n134: - **Checks: 7/7 PASS** on three runs (`r3-probe-1.log`, `r3-probe-2.log`, `final-probe.log`):\n135:   - the layout version is 1;\n136:   - magic, layout and exact consumption;\n137:   - no errors;\n138:   - the root is `file_input`;\n139:   - the token sequence with code-point spans `NUMBER 1 [0,0]`, `ADD + [2,2]`, `NUMBER 2 [4,4]`, `NEWLINE [5,5]`;\n140:   - the last token is EOF;\n141:   - malformed `\"1 +\\n\"` returns status 0 with a syntax-error buffer of two listener errors (`no viable alternative at input '+'` at 1:2, `extraneous input '\\n' …` at 2:0), and no exception crosses the boundary.\n142: - **One iteration fixed:** the first run failed the EOF check because ANTLR's EOF type is −1 and my decoder looked only in the non-negative symbol table. The probe now names −1 `\"EOF\"`, as the packet contract does. The wrapper was unchanged.\n143: - **Not compared against the JVM yet.** The NEWLINE span `[5,5]` comes from the ported positioned patch, and the EOF span `[6,5]` (zero-width at index 6) is plausible but unchecked.\n144: \n145: ## Collect-safety observations (nothing built on `:blocking` semantics)\n146: \n147: - The parse entry is bound `:blocking` as §7.5 prescribes. No collect-safety claim is made: J0a found that a full collection finishes during a 400 ms call whether or not the call is `:blocking`, and I did not re-test that here.\n148: - The `\"1 + 2\\n\"` parse takes about 3 ms, too short to observe a collection against. A long-parse collection test (§7.5) needs a larger input and a mechanism that can discriminate, and is later J0c work.\n149: \n150: ## Not done this round (later J0c rounds; not started)\n151: - Corpus parity with the JVM/Node/Dart oracle (the §7.8 fixed set), the exporter `ops` facade and `cst.jolt`, first-failure evidence and completeness probes.\n152: - Two-worker/cache isolation, static-cache growth audit, thread/stack budget, collect-safety under a long parse, sanitizer and lifetime runs, injected C++ exceptions, embedded-NUL and invalid-input policy, bounded-response failure.\n153: - The exported-symbols list. Checking the runtime zip's contents against the upstream tag tree. A reproducible archive build.\n154: - Linux x86_64 on shiva.\n155: \n156: ## Commands (foreground, in the worktree) and exit codes\n157: \n158: | command | exit | wall |\n159: |---|---|---|\n160: | `git worktree add …/jolt-j0c -b jolt-j0c jolt-j0a` (from the repo root); `mise trust` | 0 | n/a |\n161: | `bb bootstrap:jolt` (cold clone) | 0 | 81.71 s |\n162: | `gh api repos/antlr/antlr4/git/ref/tags/4.13.2` and `…/git/tags/2ac185af…` (tag → commit) | 0 | n/a |\n163: | `gh api repos/antlr/grammars-v4/contents/python/python3/Cpp?ref=8af0d4c2…` and curl of the 5 files to `build/j0c/upstream/` | 0 | n/a |\n164: | `bb build:jolt-native` (R1, runtime only at that point) | 0 | 39.67 s |\n165: | `clojure -M:antlr-gen --target cpp` (first; and two verify re-runs) | 0 / 0 / 0 | 16.75 s / 2.24 s / n/a |\n166: | `bb build:jolt-native` (runtime + wrapper; the first attempt failed on my `string_view` compile error, fixed) | 1, then 0 | 49.95 s |\n167: | `\"$JOLT_HOME\"/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj` (×3 after the decoder fix) | 0 | 6.2–7.2 s |\n168: | tamper test: append a byte to the cached zip, then `bb build:jolt-native`; then restore | 1 (expected) | n/a |\n169: | final `bb build:jolt-native`, probe, `bb smoke:jolt` | 0 / 0 / 0 | 46.47 s / n/a / n/a |\n170: | `mise exec -- cljstyle check` on changed files | clean. `manifest.edn` still reports the same 3 pre-existing JS-patch indentation hunks that HEAD has | n/a |\n171: \n172: ## Files (worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c`, uncommitted)\n173: - Modified:\n174:   - `antlr/python3/manifest.edn`: Cpp helper files and digests, `:cpp` target, patches, generated digests, license and redistribution.\n175:   - `bb.edn`: task `build:jolt-native`.\n176:   - `jolt-toolchain.edn`: `:native :antlr4-cpp-runtime`.\n177:   - `src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj`: `:exts`.\n178: - Added:\n179:   - `native/jolt-parser/CMakeLists.txt`\n180:   - `native/jolt-parser/jolt_parser.cpp`\n181:   - `src/dev/jolt_native.clj`\n182:   - `src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj`\n183: - Untracked build output, never staged:\n184:   - `build/native/` (src zip, runtime, wrapper, build-record.edn)\n185:   - `build/antlr/python3/` (upstream cache, generated Cpp)\n186:   - `build/tools/jolt/`\n187:   - `build/j0c/`"}]},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_1dc3f0f36d50455b861ed997","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 4/4 files\n--- File Contents ---\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/antlr/python3/manifest.edn (unknown)\n{:grammar {:repo \"antlr/grammars-v4\",\n           :path \"python/python3\",\n           :revision \"8af0d4c26c796ea27c15c3d85418f2d0f77c3adb\",\n           ;; The two MIT grammars are vendored verbatim beside this manifest\n           ;; (owner decision \"Vendor .g4 only\"); the Java, JavaScript and Dart\n           ;; helpers, whose licence is unresolved, are still fetched at the pinned revision.\n           ;; Every file is digest-checked either way.\n           :files {\"Python3Lexer.g4\"\n                   {