index 0; `idx()` saturation maps it to the documented 0xFFFFFFFF \"none\", so no UB reaches the wire, and DEDENT at index 0 is unreachable in practice. Also C++ sets text `\"\"` (read back from source) like Java's null; the ported patch matches the Java semantics modulo the disclosed line/col divergence. | None now; keep both under the JVM-oracle span-parity check the report already defers. |\n| F3 | info | antlr/python3/manifest.edn (:files), src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj (fetch-grammar!) | Adding the 4 Cpp helpers to `:files` makes every target's `gen:antlr` run fetch and digest-check them (r2-gen-verify.log:2-13), so a Cpp fetch failure now breaks Java/JS/Dart generation too. Outputs/digests unaffected. | Acceptable coupling (all targets re-pin together); note it in the manifest comment. |\n| F4 | info | orchestrator brief vs final-probe.log | The brief says \"six PASS lines\"; the log shows **7** PASS + SUMMARY ok + exit 0 (probe has 7 checks). Report's 7/7 is correct; the brief undercounted. | Orchestrator bookkeeping only. |\n\n## What checks out\n\n- (a) R1: jolt-toolchain.edn `:native :antlr4-cpp-runtime` pins version, URL, SHA-256, upstream tag/commit, cmake flags; jolt_native.clj `fetch!` downloads only when absent, verifies SHA-256 on both fresh and cached archives, deletes+fails on mismatch (r1-neg-sha.log: correct reason, exit 1). build-record.edn captures cmake path/version, cxx version, flags, output SHA-256s. Non-reproducible `.a` (ar timestamps) and byte-identical dylib are disclosed, with the right conclusion (digest the dylib). Zip-vs-tag content equality is NOT verified - honestly flagged (report:31).\n- (b) R2 shared-tool safety: yang_antlr_gen.clj's only behavioral change is opt-in `:exts`; for targets without it, `target-exts` returns `[(helper-ext)]` and `not-any?`/`some ends-with?` are predicate-identical to the old single-ext code, so Java/JS/Dart filtering, staging, patches and digests are untouched. Manifest `:generated` digests for all three are byte-identical to base. Exact-text patches fail closed (`apply-patch` throws unless exactly one occurrence; the duplicate `CannotBePlusMinus` lines are disambiguated by rule name). `:license`/`:redistribution` survived the brace mistake: all five top-level keys present, Cpp helpers recorded UNRESOLVED, `blocked-until` names C++.\n- (c) R3: length-based `std::string(src,len)` preserves embedded NULs; 64 MiB bound (-4); `-1` arg check; `idx()` saturation prevents u32 overflow; only `uint8_t*`/`size_t` cross the boundary; malloc/free matched via `jolt_parser_free`; tree owned by the per-call parser, freed at scope exit; per-call lexer/parser/listener objects, static ATN read-only (two-worker audit correctly deferred, §7.4); walk recursion depth unbounded - inherent to ANTLR recursive descent, §7.6 budget deferred and disclosed. The `message()` escape (F1) is the only containment hole.\n- (d) Probe: assertions are non-tautological - exact buffer consumption (`:consumed = :length`), exact token/span list via `(butlast tokens)` (empty list fails), root rule name, malformed case requires status 0 + buffer status 1 + nonempty errors, and the log shows the real listener messages; decode handles EOF type -1. Free in `finally` on every path; no pointer escapes `parse-bytes`.\n- (e) Scope: bb.edn delta is only the `build:jolt-native` task (:18-21); no dao.stream/dao.data/dao.jing/yin.vm source touched; main-tree manifest and generator confirmed at base versions.\n- (f) Report honesty: extensive NOT-done list matching §7.8 (corpus parity, exporter/cst.jolt, worker isolation, collect-safety, sanitizers, NUL/invalid-UTF-8 policy, exported-symbols list, Linux); helper provenance explicitly UNRESOLVED; helper divergences and the ported-patch authorship disclosed.\n\n## Could not verify\n\n- Upstream truth of the zip SHA-256, tag/commit IDs, and helper BLAKE3s (no network); zip contents vs `runtime/Cpp` at the tag (author-disclosed gap).\n- Re-running Java/JS/Dart generation to