P=17 on both ✓. macOS: SO_SNDBUF 0x1001=4097 ✓, SO_RCVBUF 0x1002 ✓, EAGAIN 35 ✓, EMSGSIZE 40 ✓, ENOBUFS 55 ✓. All correct against the actual headers. Platform detection is via native/os; anything else throws at load time. No macOS values in Linux paths: the errno constant in the label comes from consts; the drain cap of 65536 is platform-neutral; the item 3 injection uses the EAGAIN/ENOBUFS variables. ✓. One check: recv!'s would-block classification uses only EAGAIN — on Linux EWOULDBLOCK==EAGAIN so no problem; on macOS they're both 35 so no problem.\n\n(b) Linux SO_SNDBUF assertion: set-r returns [0 11] — setsockopt result 0; read-back 4608 ≥ 4096 ✓; restoration: request 9216 → read-back 18432 ≥ 18432 ✓. Is this tautological? It asserts that the kernel behavior documented in socket(7) (doubling, floor SOCK_MIN_SNDBUF=4096? 2048*2=4096, but shiva's udp_wmem_min=4096; observed value 4608 = max(2*2048, SOCK_MIN_SNDBUF=2304*2=4608?) Actually Linux's SOCK_MIN_SNDBUF is around 2304*2=4608 — yes, 4608 matches the floor. For 9216, 2*9216=18432 ≥. \"At least twice\" accommodates the floor. Not tautological: the actual setsockopt return code and read-back value are verified, and would fail if the kernel didn't double (in which case it would read 2048 < 4096). Honest label \"[linux]\". Sound.\n\n(c) Comparison of macOS and Linux labels: except that Linux adds \"[linux] SO_SNDBUF read-back...\" and the errno number in the label differs (a platform constant, correctly), identical. Both are 36 vs 37. No weakened or skipped items on Linux; everything else uses the same assertions. Weaknesses common to both platforms relative to §8.3:\n- Item 3: naturally occurring send-side EAGAIN/ENOBUFS was not observed on either platform (histogram is all :sent); would-block is only asserted via injection (labeled as [injected]). §8.3 item 3 explicitly permits injection \"when EAGAIN cannot be induced over loopback\", provided it is separately labeled and actual successful syscalls are also exercised alongside — the probe does exactly that ([natural] actual sendto/recvfrom succeeds after injection; naturally occurring receive-side would-block is also naturally asserted). So this conforms to spec, with disclosure. The report states natural would-block remains as RECORD. Good.\n- Short sends: injection only (impossible to induce naturally over SOCK_DGRAM) — labeled as [injected]. Spec item 1 states short sends are errors; injection is reasonable; spec doesn't forbid it. OK.\n- Item 2: MSG_TRUNC unused (uses N+1 sentinel instead) — spec says \"if using recvmsg/MSG_TRUNC instead, bind and verify it\" — unused; constant is declared but marked unused. No problem.\n- Oversize semantics: recv with limit N returns :oversize, receives only N+1 bytes (truncated by recvfrom) but asserts \"no :bytes key\" (never returns a successful prefix) and consumes the whole thing. Spec: \"lengths beyond N surface an oversize/truncation error, never a successful prefix\" ✓.\n- Item 4: poller wait, separate fiber progress, wake, cancellation, close, cleanup ✓ on both platforms (epoll on shiva).\n- Item 5: headers record jolt SHA + dirty count, chez version + path, uname, OS release, sysctls/proc values, MTU; packet lengths/counts in details; error traces in details; poller wake evidence in traces; cleanup results present ✓.\n\nOne subtle point: in the shiva log's item 4 \"poller table holds no entry for closed fd\", :fds {6 {...}} is shown — wait, that's a check about fd c; the debug shows fds {6 ...} — fd 6 is socket b (still open), so `contains? fds c` is false → PASS. No problem, and the final cleanup asserts it's empty.\n\nAlso, \"waits 0\" vs macOS's \"waits 1\" in round-trips — on Linux packets often arrive before recv (faster); recv-wait gets the packet immediately with waits 0. In item 4, waits ≥ 1 is asserted (park is required) — passes on shiva with waits 1. No relaxation.\n\n(d) Report vs log: report claims 36 assertions macOS × 5 runs, Linux expected value 37 — shiva log shows exactly 37/37/3. Report claims labels are identical to run-6 (cannot verify run-6 diff, but run-7 exists). Report is honest that at time of writing Linux was UNTESTED; subsequent shiva runs (by orchestrator) confirmed. Report claims \"run-11 from jolt-j0a worktree\" — log exists. Does run.sh's output claim more than it shows? run.sh header outputs jolt-sha dirty=0 — matches §8.3 item 5. One nuance: shiva log's `chez: /home/sto/...` — no problem.\n\nPotential finding: run.sh's `sysctl` label line on Linux outputs \"sysctl:\" with net.core... entries — no problem. `sed -n 's/^PRETTY_NAME=...'` is POSIX-compliant. `sw_vers` runs only in the Darwin branch. `git -C` is used on both — is git available on shiva? The log shows jolt-sha with output → yes. All POSIX sh: case, tr, wc, sed, cat — no problem. `$(...)` nesting is fine even in dash. `[ -x ]` no problem. One portability nitpick: `echo $k | tr / .` inside a for loop — word splitting of unquoted $k is intentional; POSIX OK.\n\nCandidate findings:\n1. INFO: run.sh sources build/tools/jolt-env.sh relative to CWD (must be run from repo root; noted in header). Minor: script resolves probe path via $0's dirname but env file via CWD — could source \"$dir/../../../build/tools/jolt-env.sh\"? Actually J0a layout env is at repo root's build/tools/jolt-env.sh; the comment says run from repo root. Minor portability note.\n2. INFO: `msg-trunc` constant is declared but unused (documented as such) — no problem.\n3. LOW/INFO: item 3's naturally occurring would-block is never observed on either platform → :would-block send path is demonstrated only via injection; however this is explicitly permitted by spec (§8.3 item 3) provided it is labeled and actual syscalls are exercised alongside — satisfied. Not a defect; noted for the record.\n4. Linux RECORD \"drained receiver {:packets-delivered 93}\" vs macOS's 745 — receiver drops due to smaller effective buffer; recording only, no problem.\n5. One more check: does any macOS hardcoding remain in Linux paths? item-2's drain cap 65536 is platform-neutral. The comment \"macOS stops lower\" is fine. Check label \"errno 35\" — now outputs EAGAIN variable (label shows errno 11 on shiva ✓).\n6. bisection [1,65507]: on Linux max-ok=65507, over=65508 → EMSGSIZE 90 ✓ matches spec item 2 (65508 > IPv4 max).\n\nThings I cannot verify: identity of shiva-2/3 (the task says identical; only one read — should I quickly read 2 and 3? Word budget is fine but reading three long logs consumes tokens; task states \"three identical results\" and orchestrator's byte-match verification of probe files. Spot check is possible. Also contents of j0a-smoke-shiva.log/j0a-bootstrap-shiva.log unread. Let me quickly read these two j0a shiva logs, and check the SUMMARY lines of shiva-2/3 with grep.\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Quick spot-checks: shiva runs 2-3 summaries and the shiva J0a logs.\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_10125ec324424f41952bf246","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"SUMMARY|exit:|jolt-sha|chez:|uname:","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/build/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva","output_mode":"content","-n":true}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_0ad81e0ce18c4ed8a97c9f30","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"SUMMARY|exit|verified|wrote|jolt |chez ","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/build/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0a-smoke-shiva.log","output_mode":"content","-n":true}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_e9a2d7085a7047539cfa20a7","name":"read_file","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/build/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0a-bootstrap-shiva.log","offset":-25}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1792487559800,"messageId":"b3ce6c85-7f9a-4d3a-8148-76a74ba3c05f"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_10125ec324424f41952bf246","content":[{"type":"text","text":"build/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-3.log:2:jolt-sha: 96d7b8662d7c491722445bf976b2e25e36ce5d63 dirty=0\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-3.log:3:chez: /home/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme 10.4.1\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-3.log:4:uname: Linux x86_64 Ubuntu 24.04.5 LTS\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-3.log:49:SUMMARY 37 assertions: 37 pass, 0 fail; 3 records\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-3.log:50:exit: 0\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-2.log:2:jolt-sha: 96d7b8662d7c491722445bf976b2e25e36ce5d63 dirty=0\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-2.log:3:chez: /home/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme 10.4.1\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-2.log:4:uname: Linux x86_64 Ubuntu 24.04.5 LTS\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-2.log:49:SUMMARY 37 assertions: 37 pass, 0 fail; 3 records\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-2.log:50:exit: 0\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0a-smoke-shiva.log:9:SUMMARY ok\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-1.log:2:jolt-sha: 96d7b8662d7c491722445bf976b2e25e36ce5d63 dirty=0\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-1.log:3:chez: /home/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme 10.4.1\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-1.log:4:uname: Linux x86_64 Ubuntu 24.04.5 LTS\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-1.log:49:SUMMARY 37 assertions: 37 pass, 0 fail; 3 records\nbuild/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0b-shiva-1.log:50:exit: 0"}]},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_0ad81e0ce18c4ed8a97c9f30","content":[{"type":"text","text":"build/jolt-spike/j0b/shiva/j0a-smoke-shiva.log:9:SUMMARY ok"}]},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_e9a2d7085a7047539cfa20a7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 10 lines\nNote: showing the last 10 lines, which is the whole file.\n1: chez 10.4.1 threaded #t /home/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme\n2: cmake version 4.4.4 /home/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/cmake-4.4.4-linux-x86_64/bin/cmake\n3: cloning https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt into /home/sto/ci/datomworld-jolt-j0a/build/tools/jolt\n4: jolt 96d7b8662d7c491722445bf976b2e25e36ce5d63 with 7 submodules verified\n5: wrote /home/sto/ci/datomworld-jolt-j0a/build/tools/jolt-env.sh\n6: jolt smoke (+ 1 2) => 3\n7: \n8: real\t0m21.204s\n9: user\t0m28.571s\n10: sys\t0m3.795s"}]}],"meta":{"source":"tool","messageId":"47bf7e93-07c6-4b85-abc1-1e61cbe243c7"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All evidence has been verified. Writing the review. Within 450 words.\n\nFindings:\n- Constants are all correct (cross-checked against actual Linux/macOS headers from my own knowledge): Linux EAGAIN 11, EMSGSIZE 90, ENOBUFS 105, EBADF 9, SO_SNDBUF 7, SO_RCVBUF 8, MSG_TRUNC 0x20, SOCK_DGRAM 2, IPPROTO_UDP 17; macOS 35/40/55/9, 0x1001/0x1002, 0x10, 2, 17. Unsupported platforms throw at load time. No cross-contamination: errno labels/injections are derived from consts (shiva's log displays errno 11/105 labels).\n- (b) Linux SO_SNDBUF assertion: not a tautology — it requires setsockopt to return 0 AND the actual readback to be ≥ 2× the requested value (4608 ≥ 4096; 18432 ≥ 18432). 4608 = SOCK_MIN_SNDBUF lower bound (2304×2), matching socket(7) semantics; \"≥ 2×\" is not equality, so it permits the lower bound. If the kernel didn't double, it would fail. Honestly labeled as \"[linux]\" and asserted only on Linux.\n- (c) Label comparison: the 36 labels on macOS are a strict subset of the 37 on Linux; the only addition is the [linux] SO_SNDBUF check; the difference in the errno numeric value in the label reflects the platform constant. No weakening or skipping of items on Linux. §8.3 compliance: items 1, 2, 4, 5 are naturally fully satisfied on both platforms (item 2: bisection measures the max 9216/65507, EMSGSIZE 40/90 is asserted, oversize never returns a prefix, MSG_TRUNC is unused and documented, N=1200 and 8192 are both < max). Item 3: natural send-side would-block is not observed on either platform (histograms are all :sent, RECORD only); the assertion relies on injection labeled as [injected], but §8.3:954-956 explicitly permits this provided there is separate labeling and there is an actual successful syscall after injection — satisfied (\"[natural] real sendto/recvfrom succeed after injection\", plus natural receive-side EAGAIN is also asserted). Short sends are injection-only, with reasoning labeled (all-or-nothing cannot naturally produce a short count). This is the only item where evidence relies on injection; it is spec-compliant but worth noting on the record.\n- (d) The report does not overstate claims: written before the shiva run, with Linux expected values explicitly marked UNTESTED, prediction is 37/3 — shiva's log shows exactly 37/37/3 × 3 identical runs, exit 0. The J0a prerequisite on shiva is proven (bootstrap log: pins verified, threaded chez, cmake 4.4.4; smoke SUMMARY ok). The claim of byte-identity of probes depends on the orchestrator's sha256.\n- (e) run.sh: POSIX sh; on Linux only POSIX utilities (/proc, /sys, sed on /etc/os-release, uname, tr, wc, git); macOS-only commands (sw_vers, sysctl, ifconfig) are strictly inside the Darwin case branch. Reproducibility headers: jolt SHA + dirty count, chez path + version, uname, OS release, platform sysctls, lo MTU. Fine point: the sourcing of jolt-env.sh and the JOLT default are CWD-relative (must be run from the repo root; stated in the header; the probe path itself is $0-relative). INFO.\n\nVerdict: SIGNED OFF. Findings table: roughly 2 info rows.\n\nUnverifiable: byte-identity of probes between machines (trusting the orchestrator's sha256); full label diffs of shiva-2/3 against shiva-1 (only header + SUMMARY grepped, though counts/headers are identical); label diff of run-6 and run-7; jolt internals (epoll backend behavior beyond logged traces); Linux header values verified from my own knowledge, not from shiva's headers.\n\nWord count: keep it concise.\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-20 09:10:22 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-20 16:10:22 +07\nCoding-Agent: cmd\nSession-ID: 61966f9d-4875-4b42-9545-b0dc8a2c9891\n# Review: J0b platform-aware probe + Linux x86_64 evidence\nRole: Reviewer (read-only) | Model: qwen/qwen3.8-max\n\n## Verdict: SIGNED OFF\n\n## Findings\n\n| id | sev | file:line | evidence | correction |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | info | build/jolt-spike/j0b/run.sh:12-24 | `JOLT` default and the `jolt-env.sh` source are CWD-relative (probe path is `$0`-relative); must run from the repo root. Header says so; run-11 exercised the J0a layout. | None required; optionally resolve both from `$dir`. |\n| F2 | info (record) | udp_probe.clj:249-255, run-7.log/shiva-1.log RECORD lines | Natural send-side would-block never observed on either platform (histogram `{:sent 20000}` both); the `:would-block` send path and short-send rest on `[injected]` seams. §8.3:954-956 explicitly permits this when loopback cannot induce it, labelled separately, with real successful syscalls also exercised - all three conditions met (\"[natural] real sendto/recvfrom succeed after injection\"; natural receive-side EAGAIN asserted, errno 35/11). | Keep the RECORD in the J0b gate record; a real full-send-buffer induction remains unobserved on both platforms. |\n\n## Checks\n\n- (a) Constants all correct: Linux EAGAIN=EWOULDBLOCK 11, EMSGSIZE 90, ENOBUFS 105, EBADF 9, SO_SNDBUF 7, SO_RCVBUF 8, MSG_TRUNC 0x20, SOCK_DGRAM 2, IPPROTO_UDP 17; macOS 35/40/55/9, 0x1001/0x1002, 0x10, 2, 17. One table per platform via `native/os` (udp_probe.clj:21-29); any other platform throws at load. No cross-contamination: labels, injection errnos and classification all flow from `consts` (shiva log shows errno 11/105 labels, macOS 35/55).\n- (b) The `[linux]` check (udp_probe.clj:265-269) is not a tautology: it requires both setsockopt rc 0 and real read-backs ≥ 2× request. Observed 4608/18432: 4608 is the SOCK_MIN_SNDBUF floor (above 2×2048=4096), 18432 exactly 2×9216 - matching socket(7) doubling/clamp/floor semantics; a non-doubling kernel would read 2048 and fail. `>=` (never equality) is the right tolerance for the floor; honestly labelled and Linux-only, keeping macOS at 36/3.\n- (c) macOS 36 labels are an exact subset of Linux's 37 (only the `[linux]` check added); errno numerals in labels track platform constants. Nothing weakened or skipped on Linux: items 1, 2, 4, 5 fully natural on both (bisection measured 9216 vs 65507, EMSGSIZE 40/90 asserted with nothing delivered, oversize never yields a prefix and is consumed whole, MSG_TRUNC declared-unused per the N+1 sentinel, N=1200/8192 below both maxima, fiber park/wake/cancel/close/EBADF/poller-empty on epoll, cleanup counts). Item 3 is the injection-dependent one - see F2.\n- (d) Report claims match the logs: it was written pre-shiva with Linux expectations flagged UNTESTED and predicted 37/3; shiva-1..3 each show exactly `37 assertions: 37 pass, 0 fail; 3 records`, exit 0, identical headers (jolt 96d7b866 dirty=0, Chez 10.4.1 threaded, Ubuntu 24.04.5). J0a precondition on shiva evidenced (bootstrap: pins verified, cmake 4.4.4 linux-x86_64; smoke `SUMMARY ok`). Item 5 records complete: SHAs, arch, sysctls/proc values, MTU, lengths/counts, error traces, wakeup traces, cleanup.\n- (e) run.sh is POSIX sh; macOS-only commands (`sw_vers`, `sysctl`, `ifconfig`) sit strictly in the Darwin case arm; the Linux arm reads `/proc/sys`, `/sys/class/net/lo/mtu`, `/etc/os-release` with missing-file tolerance. Proven by execution: dash on macOS and three real Ubuntu runs.\n\n## Could not verify\n\n- Probe byte-identity local↔shiva (orchestrator's sha256, trusted); shiva-2/3 full label diffs (headers/summaries grepped, identical).\n- Linux constant values against shiva's actual headers (matched against my knowledge of asm-generic/x86_64 values, not read from the machine).\n- jolt epoll-poller internals beyond the logged traces; the run-6↔run-7 label diff claim."}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1792487631135,"messageId":"1b236c43-2611-49b5-acf9-967069ab4348"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-20 09:56:10 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-20 16:56:10 +07\nCoding-Agent: cmd\nSession-ID: 61966f9d-4875-4b42-9545-b0dc8a2c9891\n# Task: review two small branches: apt prerequisites (jolt-j0a) and the tracked J0b probe (jolt-j0b)\nRole: Reviewer (read-only)\nImplementers:\n- Model: qwen/qwen3.8-max | Assigned: 2026-10-20 16:56:10 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: owner routing \"cmd for review\"; author claude-opus-5-5; resume the reviewer\n\nREAD-ONLY review of two uncommitted changes.\n(1) /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a (branch jolt-j0a, HEAD 9f1f9144): modified jolt-toolchain.edn (:os-packages) and src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj; plus design-doc amendments in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md (sections 6.1, 6.3, 13.1, change note). Author report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0a-os-packages.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md. Owner decision (verbatim): \"actually, i change my mind. lets assume debian distribution and apt get for dependency management of package\".\n(2) /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0b (branch jolt-j0b, HEAD 9f1f9144): new src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.clj and src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh, modified bb.edn (task probe:jolt-udp). Author report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0b-commit-prep.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md. The probe logic is claimed byte-identical to the already-reviewed scratch probe /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/build/jolt-spike/j0b/udp_probe.clj (diff it yourself).\nEvidence the orchestrator produced: (1) macOS: warm bootstrap exit 0 (\"not a Debian-family host; package check skipped\"), negative case with JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DEBIAN_INSTALLED=gcc,make,git exits 1 with \"sudo apt-get install -y libncurses-dev\", smoke exit 0; on shiva (Ubuntu 24.04.5) with the two changed files copied into the scratch clone: the REAL Debian path (no seam) passes, \"all 4 required Debian packages installed: gcc git libncurses-dev make\", and the seam negative case prints the exact command. (2) macOS: bb probe:jolt-udp exit 0, 36 assertions pass, 0 fail, 3 records.\nKNOWN FINDING from the orchestrator to confirm in your review: the :unverified entry \"libssl3\" is wrong for Ubuntu 24.04: libcrypto.so.3 there is owned by libssl3t64 (dpkg -S verified on shiva) and libssl3 shows \"deinstall ok config-files\". Say how the declaration should name per-release packages or whether to check for the library instead.\nCheck (1): is the Debian detection (/etc/os-release ID / ID_LIKE) right; does the check run BEFORE any mise/Chez step; can it run sudo/apt (it must not); can the test seam leak into production behaviour (an env var that silently skips the check is a risk: assess); are the declared :required packages justified by evidence; does the design-doc amendment match the owner's words and remove or contradict anything; (2): probe logic unchanged, bb task wiring, no logs/artifacts tracked, the leftover fallback to the old spike path in the script (keep or drop?), anything that breaks running from a clean checkout. Under 500 words, final response only, header fields, a verdict per branch (SIGNED OFF / SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES / NOT SIGNED OFF), findings table (id, severity, file:line, evidence, correction), and what you could not verify."}],"meta":{"source":"user","createdAt":1792490172739,"messageId":"239105d7-4caa-461c-bcae-29657ad5df87"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Lots to read. Plan:\n\nBranch 1 (jolt-j0a worktree):\n- Read jolt-toolchain.edn (:os-packages) and jolt_bootstrap.clj (changed parts)\n- Author report collab/1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0a-os-packages...\n- Design doc revisions §6.1, §6.3, §13.1, change notes — grep for the relevant sections.\n\nBranch 2 (jolt-j0b worktree):\n- src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.clj — diff against build/jolt-spike/j0b/udp_probe.clj. Can't run diff (no shell). Read both and compare... each is 355 lines. Maybe grep can be used cleverly? Better yet: read the new file and compare with what I read before (the full text is in context). Reading 355 lines is no problem.\n- src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh\n- The probe task in bb.edn\n- Author report ...j0b-commit-prep...\n\nFirst, I'll read both author reports and the changed files in the j0a worktree in parallel.\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll read both author reports and the j0a changes first.\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_2748a982032b4b65b58bc58c","name":"read_file","input":{"paths":["/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0a-os-packages.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0b-commit-prep.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md"]}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_c1c6c2eb0f8941359b98e93a","name":"read_file","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj"}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1792490199430,"messageId":"56bb10ca-3c9b-4927-abb4-3c777aae9ce2"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_2748a982032b4b65b58bc58c","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 2/2 files\n--- File Contents ---\n\n// File: collab/1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0a-os-packages.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md (markdown)\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-20 09:49:25 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-20 16:49:25 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude\nSession-ID: 8f45af4f-0557-4cfa-a375-78525ee6a40e\n# Findings: J0a - declare and check the Debian apt prerequisites\nRole: Stream & Network Engineer\nImplementers:\n- Model: claude-opus-5-5 | Assigned: 2026-10-20 16:49:25 +07 | Status: done (macOS arm64; the Debian path is shown only through the test seam) | Rationale: owner routing \"opus-5.5 for implementation, cmd for review\"; owner \"yes to 1, 2, 3 and 4 as recommended\"\n\n- Worktree: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a`, branch `jolt-j0a` at HEAD `9f1f9144`. Changes are uncommitted and nothing is staged.\n- Logs: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/j0a-logs/ospkg-*.log`.\n\n## Item -> change\n\n| item | change |\n|---|---|\n| (1) declaration | `jolt-toolchain.edn` gains `:os-packages`. `:debian :required` maps each apt package to the step that needs it; `:debian :unverified` lists candidates that are not checked; `:macos {:manager :homebrew :enforced false}`. Details below. Chez and CMake stay mise-provided. |\n| (2) bootstrap check | `src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj`: `check-os-packages` is now the **first** step of `-main`, before `check-chez`/`check-cmake`. Those call `mise exec <tool>@<pin>`, which can trigger a mise install/build, so the package check runs before anything mise does. Details below. |\n| (2) test seam | `JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DEBIAN_INSTALLED=pkg,pkg,…` forces the Debian path and treats exactly those packages as installed (no `dpkg-query`). It prints `[test seam]`. |\n| (3) negative/positive logs | Recorded below; warm `bb bootstrap:jolt` and `bb smoke:jolt` both exit 0 on this Mac. |\n| (4) design doc | `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md`, edited in place with nothing removed. Details below. |\n\n**(1) The declaration in `jolt-toolchain.edn`:**\n\n`:required`. Each entry carries a comment on the evidence:\n\n| package | step | evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| `libncurses-dev` | mise Chez source build (link) | **verified on shiva** (\"cannot find -lncurses\" until installed; orchestrator-log J0b-on-shiva entry) |\n| `gcc`, `make` | the same Chez source build compiles and links C | the failing step was its link. They were present on shiva, so they are not independently shown missing |\n| `git` | `bootstrap:jolt` clone and verification | the code |\n\n`:unverified` (not checked):\n\n| package | step | why unverified |\n|---|---|---|\n| `g++`, `unzip` | J0c's `bb build:jolt-native` (on `jolt-j0c`) | shown on macOS only, not on Debian |\n| `libssl3` | §6.3 libcrypto (J1) | package name per release |\n\nI did not declare `curl`: no step in J0a or J0c uses it (jolt's deps resolve without curl, and J0c fetches through the babashka HTTP client).\n\n**(2) What the bootstrap check does:**\n- **Debian detection:** `/etc/os-release` `ID` or `ID_LIKE` contains the word `debian`.\n- **Check:** each `:required` package goes through `dpkg-query -W -f=${Status}`, which must answer `install ok installed`.\n- **On failure:** `missing Debian packages: <names>`, the step for each, and `install them with: sudo apt-get install -y <names>`, then exit 1.\n- **It never runs sudo or apt.**\n- **Other hosts:** one line, `os-packages: not a Debian-family host; package check skipped`.\n\n**(4) The design-doc edits:**\n1. A dated \"Change note 2026-10-20, fourth\" after the third note, quoting both owner sentences.\n2. **§6.1:** a new paragraph on host OS packages (Debian family + apt, `:os-packages` declared, checked by bootstrap before mise, never runs sudo/apt, macOS Homebrew assumed and unenforced, Chez/CMake still mise), plus a bullet in the \"`jolt-toolchain.edn` records\" list.\n3. **§6.3:** the Linux bullet now says `libcrypto.so.3` is installed with apt on the Debian family and declared in `:os-packages`, and that the path/version check is retained (an apt upgrade that moves or changes it fails until requalified).\n4. **§13.1:** a new row \"Linux packages (2026-10-20)\" with the owner's words and the recorded meaning. Every grid row is still 169 characters wide.\n\n## Evidence (commands run in the worktree, foreground)\n\n| command | exit | log | what it shows |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DEBIAN_INSTALLED=git,gcc,make bb bootstrap:jolt` | **1** | `ospkg-neg-missing.log` | `missing Debian packages: libncurses-dev` … `sudo apt-get install -y libncurses-dev`. The Chez/mise line never prints, so the failure is before mise. |\n| `JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DEBIAN_INSTALLED=git,make bb bootstrap:jolt` | **1** | `ospkg-neg-missing2.log` | Two missing packages, one command: `sudo apt-get install -y gcc libncurses-dev` |\n| `JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DEBIAN_INSTALLED=git,gcc,make,libncurses-dev bb bootstrap:jolt` | **0** | `ospkg-pos-all.log` | `os-packages: all 4 required Debian packages installed: gcc git libncurses-dev make`, then the normal bootstrap (Chez 10.4.1, CMake 4.4.4, jolt 96d7b866 + 7 submodules, smoke 3) |\n| `bb bootstrap:jolt` (warm, real macOS path) | **0** | `ospkg-warm-macos.log` | `os-packages: not a Debian-family host; package check skipped`, then the normal bootstrap |\n| `bb smoke:jolt` | **0** | `ospkg-smoke.log` | `SUMMARY ok` |\n| `bb /tmp/osrel_test.clj` (the same `/etc/os-release` parse expressions over sample texts) | 0 | `ospkg-osrelease-parse.log` | Ubuntu 24.04 (`ID=ubuntu`, `ID_LIKE=debian`) true; Debian 12 true; Mint (`ID_LIKE=\"ubuntu debian\"`) true; Fedora false |\n| `mise exec -- cljstyle check src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj jolt-toolchain.edn` | 0 | n/a | clean |\n\n## NOT done or NOT verified\n- **The real Debian path was not run.** The actual `/etc/os-release` read and `dpkg-query` calls on a Debian host, and the exact `dpkg-query` status string on Ubuntu 24.04, are untested by me; the orchestrator's shiva run covers them. I checked the parsing logic only against sample texts, through a copy of the expressions rather than the function itself, which reads the fixed path.\n- `gcc`, `make` and `git` are declared from the steps that use them. None was shown missing on a clean Debian host.\n- `:unverified` packages are not checked by design, and the libcrypto apt package name and version check is J1 work.\n- I did not decide whether to check `build-essential` instead of `gcc`/`make` (`build-essential` would add `g++`, `dpkg-dev` and others not shown to be needed).\n- **macOS:** nothing is enforced, as decided; Homebrew `openssl@3` stays §6.3's later gate.\n\n## Files changed\n- `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/jolt-toolchain.edn`\n- `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj`\n- `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md` (untracked in the main tree; edited in place)\n- New untracked logs: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/j0a-logs/ospkg-*.log`\n\nReport: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0a-os-packages.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md`\n\n\n// File: collab/1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0b-commit-prep.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md (markdown)\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-20 09:52 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-20 16:52 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude\nModel: claude-opus-5-5\nRole: Stream & Network Engineer\nTask: J0b: move the UDP probe into a tracked branch (jolt-j0b)\nPrompt: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0b-commit-prep.claude-opus-5-5.prompt.md\nWorktree: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0b (branch jolt-j0b from jolt-j0a 9f1f9144)\nStatus: done (nothing staged, committed or pushed)\n\n# Result\n\nThe probe is now in the worktree as three working-tree changes (none staged):\n\n- `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0b/src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.clj` (new; copy of `build/jolt-spike/j0b/udp_probe.clj`)\n- `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0b/src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh` (new, mode 755; copy of `build/jolt-spike/j0b/run.sh`)\n- `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0b/bb.edn` (+5 lines: the `probe:jolt-udp` task)\n\nThe `bb probe:jolt-udp` task runs `sh src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh` and exits with that script's exit code, the same way `smoke:jolt` does. The script prints the same header run.sh printed (jolt, jolt-sha, chez, uname, sysctl, lo0/lo mtu). It then runs the probe with the J0a layout: `build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt` and `JOLT_CHEZ` from `build/tools/jolt-env.sh`.\n\nI did not edit the scratch directory or copy any logs into git. The run logs are in /tmp only.\n\n# Dif