build/jolt-spike/jolt/bin/jolt`) and the mise Chez path unchanged, to keep the change minimal. In the tracked tree the J0a layout is always present after `bb bootstrap:jolt`, so the fallback is dead but harmless. A reviewer may ask for it to be removed.\n- I did not run kondo on the new `.clj`. It requires jolt-only namespaces (`jolt.ffi`, `jolt.socket.native`, ...), so kondo would only report unresolved namespaces, the same as for `jolt_smoke.clj`.\n- `git status`: ` M bb.edn`, `?? src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.clj`, `?? src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh`. `build/` is ignored.\n\nReport: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0b-commit-prep.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md\n\n"}]},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_c1c6c2eb0f8941359b98e93a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 193 lines\n1: (ns jolt-bootstrap\n2:   \"bb bootstrap:jolt — materialize the jolt toolchain declared in\n3:    jolt-toolchain.edn (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §4.3, §6.1).\n4: \n5:    * Chez and CMake come from mise at the exact pinned versions; this task\n6:      checks them and never installs or upgrades them (`mise install` does).\n7:    * jolt is cloned from the declared origin into build/tools/jolt and checked\n8:      out at the declared full SHA with its recursive submodules. An existing\n9:      checkout is verified, never pulled: a HEAD, submodule or dirty-tree\n10:      mismatch fails the task. Advancing the pin is the upgrade gate's job.\n11:    * build/tools/jolt-env.sh is written with JOLT_CHEZ set explicitly, so jolt\n12:      never searches PATH for a Chez.\n13:    * First of all, on a Debian-family host, the :os-packages :debian\n14:      :required packages are checked with dpkg-query; a missing one fails the\n15:      task before mise is asked for anything, naming the exact\n16:      `sudo apt-get install -y ...` command. Nothing here runs sudo or apt.\n17:      Test seam: JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DEBIAN_INSTALLED=pkg,pkg,... treats the\n18:      host as Debian and those packages as the installed set (no dpkg-query).\n19: \n20:    Exit status is nonzero on any mismatch.\"\n21:   (:require [babashka.fs :as fs]\n22:             [babashka.process :as p]\n23:             [clojure.edn :as edn]\n24:             [clojure.string :as str]))\n25: \n26: \n27: (defn- fail!\n28:   [& msg]\n29:   (binding [*out* *err*]\n30:     (println \"bootstrap:jolt FAILED:\" (apply str msg)))\n31:   (System/exit 1))\n32: \n33: \n34: (defn- sh\n35:   \"Run a command, answer trimmed stdout; fail the task on a nonzero exit.\"\n36:   [& args]\n37:   (let [opts (if (map? (first args)) (first args) {})\n38:         cmd (if (map? (first args)) (rest args) args)\n39:         r (apply p/shell (merge {:out :string :err :string :continue true} opts) cmd)]\n40:     (when-not (zero? (:exit r))\n41:       (fail! (str/join \" \" cmd) \" exited \" (:exit r) \"\\n\" (:err r)))\n42:     (str/trim (:out r))))\n43: \n44: \n45: (defn- mise-bin\n46:   \"The path of executable `exe` from mise tool `tool` at exactly `version`\n47:    (mise's own resolution: the layout differs per platform).\"\n48:   [tool version exe]\n49:   (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true}\n50:                    \"mise\" \"exec\" (str tool \"@\" version) \"--\" \"which\" exe)]\n51:     (when-not (zero? (:exit r))\n52:       (fail! \"mise has no \" tool \"@\" version \" installed; run `mise install \" tool \"`\"))\n53:     (str/trim (:out r))))\n54: \n55: \n56: (defn- check-chez\n57:   [{:keys [version binary threaded]}]\n58:   (let [scheme (mise-bin \"chezscheme\" version (str (fs/file-name binary)))\n59:         v (sh scheme \"--version\")\n60:         t (sh {:in \"(display (threaded?))\"} scheme \"-q\")]\n61:     (when-not (= version v) (fail! \"Chez at \" scheme \" reports \" v \", pinned \" version))\n62:     (when (and threaded (not= \"#t\" t)) (fail! \"Chez at \" scheme \" is not threaded\"))\n63:     (println \"chez\" v \"threaded\" t scheme)\n64:     scheme))\n65: \n66: \n67: (defn- check-cmake\n68:   [{:keys [version]}]\n69:   (let [cmake (mise-bin \"cmake\" version \"cmake\")\n70:         v (first (str/split-lines (sh cmake \"--version\")))]\n71:     (when-not (= (str \"cmake version \" version) v)\n72:       (fail! \"CMake at \" cmake \" reports \" v \", pinned \" version))\n73:     (println v cmake)\n74:     cmake))\n75: \n76: \n77: (defn- submodule-shas\n78:   [dir]\n79:   ;; Not through `sh`: its trim would eat the status column of the first line\n80:   ;; (\" \" checked out at the recorded commit, \"-\" uninitialized, \"+\" differs).\n81:   (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true}\n82:                    \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"submodule\" \"status\" \"--recursive\")]\n83:     (when-not (zero? (:exit r)) (fail! \"git submodule status: \" (:err r)))\n84:     (into {}\n85:           (map (fn [line]\n86:                  (let [[sha path] (str/split (str/trim (subs line 1)) #\"\\s+\")]\n87:                    (when (not= \\space (first line))\n88:                      (fail! \"submodule \" path \" is not checked out at its recorded commit: \" line))\n89:                    [path sha])))\n90:           (remove str/blank? (str/split-lines (:out r))))))\n91: \n92: \n93: (defn- materialize!\n94:   [{:keys [origin sha dir]}]\n95:   (when-not (fs/exists? dir)\n96:     (fs/create-dirs (fs/parent dir))\n97:     (println \"cloning\" origin \"into\" dir)\n98:     (sh \"git\" \"clone\" \"--no-checkout\" origin dir)\n99:     (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"checkout\" \"--detach\" sha)\n100:     (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"submodule\" \"update\" \"--init\" \"--recursive\")))\n101: \n102: \n103: (defn- verify!\n104:   [{:keys [origin sha dir submodules patches]}]\n105:   (let [head (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"rev-parse\" \"HEAD\")\n106:         remote (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"remote\" \"get-url\" \"origin\")]\n107:     (when-not (= origin remote)\n108:       (fail! dir \" has origin \" remote \", declared \" origin))\n109:     (when-not (= sha head)\n110:       (fail! dir \" is at \" head \", declared \" sha\n111:              \"; ordinary runs never pull — advance the pin through qualify:jolt-upgrade\"))\n112:     (when (seq patches)\n113:       (fail! \"patches are declared but this task does not apply them yet\"))\n114:     ;; Known gap (input to the §6.4 gate hardening): `status --porcelain`\n115:     ;; does not see changes to gitignored files inside the clone.\n116:     (let [dirty (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"status\" \"--porcelain\")]\n117:       (when-not (str/blank? dirty) (fail! dir \" has local changes:\\n\" dirty)))\n118:     (let [actual (submodule-shas dir)]\n119:       (when-not (= submodules actual)\n120:         (fail! \"submodule SHAs differ from jolt-toolchain.edn: \" (pr-str actual))))\n121:     (println \"jolt\" head \"with\" (count submodules) \"submodules verified\")))\n122: \n123: \n124: (defn- debian-family?\n125:   \"/etc/os-release names debian as its ID or in ID_LIKE.\"\n126:   []\n127:   (let [f \"/etc/os-release\"]\n128:     (when (fs/exists? f)\n129:       (let [kv (into {}\n130:                      (keep (fn [line]\n131:                              (when-let [[_ k v] (re-matches #\"([A-Z_]+)=\\\"?([^\\\"]*)\\\"?\" line)]\n132:                                [k v])))\n133:                      (str/split-lines (slurp f)))\n134:             words (set (str/split (str (get kv \"ID\") \" \" (get kv \"ID_LIKE\")) #\"\\s+\"))]\n135:         (contains? words \"debian\")))))\n136: \n137: \n138: (defn- dpkg-installed?\n139:   [pkg]\n140:   (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true}\n141:                    \"dpkg-query\" \"-W\" \"-f=${Status}\" pkg)]\n142:     (and (zero? (:exit r)) (= \"install ok installed\" (str/trim (:out r))))))\n143: \n144: \n145: (defn- check-os-packages\n146:   \"Fail, before any mise build, when a declared Debian package is missing.\"\n147:   [{:keys [debian]}]\n148:   (let [seam (System/getenv \"JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DEBIAN_INSTALLED\")\n149:         required (sort (keys (:required debian)))\n150:         installed? (cond\n151:                      seam (let [pkgs (set (remove str/blank? (str/split seam #\",\")))]\n152:                             (println \"os-packages: [test seam] Debian path forced; installed =\"\n153:                                      (str/join \" \" (sort pkgs)))\n154:                             pkgs)\n155:                      (debian-family?) dpkg-installed?\n156:                      :else nil)]\n157:     (if-not installed?\n158:       (println \"os-packages: not a Debian-family host; package check skipped\")\n159:       (let [missing (remove installed? required)]\n160:         (when (seq missing)\n161:           (fail! \"missing Debian packages: \" (str/join \" \" missing)\n162:                  \"\\n  needed by: \"\n163:                  (str/join \"; \" (map #(str % \" (\" (get-in debian [:required %]) \")\") missing))\n164:                  \"\\n  install them with:\\n    sudo apt-get install -y \" (str/join \" \" missing)))\n165:         (println \"os-packages: all\" (count required) \"required Debian packages installed:\"\n166:                  (str/join \" \" required))))))\n167: \n168: \n169: (defn -main\n170:   [& _]\n171:   (let [{:keys [jolt chez cmake os-packages]} (edn/read-string (slurp \"jolt-toolchain.edn\"))\n172:         _ (check-os-packages os-packages)\n173:         scheme (check-chez chez)\n174:         _ (check-cmake cmake)\n175:         dir (str (fs/absolutize (:dir jolt)))\n176:         jolt (assoc jolt :dir dir)\n177:         env-file (str (fs/path (fs/parent dir) \"jolt-env.sh\"))]\n178:     (materialize! jolt)\n179:     (verify! jolt)\n180:     (spit env-file\n181:           (str \"# written by bb bootstrap:jolt from jolt-toolchain.edn; do not edit\\n\"\n182:                \"export JOLT_CHEZ='\" scheme \"'\\n\"\n183:                \"export JOLT_HOME='\" dir \"'\\n\"))\n184:     (println \"wrote\" env-file)\n185:     (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true\n186:                       :extra-env {\"JOLT_CHEZ\" scheme}}\n187:                      (str (fs/path dir \"bin\" \"jolt\")) \"-e\" \"(+ 1 2)\")]\n188:       (when-not (= \"3\" (str/trim (:out r)))\n189:         (fail! \"jolt smoke (+ 1 2) answered \" (pr-str (:out r)) \" \" (:err r)))\n190:       (println \"jolt smoke (+ 1 2) => 3\"))))\n191: \n192: \n193: (apply -main *command-line-args*)"}]}],"meta":{"source":"tool","messageId":"38dab9e6-6637-4d01-b5cd-d3b11be9ffeb"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Next, read jolt-toolchain.edn :os-packages, the design doc revision sections (6.1, 6.3, 13.1, change notes), and the j0b worktree files (diff of jolt_udp_probe.clj — I need to verify the claim that they're byte-identical; can't run diff, but I have the scratch probe from an earlier read in context, so I'll read the tracked one and compare; jolt_udp_probe.sh vs run.sh; bb.edn task).\n\nAssessment of bootstrap code:\n- check-os-packages runs first in -main ✓ before check-chez ✓.\n- No sudo/apt: the strings only appear inside fail! messages ✓. dpkg-query is read-only ✓.\n- Seam risk: the JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DEBIAN_INSTALLED env var, if set in the environment, will force the Debian path even in production — it can't silently skip checks on an actual Debian host… wait: if seam is set to a list containing all required pkgs, checks will pass on any host without dpkg — that could silently let a truly missing package through if the env var leaks into CI. It prints \"[test seam]\" so it's visible in logs, not silent. Risk: env var lingering in a shell/CI. Mitigation: the visible label + fail-closed default (when unset → real path). Assessment: low; could also gate with a bb task flag instead of env var, or require seam value to equal \"enabled\"… acceptable given the disclosure; recommend either renaming it to be clearly test-only (already is) or restricting to non-CI. Also note: seam can't cause a false-pass silently — every use prints. OK.\n- debian-family? regex: `([A-Z_]+)=\\\"?([^\\\"]*)\\\"?` — for `ID_LIKE=debian` (unquoted), `[^\\\"]*` captures \"debian\". For quoted `ID_LIKE=\"ubuntu debian\"`, captures ubuntu debian. Words are split on whitespace. Edge case: unquoted values with trailing comment? os-release doesn't have comments on a line. `ID=ubuntu` ✓. What if a line is like `PRETTY_NAME=\"Debian GNU/Linux 12\"`? — words would include… wait, only ID and ID_LIKE are looked up, other keys ignored. But note: if PRETTY_NAME contains the word \"debian\" — it's not referenced. Good. One subtle bug: regex `([A-Z_]+)=\\\"?([^\\\"]*)\\\"?` — greedy `[A-Z_]+` is fine. OK.\n- dpkg-installed?: `dpkg-query -W -f=${Status}` — exit 0 with \"install ok installed\". The libssl3 case: \"deinstall ok config-files\" → not considered installed → correct strictness. For a truly missing package, dpkg-query exits 1 → false ✓.\n- Required packages justified: libncurses-dev verified on shiva (evidence of missing); gcc/make inferred from link failure (were present, but Chez source build requires them — reasonable, disclosed); git needed by code. OK.\n\nNow known finding: :unverified \"libssl3\" is wrong for Ubuntu 24.04 (t64 transition → libssl3t64). Recommendation: don't hard-code per-release package names; instead, at usage time (J1 §6.3 libcrypto gate), check the library's presence itself (e.g. ldconfig -p / dlopen path + version check), and only keep package names as per-release documentation, or map them via `dpkg -S` at runtime. Or declare per-release: {:debian {:release {\"ubuntu/noble\" \"libssl3t64\" :default \"libssl3\"}}}. My recommendation: since §6.3 already retains a path/version check for libcrypto, declare the requirement as a library (soname libcrypto.so.3) not a package, and let the apt hint resolve the provider at failure time via `dpkg -S` / apt-file. Simplest: rename the unverified entry to soname + a note.\n\nNext to read: toolchain's os-packages block, design doc sections, j0b files. Grep for change notes and 13.1 lines in the design doc.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now the toolchain declaration, design-doc amendments, and the j0b tracked files.\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_eb81a533f1b24c34949f4628","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"os-packages|debian|apt|Change note 2026-10-20, fourth|Linux packages","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/jolt-toolchain.edn","output_mode":"content","-n":true,"-C":6}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_fd4df8fbaf054aa089ab0327","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fourth|os-packages|apt-get|Debian|libssl3t64|Linux packages","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md","output_mode":"content","-n":true,"-C":4}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1792490240291,"messageId":"d933b5c2-aa0a-4fe9-8b63-6411553cb1a8"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_eb81a533f1b24c34949f4628","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/jolt-toolchain.edn-23-               \"vendor/irregex\" \"c948a704fc732914a243c1643bfe359913d11c7b\"\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/jolt-toolchain.edn-24-               \"vendor/process\" \"43bdd65e189f2ccacc56662c53a21f5470ff1500\"\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/jolt-toolchain.edn-25-               \"vendor/sci\" \"32d62a5136ad3dc148588752f5bcc4cc30b14752\"}\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/jolt-toolchain.edn-26-  ;; proposed default 2 (§13.2): none recorded, so none applied\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/jolt-toolchain.edn-27-  :patches []}\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/jolt-toolchain.edn-28-\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/jolt-toolchain.edn:29: ;; Host OS packages (owner 2026-10-20: Linux = the Debian family with apt).\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/jolt-toolchain.edn-30- ;; `bb bootstrap:jolt` checks :required with dpkg-