def LIBX11` (1189); `s_ee_get_clipboard` (1196) uses XConvertSelection/XGetWindowProperty etc. — the X11 clipboard claim is corroborated by the 1189-1212 range ✓.\n- Confirmed that --disable-x11 (configure:396-397) and --disable-curses (:399-400, help :684-685) are configure options ✓. The comment says \"the mise plugin doesn't pass them\" — indirectly backed up by the fact that the build defines LIBX11 and fails (if the option were passed, there'd be no X11 include). I couldn't read the mise plugin itself — a minor unverifiable item, but the failure itself proves the flag wasn't passed.\n\n(b) libx11-dev is the correct Debian/Ubuntu package that provides X11/Xlib.h ✓. Grepped the entire jupiter log for fatal error/cannot find/undefined reference: exactly 1 hit — only X11, nothing else missing ✓. Also, the link line shows -lncurses (already declared), -lrt -ldl -lm -lpthread (glibc built-in).\n\n(c) Conventions: comment style matches (basis + location, same as the libncurses-dev entry); placed between libncurses-dev and gcc within :required; the libssl3 note in :unverified remains fixed as before; the value string \"mise Chez source build (compile, X11 clipboard in the editor)\" is consistent with others.\n\n(d) Single-entry change: the current file shows exactly a 7-line block (6 lines of comment :43-48 + entry :49); can't run git show (shell was refused), but COMMIT_EDITMSG matches, and the file's diff against the previously reviewed state is only that block. Everything else is identical to the signed-off version.\n\n(e) Commit message: honest — states the expeditor X11 clipboard include, the jupiter failure, that shiva never failed, and the bootstrap check behavior. Subject-line convention `fix(jolt):` matches the repo's style (feat(dao.stream)... etc.).\n\nMinor notes: one small nitpick — the comment says \"Chez's expression editor (c/expeditor.c:1189-1212) reads the X11 clipboard\" — but strictly the code also does dlopen-based dynamic loading (pXOpenDisplay via handle), the include is guarded by LIBX11, and at runtime it's optional via dlopen. So build-time header requirement, runtime is optional. The declaration is still correct (the build needs the header). Not a finding worth tabulating? Could be info: the comment's \"reads the X11 clipboard\" is accurate. No issue.\n\nAnother consideration: --disable-x11 exists, and since jolt never uses the interactive Chez editor's clipboard, the alternative was to pass that flag via the mise plugin configuration — but the comment itself notes that the mise plugin doesn't pass it, and the owner's decision is to manage via apt. No issue; could note it as an alternative but not required.\n\nVerdict: SIGNED OFF. Findings table: no blocking factors; one info row about git show being unavailable? That goes into \"unverifiable items.\" Keep the table minimal — probably zero findings, or one info item. Under 300 words.\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-20 18:07:54 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-21 01:07:54 +07\nCoding-Agent: cmd\nSession-ID: 61966f9d-4875-4b42-9545-b0dc8a2c9891\n# Review: libx11-dev declaration (d5b4ce95, jolt-j0a)\nRole: Reviewer (read-only) | Model: qwen/qwen3.8-max\n\n## Verdict: SIGNED OFF\n\n## Findings\n\n| id | sev | file:line | evidence | correction |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| L1 | info | jolt-toolchain.edn:47-48 | The comment notes `--disable-x11`/`--disable-curses` exist but the mise plugin does not pass them - correct alternative would be build flags, since jolt never uses Chez's interactive editor. The apt route matches the owner's decision, so this is context, not a defect. | None; optionally note the flag alternative for a future mise-plugin change. |\n\n## Checks\n\n- (a) Evidence accurate. jupiter-mise-install.log:503-504 shows exactly `c/expeditor.c:1191:10: fatal error: X11/Xlib.h: No such file or directory` with `#include <X11/Xlib.h>` - the quoted line and include match. The orchestrator's tarball excerpt (collab/1792519674000