cted `#?(:clj` in a file outside list 1 and on one     |\n698: |       |        | **list 1** (files permitted non-exempt host arms, §8.1) and **list 2**         | injected `(random-uuid)` outside list 2 (two negative tests), and |\n699: |       |        | (resolved effect calls permitted: the §3.2 sites, plus the callers of M        | fails distinctly when it reads zero files (scan failure is not    |\n700: |       |        | entries named in §2.4), exempting §3.3 patterns; the gate scans files          | zero matches). Counts recorded.                                   |\n701: |       |        | recursively and fails if it read none; (c) per-lane counts; (d) the corpus     |                                                                   |\n702: |       |        | hash set.                                                                      |                                                                   |\n703: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n704: | H1    | expand | Create `dao.host.integer`, `.float`, `.number`, `.bytes`, `.text` with today's | Green; counts unchanged plus the named new tests; the new tests   |\n705: |       |        | arms moved verbatim where the law is today's behaviour, and **with the new     | require and call `dao.host.*` directly; corpus bytes identical;   |\n706: |       |        | laws where it is not**: `utf8-encode` refuses an unpaired surrogate (today's   | the P-entry argument-immutability property test and the M-entry   |\n707: |       |        | helpers substitute: JVM `getBytes` emits `?`, `goog.crypt` and `dart:convert`  | prevalidation test pass on three lanes; `utf8-encode` direct      |\n708: |       |        | emit U+FFFD, `jing.cljc:66,69,71,132-135`, `sign.cljc:62-66`, R for the        | refusal test and `utf8-decode` strict tests pass. List 1 grows by |\n709: |       |        | library behaviour); `utf8-decode` is extracted from the already strict         | five files.                                                       |\n710: |       |        | `cbor.cljc:1240-1271` (V). The `Float64`/`Rational`/`Decimal` deftypes move    |                                                                   |\n711: |       |        | with their protocol blocks. Tests: `dao.host.conformance-test`,                |                                                                   |\n712: |       |        | `dao.host.bytes-test`, `dao.host.text-test` (table D). Table C laws written    |                                                                   |\n713: |       |        | into the docstrings of `values.cljc` and the moved carriers. No consumer       |                                                                   |\n714: |       |        | changes, so no behaviour change is observable yet.                             |                                                                   |\n715: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n716: | H2    | migr.  | Every consumer moves: `yin/vm.cljc:32`, `yin/vm/engine.cljc:38`,               | Green; counts unchanged plus the `asort` stability, `acopy`       |\n717: |       |        | `yin/vm/values.cljc:30`, `yin/vm/data.cljc:41`, `yin/vm/integer.cljc:101`,     | overlap and `acopy`/`aset` **no-partial-write** tests; corpus     |\n718: |       |        | `test/yang/python/antlr/{int_heap,int_literal,int_ops}_test.cljc` (V);         | identical. **Pre-deletion gate**: the H0 closure tool, reading    |\n719: |       |        | `dao.jing.cbor` drops `:106-254`, `:342-460`, `:483-632` for `dao.host.*`;     | `ns` forms (not text), reports `yin.vm.integer.host` required by  |\n720: |       |        | `debruijn_code.cljc:232-242,315`, `debruijn.cljc:167,241,310-321,855-885`,     | no file in `src` or `test`; the only textual mention left is its  |\n721: |       |        | `chunks`, `jing.dht`, `linker:1232`, `sign:55-66`, `datagram:63-66` read       | own file (the docstring at `integer.cljc:14` is updated in H2).   |\n722: |       |        | `bytes`/`text`/`float`; `dao.data.arrays` gains the stable sort and            | **Post-deletion gate**: the file is absent and the tool reports   |\n723: |       |        | **prevalidation before any write** in `acopy` on JS and Dart (a behaviour      | no require of it; a tool failure is distinct from \"none found\".   |\n724: |       |        | change, §2.4); the M-entry callers of §2.4 are audited for the freeze rule.    | **Host-library gate (§8.2), built in this slice** as the library  |\n725: |       |        | Then `yin.vm.integer.host` deleted; the shim mention in `integer.cljc:14`      | mode of `dao.host.gate-test`: within the adopted closure, no      |\n726: |       |        | reworded. Deliverable: the library mode of `dao.host.gate-test` with the H2    | executable reference to `BigInteger`, `BigDecimal`,               |\n727: |       |        | name list (§8.2).                                                              | `clojure.lang.Ratio`, `java.text`, `unorm` outside `dao/host/`;   |\n728: |       |        |                                                                                | two negative tests: a fixture closure file holding an executable  |\n729: |       |        |                                                                                | `BigInteger` reference outside the allowlist fails the gate, and  |\n730: |       |        |                                                                                | a fixture file naming `BigInteger` only in a docstring and a      |\n731: |       |        |                                                                                | keyword passes. `yin.vm.engine` is touched (its require) and      |\n732: |       |        |                                                                                | pinned by the engine suites. List 1 shrinks by the migrated files |\n733: |       |        |                                                                                | (§8.1).                                                           |\n734: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n735: | H3    | expand | `dao.host.hash`, `dao.host.sign`; `dao.jing` and `yin.vm.linker.sign` require  | Green; counts unchanged plus `dao.host.hash-test`; every corpus   |\n736: |       | +migr. | them (`generate` stays, deferred). The string hash forms and `sign`'s `utf8`   | address identical; `sign_test` 4/4; `base64_test` 3/3 on three    |\n737: |       |        | switch to `text/utf8-encode`: a **named behaviour change** for strings with an | lanes; a direct test that `digest-string` and `message` refuse an |\n738: |       |        | unpaired surrogate (refusal instead of a substituted byte), recorded in the    | unpaired-surrogate string; **host-library gate (§8.2)**: within   |\n739: |       |        | slice report; such strings are already refused by the canonical codec (corpus  | the adopted closure, no executable reference to `MessageDigest`,  |\n740: |       |        | `unpaired-surrogate` class), so no persisted address changes. Base64 made      | `Blake3`, `noble`, `blake3_dart`, `package:crypto`,               |\n741: |       |        | portable (table B; a replacement).                                             | `ed25519_edwards`, `goog.crypt.base64` outside `dao/host/`, and   |\n742: |       |        |                                                                                | for the Ed25519 names outside `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`           |\n743: |       |        |                                                                                | (`generate`); scan errors reported distinctly.                    |\n744: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n745: | H4    | migr.  | Portable Jing CBOR writer over `dao.host.*`; `dao.jing.cbor.boring` and        | Green; `cbor-v1.json` byte-identical on three lanes with the      |\n746: |       |        | `dao.jing.cbor.cljd` deleted; Boring stays for `dao.stream.cbor.boring` and    | errata skips unchanged (`documented-skips-match-the-errata-and-   |\n747: |       |        | the Dart `cbor` package for `dao.stream.cbor.cljd` (OQ4). A measurement:       | leave-no-case-unrun`); fixtures, DHT and linker image goldens     |\n748: |       |        | corpus and one large module image, old writer against new, JVM and Node.       | unchanged; the measurement in the slice report, no threshold      |\n749: |       |        |                                                                                | (OQ7). Slow tier once after landing.                              |\n750: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n751: \n752: Dependencies: H0, H1, H2 in order; H3 and H4 after H2, in either order.\n753: \n754: ### 8.1 List 1: the files permitted non-exempt host arms, baseline and final\n755: \n756: The gate never promises \"no arms across `src/cljc`\", only \"no non-exempt\n757: arms outside list 1\". List 1 is generated at H0 by the gate from the actual\n758: closure (every closure file holding a non-exempt arm, §3.3) and must equal\n759: the **H0 baseline** below, by category, with each file's reason; a\n760: difference either way is an H0 finding to resolve before H1. The baseline\n761: is today's tree: the seven `dao.host.*` files are **planned additions**\n762: (five in H1, two in H3) and are not part of the H0 baseline; they are\n763: marked as such in the table.\n764: \n765: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n766: | Category (reason)          | Files (V, from §1 and the closure)                                                              | After H4                    |\n767: +============================+=================================================================================================+=============================+\n768: | H1-H4 migration sources    | `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`,                  | Removed from list 1 as each |\n769: |                            | `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (the Dart Jing writer; a lane-specific file counted here,    | slice lands; `sign.cljc`    |\n770: |                            | not under seams), `dao/jing.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn.cljc`,           | stays for `generate` only;  |\n771: |                            | `yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc` (table C blocks stay, as  | three of these files are    |\n772: |                            | exempt protocol syntax), `dao/stream/chunks.cljc`, `dao/stream/base64.cljc`,                    | deleted (§8.1 paragraph).   |\n773: |                            | `dao/jing/dht.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker.cljc`, `dao/stream/datagram.cljc` (bytes arms only).        |                             |\n774: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n775: | Profile (the arms belong   | Baseline: `dao/data/arrays.cljc`. Planned additions, not in the H0 baseline:                    | Stay; the seven additions   |\n776: | here by design)            | `dao/host/{integer,float,number,bytes,text,hash,sign}.cljc` (P; five join list 1 at H1, two at  | are on list 1 from the      |\n777: |                            | H3).                                                                                            | slice that creates them.    |\n778: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n779: | Retained runtime           | `dao/data/btree.cljc` (atomic flag `:102-119`, weak and soft references `:212-245`: substantive | Stay, with the table C      |\n780: | prerequisites (table C)    | arms, not protocol syntax, retained by design); `dao/data/btree/storage.cljc` (promise facade,  | reason recorded in the      |\n781: |                            | deferred §9.1); `dao/pretty.cljc` (`StringWriter`/pprint, display only, §3.1).                  | gate's list.                |\n782: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n783: | Codec-track files          | `dao/stream/ws.cljc`, `transit.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`, `cbor/boring.cljc`, `codec.cljc`,            | Stay; owned by that track;  |\n784: | (untouched by this track)  | `remote_channel.cljc`, `ws_project.cljc`, `jing/stream.cljc`.                                   | `codec.cljc:45` after C4.   |\n785: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n786: | Seams and driver           | `src/clj`, `src/cljs`, `src/cljd` seam and shadow files (§3.1 lane-specific list) **except**    | Stay, except the Dart Jing  |\n787: |                            | `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`, which is a Jing writer H4 deletes, not a seam; it is on the | writer, deleted in H4.      |\n788: |                            | baseline under the first row's `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc` twin. `yin/repl/main.cljc`,          |                             |\n789: |                            | `yin/repl/host.cljc`, `yin/repl/state.cljc`.                                                    |                             |\n790: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n791: | Deferred-scope files (§9)  | `dao/jing/file.cljc`, `dao/space/store/fs.cljc`, `dao/space/store.cljc`,                        | Stay until the deferred     |\n792: |                            | `dao/stream/journal/file.cljc`, `dao/jing/content/async.cljc`, `dao/jing/coordinate.cljc`,      | design lands.               |\n793: |                            | `dao/space/dht.cljc`, `yin/repl.cljc`, `yang/python/antlr/parser.cljc` and the other            |                             |\n794: |                            | `yang/python/antlr/*.cljc` with arms, `dao/stream/udp.cljc`, `dao/stream/journal.cljc`          |                             |\n795: |                            | (`locking`), `dao/space/transactor.cljc`, `dao/space/schema.cljc`, `yin/vm/ucf/authority.cljc`  |                             |\n796: |                            | (`locking`), and every remaining closure file whose arms are only `catch`/hint/protocol syntax  |                             |\n797: |                            | is **not** on list 1 (it is exempt by pattern).                                                 |                             |\n798: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n799: \n800: **Baseline versus additions and deletions.** The H0 baseline is the set of\n801: **existing** files above (every entry except the planned additions named\n802: in the profile row). The planned additions are the seven `dao/host/*.cljc`\n803: files (five in H1, two in H3), which join list 1 when their slices land. The deletions are\n804: three: `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc` (H2), `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc` (H4, the\n805: JVM/JS Boring wrapper) and `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (H4, the Dart\n806: Jing writer, a lane-specific file that the seams row excludes and the first\n807: row lists, so that the lane-specific category cannot silently retain it).\n808: The final list 1 after H4 is therefore: the baseline minus the first row\n809: (except `sign.cljc` for `generate`), both deleted Jing writers included in\n810: that subtraction, plus the seven profile files. The host-library gate of\n811: §8.2 is consistent with it.\n812: \n813: ### 8.2 The host-library gate (H2, H3): executable references within the closure\n814: \n815: A literal `grep` over `src/cljc` is **not** the gate: it matches a docstring\n816: in the untouched `dao/data.cljc:54` (\"a BigInt/BigDecimal\", V) and the\n817: out-of-scope `dao/postgraphics/lowering.cljc:587` (`:rgba8unorm`, V), so\n818: its asserted result would be false. The gate is instead `dao.host.gate-test`\n819: run in **library mode**, which **lands with H2**, not H0: H0 is a freeze\n820: with no source change and the library mode has no consumer before H2's\n821: deletion, so building it in H0 would add a deliverable nothing exercises\n822: and nothing can falsify; H2 builds it with the H2 name list and its two\n823: negative tests (below), and H3 extends the name list. In library mode the\n824: gate takes the H0 closure tool's tagged file list\n825: for the adopted closure (so out-of-scope files never count), reads each\n826: file with the Clojure reader per lane feature (so comments and string\n827: literals, docstrings included, never count), and collects symbols, class\n828: names and import/require forms; a hit is any such symbol naming\n829: `BigInteger`, `BigDecimal`, `clojure.lang.Ratio`, `java.text`, `unorm`\n830: (H2) or `MessageDigest`, `Blake3`, `noble`, `blake3_dart`, `package:crypto`,\n831: `ed25519_edwards`, `goog.crypt.base64` (H3) in a file outside `dao/host/`\n832: and, for H3's Ed25519 names, outside `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc` (`generate`,\n833: deferred). Codec-track files stay on list 1 and are not scanned by this\n834: mode (their arms are the codec track's). The gate fails distinctly when the\n835: closure list is empty or a file cannot be read, which is a scan error, not\n836: \"no hits\".\n837: \n838: ### 8.3 File-disjointness from the codec track, including tests (re-checked, V)\n839: \n840: Codec-track source files (`codec.md` §7.1): `dao/stream/ws.cljc`,\n841: `transit.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`, `cbor/boring.cljc`, `codec.cljc`,\n842: `remote_channel.cljc`, `jing/stream.cljc`, `data.cljc`, the four ws adapters,\n843: `yin/repl/{serve,connect}.cljc`. Codec-track test namespaces (`codec.md`\n844: §7.2): the 22 requiring Transit, including `ws_test`, `ws-codec-test`,\n845: `remote-route-test`, `loopback-net`, `transit-test`, `dao.stream.cbor-test`,\n846: `dao.jing.stream-test`, `yin.repl.main-test`.\n847: \n848: H0-H4 source files: `dao/host/*` (new), `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`,\n849: `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`, `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`,\n850: `dao/jing.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn.cljc`,\n851: `yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc`,\n852: `yin/vm.cljc`, `yin/vm/engine.cljc`, `yin/vm/integer.cljc`,\n853: `dao/stream/chunks.cljc`, `dao/stream/base64.cljc`, `dao/jing/dht.cljc`,\n854: `yin/vm/linker.cljc`, `dao/stream/datagram.cljc`, `dao/data/arrays.cljc`.\n855: H0-H4 test files: `dao/host/*_test` (new), `yin/vm/integer_test`,\n856: `yang/python/antlr/{int_heap,int_literal,int_ops}_test`, `dao/jing/cbor_*`,\n857: `dao/jing_test`, `yin/vm/linker/sign_test`, `dao/stream/base64_test`,\n858: `yin/vm/debruijn_code_test`, `yin/vm/data_test`, `dao/data/btree_*`.\n859: \n860: Intersection: none, with two recorded deferrals: `dao/stream/codec.cljc:45`\n861: (`host-bytes?` over `dao.host.bytes`) after C4, and `dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc`\n862: (the transport writer) is **not** touched by H4. The `dao.stream.cbor-test`\n863: and `dao.jing.cbor_test` namespaces are distinct files. The deferred H5\n864: (§9.1) would touch `ws.cljc:122`, `ws_test.cljc:11` and\n865: `remote_route_test.cljc:24` (V: identity-less ring creation), which is why\n866: it is deferred behind the codec track as well as behind its own design.\n867: \n868: Coordination with a host-lane probe track: its \"narrow source adaptations\"\n869: (R: the spike touched `integer/host.cljc`, `jing.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`,\n870: `cbor/boring.cljc`) are exactly the H1-H4 files; under OQ3 that work is\n871: paused until H4 lands and needs file-level coordination, not just a rebase.\n872: "}]}],"meta":{"source":"tool","messageId":"6c32c1c1-f3e0-464e-9c58-38125c25fff6"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Here I'll read the tools: closure.clj, gate_test.clj, corpus_hashes.clj. These are probably large. Main check items:\n\n(a) Fidelity of the closure tool: features per lane, resolution src/<lane> taking precedence over src/cljc, not treating :as-alias/string libspecs as dependencies, handling of #?@ (tools.namespace's read-ns-decl processes reader conditionals with the given features — splicing is also handled by the reader). Verify the strip-nils adaptation. Independency of the second traversal in gate_test: it must not share code with tools.namespace, and must use tools.reader's :preserve and its own arm selection.\n\n(b) Gate tests: in-memory negatives, scan-failure, exemption by form, honesty of list 1 (:h0-unlisted 16).\n\n(c) corpus_hashes: 18 files, tests assert the digests.\n\n(d) Verify F2 myself: grep for random-uuid occurrences within src/cljc; grep for places that require dao.await / yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve.\n\n(e) Scope: only src/dev/host_boundary, test/dao/host/gate_test.clj, docs/design/host-boundary/* — confirm that deps.edn/bb.edn are unchanged (compared to base? Can't diff without git, but can compare the main tree's deps.edn with what I saw in j0c... the main tree's deps.edn was already read earlier in this session (j0c worktree + main). Check whether the host-h0 worktree's deps.edn matches main. Actually base eacaed90 is the local master; the main tree's deps.edn that I read in a previous turn — the worktree one should be identical. Quick check by grepping for hb alias (should not exist).\n\nRead closure.clj and gate_test.clj. gate_test is probably big (10 deftests + traversal B). First read closure.clj and corpus_hashes.clj, then gate_test.clj, after that do targeted greps.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now the tool sources.\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_a96da9c82ca34cc4a5ec9729","name":"read_file","input":{"paths":["/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj","/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj"]}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1792522654730,"messageId":"11461243-dd8b-40f3-8173-d080c8cddc9f"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_a96da9c82ca34cc4a5ec9729","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 2/2 files\n--- File Contents ---\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj (clojure)\n(ns host-boundary.closure\n  \"The adopted closure of dao.stream.host-boundary.md §3.1, per lane.\n\n   A require-form traversal from yin.repl.main over the ns declarations,\n   parsed by clojure.tools.namespace.parse (read-ns-decl with the lane's\n   reader features, deps-from-ns-decl for :require, :use and\n   :require-macros; :as-alias and string (npm, dart:) libspecs are not\n   dependencies). Lane features: :clj #{:clj}, :cljs #{:cljs},\n   :cljd #{:cljd :clj} (the cljd build also reads :clj arms; the first\n   matching arm wins, as in tools.reader). A namespace resolves to\n   src/<lane>/<path>.<lane> first (the shadow: yin.repl.host is\n   host.cljc on the JVM, host.cljs and host.cljd elsewhere), then\n   src/cljc/<path>.cljc; a namespace with neither (clojure.core, a\n   library) is outside the closure.\n\n   It is not a compiler-resolved call graph: it over-includes a namespace\n   required but unused, and does not see dynamic loading.\n\n   Each file is tagged with its §3.1 classes (a set: a file can sit in\n   several rows of the §3.1 table; :none means no host contact beyond the\n   §3.3 exempt syntax).\n\n   Run from the repo root:\n     clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:hb {:extra-paths [\\\"src/dev\\\"]\n                      :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace\n                                   {:mvn/version \\\"1.5.0\\\"}}}}}' \\\\\n       -M:hb -m host-boundary.closure [--check]\n   writes docs/design/host-boundary/closure-{clj,cljs,cljd}.edn and\n   prints the totals; --check writes nothing and exits 1 when a committed\n   file differs from the computed closure.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    [clojure.pprint :as pp]\n    [clojure.set :as set]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [clojure.tools.namespace.parse :as parse]\n    [clojure.walk :as walk]))\n\n\n(def root 'yin.repl.main)\n(def lanes [:clj :cljs :cljd])\n(def out-dir \"docs/design/host-boundary\")\n\n\n(def lane-features\n  {:clj #{:clj}, :cljs #{:cljs}, :cljd #{:cljd :clj}})\n\n\n(defn ns->path\n  [ns-sym]\n  (-> (name ns-sym) (str/replace \"-\" \"_\") (str/replace \".\" \"/\")))\n\n\n(defn resolve-file\n  \"The repo-relative file for ns-sym on lane, or nil.\"\n  [lane ns-sym]\n  (let [p (ns->path ns-sym)\n        lane-dir (name lane)]\n    (some (fn [f] (when (.isFile (io/file f)) f))\n          [(str \"src/\" lane-dir \"/\" p \".\" lane-dir)\n           (str \"src/cljc/\" p \".cljc\")])))\n\n\n(defn strip-nils\n  \"Drops the nil a lane's arm leaves in a libspec position\n   (`#?(:cljd nil :clj [x])` reads as nil on :cljd); deps-from-ns-decl\n   refuses nil as unparsable, the compilers ignore it.\"\n  [form]\n  (walk/postwalk (fn [x]\n                   (cond (vector? x) (vec (remove nil? x))\n                         (seq? x) (apply list (remove nil? x))\n                         :else x))\n                 form))\n\n\n(defn ns-decl\n  [lane file]\n  (with-open [r (java.io.PushbackReader. (io/reader file))]\n    (strip-nils (parse/read-ns-decl r {:read-cond :allow\n                                       :features (lane-features lane)}))))\n\n\n(defn lane-closure\n  \"{file ns-sym} for every file reachable from root on lane.\"\n  [lane]\n  (loop [todo [root]\n         seen #{}\n         files {}]\n    (if-let [n (first todo)]\n      (if (seen n)\n        (recur (rest todo) seen files)\n        (let [seen (conj seen n)]\n          (if-let [f (resolve-file lane n)]\n            (let [decl (ns-decl lane f)\n                  deps (sort (parse/deps-from-ns-decl decl))]\n              (when-not (= n (parse/name-from-ns-decl decl))\n                (throw (ex-info \"ns name does not match its file\"\n                                {:lane lane :ns n :file f\n                                 :declared (parse/name-from-ns-decl decl)})))\n              (recur (concat (rest todo) deps) seen (assoc files f n)))\n            (recur (rest todo) seen files))))\n      files)))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; §3.1 classes. Keys are namespaces; a row's namespaces are named exactly as\n;; the §3.1 table names them, expanded where the table abbreviates (\".datagram\"\n;; = dao.stream.datagram, \"the seams\" = the lane-specific ws/datagram files).\n;; Files of the §3.2 random-uuid/rand list carry :deferred-entropy.\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(def class-rows\n  [[:profile-internal-pure \"H1-H2 (writer H4)\"\n    '[yin.vm.integer.host dao.jing.cbor dao.jing.cbor.boring dao.jing.cbor.cljd\n      yin.vm.debruijn yin.vm.debruijn-code yin.vm.data yin.vm.values\n      dao.stream.chunks dao.stream.base64 dao.jing.dht yin.vm.linker\n      dao.stream.datagram dao.data.arrays]]\n   [:profile-hash-sign \"H3\" '[dao.jing yin.vm.linker.sign]]\n   [:consumer \"H2 (require change only)\"\n    '[yin.vm yin.vm.engine yin.vm.values yin.vm.data yin.vm.integer]]\n   [:external-stream-seam \"none (existing streams)\"\n    '[dao.stream.ws dao.stream.datagram dao.stream.udp\n      dao.stream.ws.jvm dao.stream.ws.node dao.stream.ws.dart\n      dao.stream.ws.browser dao.stream.datagram.jvm dao.stream.datagram.node\n      dao.stream.datagram.dart yin.repl.host yin.repl.host.jvm\n      yin.repl.host.common]]\n   [:deferred-storage \"deferred §9.2\"\n    '[dao.jing.file dao.space.store.fs dao.space.store\n      dao.stream.journal.file dao.data.btree.storage]]\n   [:deferred-entropy \"deferred §9.1\"\n    '[dao.stream.ringbuffer dao.stream.memory-log dao.stream.ws\n      dao.stream.remote dao.stream.remote-pair dao.stream.remote-route\n      dao.stream.journal dao.jing.content.step dao.lease dao.await\n      dao.space.store.fs yin.vm.linker yin.vm.ucf.custody\n      yin.vm.ucf.holder.driver yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve yin.vm.telemetry\n      yin.repl yin.repl.dht dao.stream.rpc dao.jing.dht dao.space.dht\n      yin.vm.linker.sign]]\n   [:deferred-timers \"deferred §9.1\"\n    '[dao.jing.content.async dao.jing.coordinate dao.jing.content.driver\n      dao.data.btree.storage]]\n   [:driver \"driver (ambient reads deferred §9.1)\"\n    '[yin.repl.main yin.repl yin.repl.state]]\n   [:deferred-stage \"deferred §9.3\"\n    '[yang.antlr.cst yang.frontend yang.stage yin.repl.frontends]]\n   [:deferred-gensym \"deferred §9.1\"\n    '[yang.clojure yang.php dao.space.transact]]\n   [:runtime-prereq \"table C, no slice\"\n    '[dao.data.btree dao.jing.file dao.stream.journal dao.space.transactor\n      dao.space.schema yin.vm.ucf.authority]]\n   ;; §3.1 names transit, cbor and codec; the rest are the codec track's\n   ;; files by §8.3 (and ws-project by §8.1's codec row) and the lane twins.\n   [:codec-track \"codec track, untouched (§8.3)\"\n    '[dao.stream.transit dao.stream.cbor dao.stream.codec\n      dao.stream.cbor.boring dao.stream.cbor.cljd dao.stream.transit.cljd\n      dao.stream.ws dao.stream.remote-channel dao.stream.ws-project\n      dao.jing.stream dao.data dao.stream.ws.jvm dao.stream.ws.node\n      dao.stream.ws.dart dao.stream.ws.browser yin.repl.serve\n      yin.repl.connect]]\n   [:internal-pure-display \"none (list 1, display only)\" '[dao.pretty]]])\n\n\n(def prefix-rows\n  \"Rows the §3.1 table names by prefix (`yang.python.antlr.*`).\"\n  [[:deferred-stage \"yang.python.antlr.\"]])\n\n\n(def lane-rows\n  \"Lane-specific files the §3.1 table does not name in a row but §3.1's\n   lane-specific list and §8.1's \\\"Seams and driver\\\" row place: the\n   waitset timer drivers (setTimeout, Timer) are seams of dao.stream.waitset.\"\n  '{dao.stream.waitset.driver #{:external-stream-seam}})\n\n\n(defn classes-of\n  [ns-sym]\n  (let [s (name ns-sym)\n        cs (into (set (keep (fn [[c _ nss]] (when (some #{ns-sym} nss) c))\n                            class-rows))\n                 (keep (fn [[c pre]] (when (str/starts-with? s pre) c))\n                       prefix-rows))\n        cs (into cs (lane-rows ns-sym))]\n    (if (seq cs) cs #{:none})))\n\n\n(def class-legend\n  (into (sorted-map) (map (fn [[c slice _]] [c slice]) class-rows)))\n\n\n(defn lane-report\n  [lane files shared]\n  {:lane lane\n   :root root\n   :features (lane-features lane)\n   :total (count files)\n   :shared (count shared)\n   :lane-specific (count (remove shared (keys files)))\n   :class-legend (assoc class-legend :none \"no host contact beyond §3.3\")\n   :files (vec (for [[f n] (sort-by key files)]\n                 {:file f\n                  :ns n\n                  :shared (contains? shared f)\n                  :classes (into (sorted-set) (classes-of n))}))})\n\n\n(defn compute\n  []\n  (let [closures (into {} (map (fn [l] [l (lane-closure l)]) lanes))\n        shared (apply set/intersection (map (comp set keys) (vals closures)))]\n    {:shared shared\n     :reports (into {} (map (fn [[l fs]] [l (lane-report l fs shared)])\n                            closures))}))\n\n\n(defn render\n  [report]\n  (str \";; Generated by src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj (host-boundary H0).\\n\"\n       \";; Do not edit by hand; regenerate with the command in that file's ns doc.\\n\"\n       (with-out-str\n         (binding [*print-namespace-maps* false]\n           (pp/pprint report)))))\n\n\n(defn out-file\n  [lane]\n  (str out-dir \"/closure-\" (name lane) \".edn\"))\n\n\n(defn -main\n  [& args]\n  (let [check? (some #{\"--check\"} args)\n        {:keys [shared reports]} (compute)\n        stale (atom [])]\n    (doseq [l lanes]\n      (let [r (reports l)\n            text (render r)\n            f (io/file (out-file l))]\n        (println (format \"%-5s total %d shared %d lane-specific %d\"\n                         (name l) (:total r) (:shared r) (:lane-specific r)))\n        (if check?\n          (when-not (and (.isFile f) (= text (slurp f)))\n            (swap! stale conj (out-file l)))\n          (do (io/make-parents f)\n              (spit f text)))))\n    (println \"shared (all three lanes):\" (count shared))\n    (when (seq @stale)\n      (println \"STALE:\" (str/join \" \" @stale))\n      (System/exit 1))\n    (shutdown-agents)))\n\n\n// File: .claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj (clojure)\n(ns host-boundary.corpus-hashes\n  \"The corpus hash set of dao.stream.host-boundary.md H0 (d): the SHA-256\n   of every file under the Jing corpus (test/resources/dao/jing) and the\n   codec wire fixtures (test/fixtures/codec), which H1-H4 must keep\n   byte-identical.\n\n   Run from the repo root with babashka:\n     bb src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj [--check]\n   writes docs/design/host-boundary/corpus-sha256.edn; --check writes\n   nothing and exits 1 when a file's bytes, or the file set, differ from\n   the committed hash set. dao.host.gate-test asserts the same on the JVM\n   lane.\"\n  (:require\n    [babashka.fs :as fs]\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    [clojure.pprint :as pp]\n    [clojure.string :as str]))\n\n\n(def roots [\"test/resources/dao/jing\" \"test/fixtures/codec\"])\n(def out-file \"docs/design/host-boundary/corpus-sha256.edn\")\n\n\n(defn sha-256\n  [path]\n  (let [d (java.security.MessageDigest/getInstance \"SHA-256\")]\n    (apply str (map #(format \"%02x\" (bit-and % 0xff))\n                    (.digest d (fs/read-all-bytes path))))))\n\n\n(defn hash-set*\n  []\n  {:algorithm \"SHA-256\"\n   :regenerate \"bb src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj\"\n   :roots roots\n   :files (into (sorted-map)\n                (for [r roots\n                      p (fs/glob r \"**\")\n                      :when (fs/regular-file? p)\n                      :let [f (str/replace (str p) \"\\\\\" \"/\")]]\n                  [f (sha-256 p)]))})\n\n\n(defn render\n  [m]\n  (str \";; Generated by src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj (host-boundary H0).\\n\"\n       \";; Do not edit by hand; H1-H4 keep these bytes identical.\\n\"\n       (with-out-str (pp/pprint m))))\n\n\n(defn -main\n  [& args]\n  (let [m (hash-set*)\n        text (render m)]\n    (println (count (:files m)) \"files\")\n    (if (some #{\"--check\"} args)\n      (let [committed (when (fs/exists? out-file) (edn/read-string (slurp out-file)))]\n        (if (= (:files committed) (:files m))\n          (println \"corpus identical to\" out-file)\n          (do (println \"CORPUS DIFFERS from\" out-file)\n              (doseq [f (sort (into (set (keys (:files m))) (keys (:files committed))))\n                      :when (not= (get (:files m) f) (get (:files committed) f))]\n                (println \" \" f))\n              (System/exit 1))))\n      (spit out-file text))))\n\n\n(when (= *file* (System/getProperty \"babashka.file\"))\n  (apply -main *command-line-args*))\n\n"}]}],"meta":{"source":"tool","messageId":"8f350e40-8203-4d56-8a4b-8e87838f5125"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"closure.clj looks fine: lane features are correct (:cljd #{:cljd :clj}), resolution order prioritizes lane and then cljc, tools.namespace's read-ns-decl and deps-from-ns-decl (:as-alias is handled by tools.namespace 1.5.0 — deps-from-ns-decl excludes :as-alias; string libspecs: deps-from-ns-decl maps symbols; strings are… actually deps-from-ns-decl in 1.5.0 only returns symbols; string libspecs like \"npm:foo\" are ignored? The docstring claims they aren't dependencies — tools.namespace's parse-deps… in 1.5.0 does `deps-from-ns-decl` return only symbols? I think the map-spec parsing takes the first element that's a symbol; string libspecs are skipped (there was a fix to ignore strings). Reasonable; also the cljd lane reads string libspecs for `dart:` packages. ns name mismatch check → throw (fail-closed). #?@ inside ns forms: tools.reader's read-cond :allow natively handles splicing ✓ (r3's flaw was a homegrown regex script; the new tool delegates to the reader). strip-nils for cases like `#?(:cljd nil :clj [...])` → nil libspecs. Sound adaptation.\n\nPotential under-inclusion risks: (1) ns forms that fail to parse → read-ns-decl throws → tool fails loudly (fail-closed, not silent). (2) `:use` is included ✓. (3) Dynamic requires not visible — disclosed. (4) resolve-file: only checks src/<lane> and src/cljc — namespaces that exist only in src/clj but are also needed for cljs? For the cljs lane, yin.repl.host resolves to src/cljs/..., then src/cljc; src/clj is not included in cljs resolution — correct per lane semantics (shadow uses src/cljs + src/cljc). For the cljd lane: src/cljd, then src/cljc — but cljd also reads :clj arms; could a namespace exist only in src/clj and be required from cljd? If so, resolution fails → silently excluded from the closure! Hmm: the resolve-file for lane cljd checks \"src/cljd/...\" and \"src/cljc/...\". If a file exists only in src/clj and is reachable via a :clj arm on the cljd lane, it gets silently dropped. Does the cljd classpath include src/clj? The deps.edn :clojuredart build… the repo's cljd compile uses paths src/clj src/cljc src/cljd (root :paths includes everything). In practice, ClojureDart's resolution includes src/clj. But §3.1's methodology says \"resolve each namespace first to a file under src/<lane>, then to src/cljc\" — the design itself specifies this two-root rule, so the tool is faithful to the design. If src/clj-only namespaces were reachable from cljd, the design's totals wouldn't match either. Not a flaw relative to the spec; but worth mentioning? The design explicitly states this rule and the totals agree at 142/140/141, and traversal B independently agrees. OK.\n\n(5) Traversal B in gate_test — need to read gate_test.clj to verify independence and gate logic. Probably a large file. Let's read it.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now the gate test — the biggest adversarial target.\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_2cad5919095c4bbca7a595f2","name":"read_file","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/test/dao/host/gate_test.clj"}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1792522691294,"messageId":"5801e7e8-8738-4dff-ad44-9af381d64d22"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_2cad5919095c4bbca7a595f2","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 772 lines\n1: (ns dao.host.gate-test\n2:   \"The H0 freeze gate of docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md (§8 H0,\n3:    §8.1, §3.2, §3.3), over the adopted closure committed by\n4:    src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj under docs/design/host-boundary/.\n5: \n6:    The gate reads every closure file with tools.reader (:read-cond\n7:    :preserve, so every lane's arms are seen; comments, strings and\n8:    docstrings never count) and fails when\n9:    - a file outside list 1 holds a non-exempt host arm (§3.3 exempts:\n10:      ns-form arms, catch-type arms, arms equal but for hints, protocol\n11:      blocks directly inside deftype/defrecord/reify/extend bodies,\n12:      print-method defmethods, exists? tests, (Object.)/(js-obj)\n13:      sentinels); a lane-specific file (.clj .cljs .cljd) is a host arm as\n14:      a whole;\n15:    - a file holds more resolved effect calls of a kind than list 2\n16:      permits (the §3.2 kinds, and calls of the §2.4 M entries).\n17:    Effect calls are resolved lexically: a symbol bound by let, fn, loop,\n18:    for, doseq, catch, letfn or a deftype method, defined in its file, or\n19:    excluded by :refer-clojure, is not the core function; quoted forms and\n20:    (comment ...) are data. Reading zero files, or failing to read one, is\n21:    a scan failure, distinct from a pass.\n22: \n23:    JVM lane only: the gate reads source text from disk; what it checks is\n24:    the same text on every lane.\n25: \n26:    Also here: the independent second traversal of the closure (a\n27:    reader-form walker that selects reader-conditional arms itself and\n28:    parses libspecs itself, sharing no code with tools.namespace), which\n29:    must agree with the committed closure files.\"\n30:   (:require\n31:     [clojure.edn :as edn]\n32:     [clojure.java.io :as io]\n33:     [clojure.set :as set]\n34:     [clojure.string :as str]\n35:     [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n36:     [clojure.tools.reader :as reader]\n37:     [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt])\n38:   (:import\n39:     (clojure.lang\n40:       ReaderConditional)))\n41: \n42: \n43: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n44: ;; Reading\n45: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n46: \n47: (defn read-forms\n48:   \"Every top-level form of text, reader conditionals preserved.\"\n49:   [text]\n50:   (binding [reader/*read-eval* false\n51:             ;; ::alias/kw needs no real namespace: keywords never count\n52:             reader/*alias-map* (fn [sym] sym)\n53:             reader/*default-data-reader-fn* (fn [tag v] (tagged-literal tag v))]\n54:     (let [rdr (rt/indexing-push-back-reader text 1)]\n55:       (loop [acc []]\n56:         (let [form (reader/read {:read-cond :preserve :eof ::eof} rdr)]\n57:           (if (= ::eof form) acc (recur (conj acc form))))))))\n58: \n59: \n60: (defn rc?\n61:   [x]\n62:   (instance? ReaderConditional x))\n63: \n64: \n65: (defn rc-arms\n66:   \"[[feature form] ...] of a reader conditional.\"\n67:   [^ReaderConditional rc]\n68:   (map vec (partition 2 (.-form rc))))\n69: \n70: \n71: (defn splicing?\n72:   [^ReaderConditional rc]\n73:   (boolean (.-splicing rc)))\n74: \n75: \n76: (defn head\n77:   [x]\n78:   (when (and (seq? x) (symbol? (first x))) (first x)))\n79: \n80: \n81: (defn line-of\n82:   [x]\n83:   (:line (meta x)))\n84: \n85: \n86: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n87: ;; The independent closure traversal (traversal B)\n88: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n89: \n90: (def closure-root 'yin.repl.main)\n91: (def lanes [:clj :cljs :cljd])\n92: (def lane-features {:clj #{:clj}, :cljs #{:cljs}, :cljd #{:cljd :clj}})\n93: \n94: \n95: (defn select-arms\n96:   \"form with every reader conditional replaced by its lane arm: the first\n97:    arm whose feature is in features or is :default; a splicing arm's\n98:    elements spliced into the enclosing collection; no arm, nothing.\"\n99:   [features form]\n100:   (let [pick (fn [rc]\n101:                (some (fn [[k v]] (when (or (features k) (= :default k)) [v]))\n102:                      (rc-arms rc)))\n103:         expand (fn [xs]\n104:                  (mapcat (fn [x]\n105:                            (if (rc? x)\n106:                              (when-let [[v] (pick x)]\n107:                                (if (splicing? x)\n108:                                  (map #(select-arms features %) v)\n109:                                  [(select-arms features v)]))\n110:                              [(select-arms features x)]))\n111:                          xs))]\n112:     (cond\n113:       (rc? form) (some->> (pick form) first (select-arms features))\n114:       (seq? form) (apply list (expand form))\n115:       (vector? form) (vec (expand form))\n116:       (map? form) (into {} (map vec (partition 2 (expand (mapcat identity form)))))\n117:       :else form)))\n118: \n119: \n120: (defn libspec-deps\n121:   [spec]\n122:   (cond\n123:     (symbol? spec) [spec]\n124:     (or (string? spec) (keyword? spec) (nil? spec)) []\n125:     (sequential? spec)\n126:     (let [[a b] spec\n127:           opts (rest spec)]\n128:       (cond\n129:         (string? a) []\n130:         (and (symbol? a) (or (nil? b) (keyword? b)))\n131:         (if (and (= :as-alias b) (not-any? #{:as :refer :refer-macros :include-macros} opts))\n132:           []\n133:           [a])\n134:         (symbol? a)\n135:         (mapcat (fn [s]\n136:                   (map #(symbol (str a \".\" %)) (libspec-deps s)))\n137:                 (remove nil? (rest spec)))\n138:         :else []))\n139:     :else []))\n140: \n141: \n142: (defn ns-deps\n143:   \"The namespaces an ns form requires on a lane: :require, :use and\n144:    :require-macros clauses.\"\n145:   [features ns-form]\n146:   (let [f (select-arms features ns-form)]\n147:     (->> (rest f)\n148:          (filter seq?)\n149:          (filter #(#{:require :use :require-macros} (first %)))\n150:          (mapcat rest)\n151:          (mapcat libspec-deps)\n152:          set)))\n153: \n154: \n155: (defn lane-file\n156:   [lane ns-sym]\n157:   (let [p (-> (name ns-sym) (str/replace \"-\" \"_\") (str/replace \".\" \"/\"))]\n158:     (some #(when (.isFile (io/file %)) %)\n159:           [(str \"src/\" (name lane) \"/\" p \".\" (name lane))\n160:            (str \"src/cljc/\" p \".cljc\")])))\n161: \n162: \n163: (defn traverse\n164:   \"The closure files of lane from closure-root, by traversal B.\"\n165:   [lane]\n166:   (loop [todo [closure-root] seen #{} files #{}]\n167:     (if-let [n (first todo)]\n168:       (if (seen n)\n169:         (recur (rest todo) seen files)\n170:         (if-let [f (lane-file lane n)]\n171:           (let [ns-form (first (filter #(= 'ns (head %)) (read-forms (slurp f))))]\n172:             (recur (concat (rest todo) (sort (ns-deps (lane-features lane) ns-form)))\n173:                    (conj seen n)\n174:                    (conj files f)))\n175:           (recur (rest todo) (conj seen n) files)))\n176:       files)))\n177: \n178: \n179: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n180: ;; The committed closure (traversal A, src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj)\n181: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n182: \n183: (defn committed-closure\n184:   [lane]\n185:   (edn/read-string (slurp (str \"docs/design/host-boundary/closure-\" (name lane) \".edn\"))))\n186: \n187: \n188: (defn closure-files\n189:   \"The union of the three lanes' committed closure files.\"\n190:   []\n191:   (into (sorted-set) (mapcat #(map :file (:files (committed-closure %))) lanes)))\n192: \n193: \n194: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n195: ;; Host arms (§3.3 exemptions)\n196: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n197: \n198: (def deftype-heads\n199:   '#{deftype defrecord reify extend-type extend-protocol specify specify!})\n200: \n201: \n202: (def sentinels\n203:   '#{(Object.) (js-obj) (js/Object.) (java.lang.Object.)})\n204: \n205: \n206: (defn exemption\n207:   \"The §3.3 pattern that exempts rc, given its ancestors (outermost first),\n208:    or nil.\"\n209:   [rc ancestors]\n210:   (let [parent (peek ancestors)\n211:         arms (map second (rc-arms rc))\n212:         catch-form? #(and (seq? %) (= 'catch (first %)))]\n213:     (cond\n214:       (some #(= 'ns (head %)) ancestors) :ns-require-arm\n215:       (and (catch-form? parent) (identical? rc (second parent))) :catch-type\n216:       (and (< 1 (count arms)) (apply = arms)) :hint-only\n217:       (and (splicing? rc) (deftype-heads (head parent))) :protocol-block\n218:       (some #(and (= 'defmethod (head %)) (= 'print-method (second %))) ancestors) :print-method\n219:       (every? #(and (seq? %) (= 'defmethod (first %)) (= 'print-method (second %))) arms)\n220:       :print-method\n221:       (every? #(= 'exists? (head %)) arms) :exists\n222:       (every? sentinels arms) :sentinel\n223:       :else nil)))\n224: \n225: \n226: (defn non-exempt-arms\n227:   \"[line ...] of the non-exempt reader conditionals in forms.\"\n228:   [forms]\n229:   (let [acc (atom [])\n230:         walk (fn walk\n231:                [form ancestors]\n232:                (let [down (conj ancestors form)]\n233:                  (cond\n234:                    (rc? form)\n235:                    (do (when-not (exemption form ancestors)\n236:                          (swap! acc conj (or (some (comp line-of second) (rc-arms form))\n237:                                              (some line-of (rseq ancestors)))))\n238:                        (doseq [[_ arm] (rc-arms form)]\n239:                          (if (splicing? form)\n240:                            (doseq [x arm] (walk x down))\n241:                            (walk arm down))))\n242:                    (and (seq? form) (= 'comment (first form))) nil\n243:                    (map? form) (doseq [[k v] form] (walk k down) (walk v down))\n244:                    (coll? form) (doseq [x form] (walk x down))\n245:                    :else nil)))]\n246:     (doseq [f forms] (walk f []))\n247:     @acc))\n248: \n249: \n250: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n251: ;; Resolved effect calls (§3.2 kinds, §2.4 M entries)\n252: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n253: \n254: (def core-ns #{nil \"clojure.core\" \"cljs.core\" \"cljd.core\"})\n255: \n256: \n257: (defn effect-kind\n258:   \"The §3.2 kind of a symbol that names a host effect, or nil. core? is\n259:    false when an unqualified name is shadowed in its file.\"\n260:   [sym core?]\n261:   (let [n (name sym)\n262:         q (namespace sym)\n263:         core (and (contains? core-ns q) (or q core?))]\n264:     (cond\n265:       (and core (= n \"random-uuid\")) :random-uuid\n266:       (and core (#{\"rand\" \"rand-int\" \"rand-nth\" \"shuffle\" \"random-sample\"} n)) :rand\n267:       (or (str/includes? n \"SecureRandom\")\n268:           (= n \"Random.secure\")\n269:           (= n \"randomUUID\")\n270:           (and (= q \"js\") (str/starts-with? n \"crypto\"))\n271:           (#{\"getRandomValues\" \"randomBytes\" \"generateKey\"} n)) :secure-random\n272:       (and core (= n \"gensym\")) :gensym\n273:       (or (and (#{\"System\" \"java.lang.System\"} q) (#{\"currentTimeMillis\" \"nanoTime\"} n))\n274:           (and (= q \"js\") (or (str/starts-with? n \"Date\") (str/starts-with? n \"performance\")))\n275:           (str/starts-with? n \"DateTime.now\")\n276:           (and q (str/ends-with? q \"Instant\") (= n \"now\"))) :clock\n277:       (or (and (#{\"System\" \"java.lang.System\"} q) (#{\"getenv\" \"getProperty\" \"getProperties\"} n))\n278:           (and (= q \"js\") (str/starts-with? n \"process\"))\n279:           (str/starts-with? n \"Platform.\")) :ambient\n280:       (or (and core (#{\"println\" \"print\" \"prn\" \"pr\" \"printf\" \"newline\"} n))\n281:           (and (= q \"js\") (str/starts-with? n \"console\"))) :print\n282:       (or (and (= q \"js\") (#{\"setTimeout\" \"setInterval\" \"setImmediate\" \"queueMicrotask\"} n))\n283:           (str/starts-with? n \"Timer\")\n284:           (and (#{\"Thread\" \"java.lang.Thread\"} q) (= n \"sleep\"))\n285:           (str/starts-with? n \"Future.delayed\")) :timer\n286:       :else nil)))\n287: \n288: \n289: (def m-entry-nss\n290:   \"The namespaces holding §2.4's M entries, now and after H1.\"\n291:   '#{dao.data.arrays dao.host.bytes})\n292: \n293: \n294: (def m-entry-names #{\"aset\" \"acopy\" \"asort\" \"set!\" \"copy!\"})\n295: \n296: \n297: (defn all-arms\n298:   \"form with every reader conditional replaced by all its arms, so every\n299:    lane's text is seen: a splicing conditional's elements are spliced into\n300:    the enclosing collection; a non-splicing one becomes (do arm ...), or,\n301:    with splice-all?, is spliced too (for ns clauses, where position does\n302:    not bind).\"\n303:   ([form] (all-arms false form))\n304:   ([splice-all? form]\n305:    (let [expand (fn [xs]\n306:                   (mapcat (fn [x]\n307:                             (if (and (rc? x) (or splice-all? (splicing? x)))\n308:                               (map #(all-arms splice-all? %)\n309:                                    (mapcat (fn [[_ v]] (if (splicing? x) v [v])) (rc-arms x)))\n310:                               [(all-arms splice-all? x)]))\n311:                           xs))]\n312:      (cond\n313:        (rc? form) (cons 'do (map #(all-arms splice-all? %)\n314:                                  (mapcat (fn [[_ v]] (if (splicing? form) v [v]))\n315:                                          (rc-arms form))))\n316:        (seq? form) (with-meta (apply list (expand form)) (meta form))\n317:        (vector? form) (vec (expand form))\n318:        (map? form) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(all-arms splice-all? k) (all-arms splice-all? v)])\n319:                                  form))\n320:        :else form))))\n321: \n322: \n323: (defn file-scope\n324:   \"{:aliases {alias ns} :refers {sym ns} :shadowed #{sym}} of a file:\n325:    every lane's ns arms, its top-level defs, its :refer-clojure excludes.\"\n326:   [forms]\n327:   (let [ns-form (all-arms true (first (filter #(= 'ns (head %)) forms)))\n328:         specs (->> (rest ns-form)\n329:                    (filter seq?)\n330:                    (filter #(#{:require :use} (first %)))\n331:                    (mapcat rest)\n332:                    (filter vector?))\n333:         opts (fn [spec] (apply hash-map (rest (if (even? (count spec)) (butlast spec) spec))))\n334:         excluded (->> (rest ns-form)\n335:                       (filter #(and (seq? %) (= :refer-clojure (first %))))\n336:                       (mapcat #(:exclude (apply hash-map (rest %)))))\n337:         defs (->> forms\n338:                   (map all-arms)\n339:                   (mapcat (fn [f] (if (= 'do (head f)) (rest f) [f])))\n340:                   (keep (fn [f]\n341:                           (when (#{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro 'defonce 'declare\n342:                                    'defprotocol 'defmulti} (head f))\n343:                             (second f)))))]\n344:     {:aliases (into {} (keep (fn [s] (when-let [a (:as (opts s))] [a (first s)])) specs))\n345:      :refers (into {} (mapcat (fn [s]\n346:                                 (let [r (:refer (opts s))]\n347:                                   (when (sequential? r) (map (fn [x] [x (first s)]) r))))\n348:                               specs))\n349:      :shadowed (set (filter symbol? (concat excluded defs)))}))\n350: \n351: \n352: (defn binding-syms\n353:   \"Every symbol in a binding form (destructuring included).\"\n354:   [b]\n355:   (cond\n356:     (symbol? b) (if (= '& b) [] [b])\n357:     (map? b) (mapcat binding-syms (concat (keys b) (vals b)))\n358:     (coll? b) (mapcat binding-syms b)\n359:     :else []))\n360: \n361: \n362: (def let-heads\n363:   '#{let let* loop loop* when-let if-let when-some if-some when-first\n364:      with-open dotimes for doseq})\n365: \n366: \n367: (def fn-heads '#{fn fn* defn defn- defmacro defmethod})\n368: \n369: \n370: (defn effect-calls\n371:   \"[[kind line] ...] for the resolved effect calls in forms.\"\n372:   [forms]\n373:   (let [{:keys [aliases refers shadowed]} (file-scope forms)\n374:         acc (atom [])\n375:         hit! (fn [kind sym] (swap! acc conj [kind (line-of sym)]))\n376:         resolve-m (fn [sym]\n377:                     (if-let [q (namespace sym)]\n378:                       (get aliases (symbol q) (symbol q))\n379:                       (get refers sym)))]\n380:     (letfn [(walk\n381:               [form bound]\n382:               (cond\n383:                 (symbol? form)\n384:                 (when-not (and (nil? (namespace form)) (bound form))\n385:                   (if-let [k (effect-kind form (not (shadowed form)))]\n386:                     (hit! k form)\n387:                     (when (and (m-entry-nss (resolve-m form)) (m-entry-names (name form)))\n388:                       (hit! :m-entry form))))\n389: \n390:                 (seq? form)\n391:                 (let [h (head form)]\n392:                   (cond\n393:                     (#{'quote 'comment 'ns} h) nil\n394:                     (let-heads h) (walk-let (second form) (nnext form) bound)\n395:                     (= 'letfn h) (let [fns (second form)\n396:                                        b (into bound (map first fns))]\n397:                                    (doseq [f fns] (walk-fn (rest f) b))\n398:                                    (walk-all (nnext form) b))\n399:                     (fn-heads h) (walk-fn (rest form) bound)\n400:                     (= 'catch h) (walk-all (drop 3 form) (conj bound (nth form 2 nil)))\n401:                     (deftype-heads h) (let [fields (filter vector? (take 3 form))\n402:                                             b (into bound (mapcat binding-syms fields))]\n403:                                         (doseq [x (drop 2 form)]\n404:                                           (if (and (seq? x) (vector? (second x)))\n405:                                             (walk-fn x b)\n406:                                             (walk x b))))\n407:                     :else (walk-all form bound)))\n408: \n409:                 (map? form) (doseq [[k v] form] (walk k bound) (walk v bound))\n410:                 (coll? form) (walk-all form bound)\n411:                 :else nil))\n412:             (walk-all [xs bound] (doseq [x xs] (walk x bound)))\n413:             (walk-let\n414:               [bvec body bound]\n415:               (let [b (reduce (fn [b [lhs rhs]]\n416:                                 (case lhs\n417:                                   :let (do (walk-let rhs nil b) (into b (binding-syms (take-nth 2 rhs))))\n418:                                   (:when :while) (do (walk rhs b) b)\n419:                                   (do (walk rhs b) (into b (binding-syms lhs)))))\n420:                               bound\n421:                               (partition 2 (if (vector? bvec) bvec [])))]\n422:                 (walk-all body b)))\n423:             (walk-fn\n424:               [tail bound]\n425:               ;; tail: [name? doc? attrs? params body...] or [name? (params body...)...]\n426:               (let [params (concat (filter vector? tail)\n427:                                    (keep #(when (and (seq? %) (vector? (first %))) (first %)) tail))\n428:                     b (into (into bound (filter symbol? (take 1 tail)))\n429:                             (mapcat binding-syms params))]\n430:                 (walk-all (remove #(or (vector? %) (symbol? %)\n431:                                        (and (seq? %) (vector? (first %))))\n432:                                   tail)\n433:                           b)\n434:                 (doseq [x tail :when (and (seq? x) (vector? (first x)))]\n435:                   (walk-all (rest x) b))))]\n436:       (doseq [f forms] (walk (all-arms f) #{})))\n437:     @acc))\n438: \n439: \n440: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n441: ;; List 1 and list 2\n442: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n443: \n444: (def list-1\n445:   \"The closure files permitted non-exempt host arms (§8.1), by category.\n446:    Generated from the H0 tree by the gate and reconciled against the §8.1\n447:    baseline; :h0-unlisted marks the files with real arms that §8.1 does\n448:    not name (an H0 finding, to resolve before H1).\"\n449:   {;; H1-H4 migration sources\n450:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/integer/host.cljc\" :migration-source\n451:    \"src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc\" :migration-source\n452:    \"src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc\" :migration-source\n453:    \"src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd\" :migration-source\n454:    \"src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc\" :migration-source\n455:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc\" :migration-source\n456:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc\" :migration-source\n457:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc\" :migration-source\n458:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc\" :migration-source\n459:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc\" :migration-source\n460:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/chunks.cljc\" :migration-source\n461:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/base64.cljc\" :migration-source\n462:    \"src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc\" :migration-source\n463:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\" :migration-source\n464:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/datagram.cljc\" :migration-source\n465:    ;; Profile\n466:    \"src/cljc/dao/data/arrays.cljc\" :profile\n467:    ;; Retained runtime prerequisites (table C) and display\n468:    \"src/cljc/dao/data/btree.cljc\" :runtime-prereq\n469:    \"src/cljc/dao/data/btree/storage.cljc\" :runtime-prereq\n470:    \"src/cljc/dao/pretty.cljc\" :runtime-prereq\n471:    ;; Codec-track files\n472:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc\" :codec-track\n473:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/transit.cljc\" :codec-track\n474:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/cbor.cljc\" :codec-track\n475:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc\" :codec-track\n476:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/codec.cljc\" :codec-track\n477:    ;; Seams and driver: every lane-specific file, the selector, the driver\n478:    \"src/clj/dao/jing/content/driver.clj\" :seam-driver\n479:    \"src/clj/dao/stream/datagram/jvm.clj\" :seam-driver\n480:    \"src/clj/dao/stream/waitset/driver.clj\" :seam-driver\n481:    \"src/clj/dao/stream/ws/jvm.clj\" :seam-driver\n482:    \"src/clj/yang/antlr/cst.clj\" :seam-driver\n483:    \"src/clj/yin/repl/host/jvm.clj\" :seam-driver\n484:    \"src/cljs/dao/stream/datagram/node.cljs\" :seam-driver\n485:    \"src/cljs/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljs\" :seam-driver\n486:    \"src/cljs/dao/stream/ws/node.cljs\" :seam-driver\n487:    \"src/cljs/yang/antlr/cst.cljs\" :seam-driver\n488:    \"src/cljs/yin/repl/host.cljs\" :seam-driver\n489:    \"src/cljd/dao/stream/cbor/cljd.cljd\" :seam-driver\n490:    \"src/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd\" :seam-driver\n491:    \"src/cljd/dao/stream/datagram/dart.cljd\" :seam-driver\n492:    \"src/cljd/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljd\" :seam-driver\n493:    \"src/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd\" :seam-driver\n494:    \"src/cljd/yang/antlr/cst.cljd\" :seam-driver\n495:    \"src/cljd/yin/repl/host.cljd\" :seam-driver\n496:    \"src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\" :seam-driver\n497:    \"src/cljc/yin/repl/host.cljc\" :seam-driver\n498:    \"src/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc\" :seam-driver\n499:    ;; Deferred-scope files (§9)\n500:    \"src/cljc/dao/jing/file.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n501:    \"src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n502:    \"src/cljc/dao/space/store.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n503:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/journal/file.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n504:    \"src/cljc/dao/jing/coordinate.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n505:    \"src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n506:    \"src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n507:    \"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/parser.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n508:    \"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n509:    \"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n510:    \"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/render.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n511:    \"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/repl_probe.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n512:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/journal.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n513:    \"src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n514:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority.cljc\" :deferred-scope\n515:    ;; H0 finding: real host arms in closure files §8.1 does not name\n516:    \"src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :78 host numeric predicates\n517:    \"src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :808 runtime type name\n518:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :168 host atom type\n519:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :114 rand (entropy, §9.1)\n520:    \"src/cljc/yang/antlr/packet.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :67 code points\n521:    \"src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :375 runtime type name\n522:    \"src/cljc/yang/php.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :95,98 number parsing\n523:    \"src/cljc/yin/repl/adapter.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :58 edn reader\n524:    \"src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :104 edn reader\n525:    \"src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :460 byte length\n526:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :404 bytes->str decoding\n527:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :439 safe integer\n528:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :130 safe integer\n529:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :929 runtime type name\n530:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :32 byte length\n531:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc\" :h0-unlisted ; :282 byte length\n532:    })\n533: \n534: \n535: (def list-2\n536:   \"The resolved effect calls permitted, {file {kind count}}: the §3.2\n537:    sites inside the adopted closure and the callers of §2.4's M entries.\n538:    A count is a ceiling: one more call of that kind in that file fails.\"\n539:   {;; §3.2 random-uuid: 21 inside the closure (dao.await and\n540:    ;; yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve are outside it)\n541:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc\" {:random-uuid 2}\n542:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/memory_log.cljc\" {:random-uuid 1}\n543:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc\" {:random-uuid 1}\n544:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc\" {:random-uuid 1}\n545:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/remote_pair.cljc\" {:random-uuid 1}\n546:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/remote_route.cljc\" {:random-uuid 1}\n547:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/journal.cljc\" {:random-uuid 1}\n548:    \"src/cljc/dao/jing/content/step.cljc\" {:random-uuid 1}\n549:    \"src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc\" {:random-uuid 1}\n550:    \"src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc\" {:random-uuid 2, :ambient 4}\n551:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\" {:random-uuid 1}\n552:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/custody.cljc\" {:random-uuid 1}\n553:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc\" {:random-uuid 1}\n554:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/telemetry.cljc\" {:random-uuid 1}\n555:    \"src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\" {:random-uuid 4, :ambient 3}\n556:    \"src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc\" {:random-uuid 1}\n557:    ;; §3.2 rand, secure generators (sign :79 is jvm-pair's deterministic\n558:    ;; seed-replay SecureRandom proxy, §2.5), gensym\n559:    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc.cljc\" {:rand 3}\n560:    \"src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc\" {:rand 1}\n561:    \"src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc\" {:secure-random 3}\n562:    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc\" {:secure-random 3}\n563:    \"src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\" {:gensym 2}\n564:    \"src/cljc/yang/php.cljc\" {:gensym 1}\n565:    \"src/cljc/dao/space/transact.cljc\" {:gensym 1}\n566:    ;; §3.2 clocks, ambient reads, printing, timers: the driver and the seams\n567:    \"src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\" {:ambient 6, :clock 5, :print 13}\n568:    \"src/clj/dao/jing/content/driver.clj\" {:clock 2, :timer 1}\n569:    \"src/clj/dao/stream/datagram/jvm.clj\" {:timer 1}\n570:    \"src/clj/dao/stream/ws/jvm.clj\" {:clock 1}\n571:    \"src/cljs/dao/stream/ws/node.cljs\" {:clock 1}\n572:    \"src/cljs/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljs\" {:timer 2}\n573:    \"src/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd\" {:clock 1}\n574:    \"src/cljd/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljd\" {:timer 1}\n575:    ;; §2.4 M-entry callers resolved today (dao.data.arrays); chunks, cbor\n576:    ;; and sign mutate host arrays directly and call no M entry yet\n577:    \"src/cljc/dao/data/btree.cljc\" {:m-entry 33}})\n578: \n579: \n580: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n581: ;; The gate\n582: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n583: \n584: (defn lane-specific?\n585:   [file]\n586:   (not (str/ends-with? file \".cljc\")))\n587: \n588: \n589: (defn scan\n590:   \"{file {:arms [line ...] :effects {kind [line ...]}}} for sources\n591:    {file text}, or {file {:error msg}} for a file that cannot be read.\"\n592:   [sources]\n593:   (into (sorted-map)\n594:         (map (fn [[file text]]\n595:                [file (try\n596:                        (let [forms (if text\n597:                                      (read-forms text)\n598:                                      (throw (ex-info \"cannot read file\" {:file file})))]\n599:                          {:arms (if (lane-specific? file)\n600:                                   [:whole-file]\n601:                                   (non-exempt-arms forms))\n602:                           :effects (reduce (fn [m [k line]] (update m k (fnil conj []) line))\n603:                                            {}\n604:                                            (effect-calls forms))})\n605:                        (catch Exception e {:error (or (ex-message e) (str e))}))]))\n606:         sources))\n607: \n608: \n609: (defn gate\n610:   \"The gate over sources {file text}: {:verdict :pass|:fail|:scan-failure\n611:    :scanned n :errors [...] :arm-violations [...] :effect-violations [...]}.\"\n612:   [sources list-1 list-2]\n613:   (let [scanned (scan sources)\n614:         errors (vec (keep (fn [[f r]] (when (:error r) [f (:error r)])) scanned))\n615:         ok (remove (comp :error val) scanned)\n616:         arm-violations (vec (for [[f r] ok\n617:                                   :when (and (seq (:arms r)) (not (contains? list-1 f)))]\n618:                               {:file f :lines (:arms r)}))\n619:         effect-violations (vec (for [[f r] ok\n620:                                      [k lines] (:effects r)\n621:                                      :let [allowed (get-in list-2 [f k] 0)]\n622:                                      :when (> (count lines) allowed)]\n623:                                  {:file f :kind k :count (count lines)\n624:                                   :allowed allowed :lines lines}))]\n625:     {:verdict (cond (or (empty? scanned) (seq errors)) :scan-failure\n626:                     (or (seq arm-violations) (seq effect-violations)) :fail\n627:                     :else :pass)\n628:      :scanned (count ok)\n629:      :errors errors\n630:      :arm-violations arm-violations\n631:      :effect-violations effect-violations\n632:      :observed scanned}))\n633: \n634: \n635: (defn read-sources\n636:   \"{file text} for files; an unreadable file maps to nil text, which the\n637:    gate reports as a scan failure.\"\n638:   [files]\n639:   (into {} (map (fn [f] [f (when (.isFile (io/file f)) (slurp f))])) files))\n640: \n641: \n642: (def current\n643:   (delay (gate (read-sources (closure-files)) list-1 list-2)))\n644: \n645: \n646: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n647: ;; Tests\n648: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n649: \n650: (deftest closure-totals-are-the-design-totals\n651:   (testing \"§3.1: 142 / 140 / 141 files, 133 shared\"\n652:     (let [files (into {} (map (fn [l] [l (set (map :file (:files (committed-closure l))))]) lanes))]\n653:       (is (= 142 (count (files :clj))))\n654:       (is (= 140 (count (files :cljs))))\n655:       (is (= 141 (count (files :cljd))))\n656:       (is (= 133 (count (apply set/intersection (vals files)))))\n657:       (doseq [l lanes]\n658:         (is (= (count (files l)) (:total (committed-closure l))))\n659:         (is (every? #(seq (:classes %)) (:files (committed-closure l))))))))\n660: \n661: \n662: (deftest independent-traversal-agrees-with-the-committed-closure\n663:   (doseq [l lanes]\n664:     (testing (str \"lane \" l)\n665:       (let [committed (set (map :file (:files (committed-closure l))))\n666:             walked (traverse l)]\n667:         (is (= #{} (set/difference committed walked)) \"committed, not walked\")\n668:         (is (= #{} (set/difference walked committed)) \"walked, not committed\")))))\n669: \n670: \n671: (deftest gate-passes-on-the-current-tree\n672:   (let [r @current]\n673:     (is (= 155 (count (closure-files))) \"the union of the three lanes\")\n674:     (is (= (count (closure-files)) (:scanned r)))\n675:     (is (= [] (:errors r)))\n676:     (is (= [] (:arm-violations r)))\n677:     (is (= [] (:effect-violations r)))\n678:     (is (= :pass (:verdict r)))))\n679: \n680: \n681: (deftest list-1-equals-the-observed-arms\n682:   (testing \"every list-1 file is in the closure and still holds a host arm\"\n683:     (let [observed (set (keep (fn [[f r]] (when (seq (:arms r)) f)) (:observed @current)))]\n684:       (is (= (set (keys list-1)) observed)))))\n685: \n686: \n687: (deftest list-2-equals-the-observed-calls\n688:   (testing \"every permitted count is the observed count (no slack)\"\n689:     (let [observed (into {} (keep (fn [[f r]]\n690:                                     (when (seq (:effects r))\n691:                                       [f (update-vals (:effects r) count)]))\n692:                                   (:observed @current)))]\n693:       (is (= list-2 observed)))))\n694: \n695: \n696: (defn- outside\n697:   \"The first closure .cljc file outside m with no arms and no effect calls.\"\n698:   [m]\n699:   (first (for [[f r] (:observed @current)\n700:                :when (and (not (lane-specific? f)) (not (contains? m f))\n701:                           (empty? (:arms r)) (empty? (:effects r)))]\n702:            f)))\n703: \n704: \n705: (deftest an-injected-host-arm-outside-list-1-fails-the-gate\n706:   (let [target (outside list-1)\n707:         sources (update (read-sources (closure-files)) target str\n708:                         \"\\n(def injected #?(:clj (java.lang.Math/abs -1) :cljs 1))\\n\")\n709:         r (gate sources list-1 list-2)]\n710:     (is (some? target))\n711:     (is (= :fail (:verdict r)))\n712:     (is (= [target] (map :file (:arm-violations r))))\n713:     (is (= [] (:effect-violations r)))))\n714: \n715: \n716: (deftest an-injected-random-uuid-outside-list-2-fails-the-gate\n717:   (let [target (outside list-2)\n718:         sources (update (read-sources (closure-files)) target str\n719:                         \"\\n(def injected (random-uuid))\\n\")\n720:         r (gate sources list-1 list-2)]\n721:     (is (some? target))\n722:     (is (= :fail (:verdict r)))\n723:     (is (= [{:file target :kind :random-uuid :count 1 :allowed 0}]\n724:            (map #(dissoc % :lines) (:effect-violations r))))\n725:     (is (= [] (:arm-violations r)))))\n726: \n727: \n728: (deftest a-scan-failure-is-not-a-pass\n729:   (testing \"zero files read\"\n730:     (let [r (gate {} list-1 list-2)]\n731:       (is (= :scan-failure (:verdict r)))\n732:       (is (= 0 (:scanned r)))))\n733:   (testing \"a closure file that cannot be read\"\n734:     (let [r (gate (assoc (read-sources (closure-files)) \"src/cljc/no/such.cljc\" nil)\n735:                   list-1 list-2)]\n736:       (is (= :scan-failure (:verdict r)))\n737:       (is (= [\"src/cljc/no/such.cljc\"] (map first (:errors r)))))))\n738: \n739: \n740: (defn- sha-256\n741:   [file]\n742:   (let [d (java.security.MessageDigest/getInstance \"SHA-256\")]\n743:     (apply str (map #(format \"%02x\" (bit-and % 0xff))\n744:                     (.digest d (java.nio.file.Files/readAllBytes (.toPath (io/file file))))))))\n745: \n746: \n747: (deftest corpus-bytes-match-the-frozen-hash-set\n748:   (testing \"H0 (d): the Jing corpus and codec wire fixtures, byte-identical\"\n749:     (let [{:keys [roots files]} (edn/read-string (slurp \"docs/design/host-boundary/corpus-sha256.edn\"))\n750:           on-disk (into (sorted-set)\n751:                         (for [r roots\n752:                               f (file-seq (io/file r))\n753:                               :when (.isFile ^java.io.File f)]\n754:                           (str/replace (.getPath ^java.io.File f) \"\\\\\" \"/\")))]\n755:       (is (= 18 (count files)))\n756:       (is (= (set (keys files)) on-disk))\n757:       (doseq [[f h] files]\n758:         (is (= h (sha-256 f)) f)))))\n759: \n760: \n761: (deftest exemptions-and-resolution\n762:   (testing \"§3.3 patterns are exempt; a value arm is not\"\n763:     (is (= [] (non-exempt-arms (read-forms \"(try 1 (catch #?(:clj Exception :cljs :default) e e))\"))))\n764:     (is (= [] (non-exempt-arms (read-forms \"(ns a (:require #?(:clj [x :as y] :cljs [z :as y])))\"))))\n765:     (is (= [] (non-exempt-arms (read-forms \"(def s #?(:clj (Object.) :cljs (js-obj)))\"))))\n766:     (is (= 1 (count (non-exempt-arms (read-forms \"(def n #?(:clj 1 :cljs 2))\"))))))\n767:   (testing \"locals, file defs and quoted forms are not core calls\"\n768:     (is (= [] (effect-calls (read-forms \"(defn f [pr] (pr 1))\"))))\n769:     (is (= [] (effect-calls (read-forms \"(let [gensym inc] (gensym 1))\"))))\n770:     (is (= [] (effect-calls (read-forms \"(declare gensym) (gensym)\"))))\n771:     (is (= [] (effect-calls (read-forms \"(def code '(println 1))\"))))\n772:     (is (= [:random-uuid :print] (map first (effect-calls (read-forms \"(random-uuid) (println 1)\")))))))"}]}],"meta":{"source":"tool","messageId":"487004f7-2f79-428d-ace8-f35721c7e255"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"adversarial analysis of the gates:\n\n1. Exclusions are applied by reading forms ✓ (read-forms with :preserve, exclusions against ReaderConditional structures, not text). Skipping comments ✓.\n\n2. all-arms expansion in effect-calls: non-splicing rc at top level becomes (do arm1 arm2...) — walks all lanes' code ✓. In file-scope, ns-form uses splice-all ✓.\n\n3. Potential weakness: `effect-kind`'s `core` logic: `(and (contains? core-ns q) (or q core?))` — for unqualified symbols q is nil, contains? core-ns nil is true, (or nil core?) = core? (not shadowed) ✓. Qualified cljs.core/clojure.core also count. Qualified `js/console...` is handled. `str/includes? n \"SecureRandom\"` also matches names like `mySecureRandomThing` — over-matching is on the safe side (more detections → gated by list-2 ceilings, and list-2 = observed so no problem).\n\n4. Possibility of missing effect calls: symbols via refers — resolve-m handles refers for unqualified symbols; aliases for qualified. However, if a file requires [clojure.string :as str] and calls (str/...), no problem. If a file uses `println` via `:refer` from another ns… refers map handles it. If there's an unqualified call where the name is shadowed by a file's defs (e.g., the file defines its own `println`)? shadowed covers defs ✓.\n\n5. walk-fn arity tail parsing: heuristic; may mis-parse exotic fn forms and miss bindings → false positive (extra detections) rather than misses… no wait, missing bindings means a local named `pr` gets counted as core's print → over-count → should fail on list-2 equivalence test (list-2-equals-the-observed-calls asserts exact match with observed counts). Current tree passes with exact counts, so on today's tree resolution is validated. Possibility of under-count: quoted forms are skipped ✓ ('quote is skipped), but syntax-quote (`) is NOT skipped! (#{'quote 'comment 'ns} h) — what about the `` ` `` form? Syntax-quote reads as a seq whose head is…? Does tools.reader return a syntax-quote as a form with `clojure.core/seq`? Actually, syntax-quote expansion happens at read time: `(foo)` reads as (clojure.core/seq (clojure.core/concat ...)) — those contain symbols like 'foo as quoted values… a println inside a syntax-quoted form appears as a quoted symbol within the concat list — a bare symbol within a data list. walk visits symbols anywhere within a seq, so a syntax-quoted `(println 1)` would count as a call. This is a false positive (over-count), in the fail-closed direction; on today's tree the observed counts match the design. No problem — the gate can only over-detect, never under-detect… except: symbols inside vectors within syntax-quote are also walked. OK.\n\nDirection of real under-count risk: `walk` skips the entire 'ns form for effects (no problem, ns doesn't contain calls), skips quote/comment. What about method calls like `.println`? Not a core call. `Thread/sleep` is covered by qualified. `(System/currentTimeMillis)` is also covered. `js/Date.now` — does `(= q \"js\") (str/starts-with? n \"Date\")` cover js/Date.now? Symbol js/Date.now has name \"Date.now\", starts-with \"Date\" ✓.\n\n6. Negative tests: NEG1 appends an rc with different arms (:clj (java.lang.Math/abs -1) :cljs 1) — not hint-only (arms differ), not an exclusion target → arm violation exactly 1; asserts effect violations 0 — `(java.lang.Math/abs -1)` is not an effect kind ✓. NEG2 `(random-uuid)` → exactly 1 effect violation allowed 0; arm violations 0 ✓. Targets are programmatically chosen from files with no arms/effects outside the list — in memory only, `(update (read-sources ...) target str ...)` — the actual sources on disk are unmodified ✓. Both assert exact violation lists. Genuine tests.\n\n7. Scan failures: empty {} → :scan-failure (empty? scanned) ✓; nil text → error \"cannot read file\" → scan-failure with filename specified ✓. Distinguished from pass ✓.\n\n8. Honesty of list-1: the 16 :h0-unlisted entries each have line comments; the test `list-1-equals-the-observed-arms` asserts set equality between list-1 keys and observed arm files — i.e., list-1 cannot contain stale entries nor miss files with arms. Does this weaken the freeze? The gate's promise (§8.1) is \"no non-excluded arms outside list 1\" — adding 16 files to list 1 means their existing arms are grandfathered in, and new arms in those files are permitted (because the files are on list 1)! Wait — arm violations are per-file, not per-line: a file on list 1 can later gain new non-excluded arms without failing. That's also the design's granularity (\"files permitted to have non-excluded host arms\") — list 1 is file-granular by design. Therefore :h0-unlisted files are permitted at the design's own granularity; but the design says list 1 \"must match the H0 baseline per category…bidirectional differences are H0 findings to be resolved before H1\". The author recorded F1 with bidirectional diffs and tagged 16 as :h0-unlisted to keep the gate green. Is that acceptable H0 behavior? The design says findings should be resolved before H1, and the author escalated to the Architect. The gate still detects new arms in files not on the list, and list-2 caps effect counts per file+kind (effect ceiling is count-granular, so new random-uuids in listed files still fail). For arms, listed files are not line-capped — a design-inherent property. My judgment: acceptable as H0 with F1 explicitly unresolved before H1 (author's own gating). However, the 16 :h0-unlisted files constitute a substantive widening beyond §8.1's baseline — flag for Architect; the report did so.\n\nHmm, but a subtle point: is there a risk that these 16 arms should have been excluded (i.e., is the exclusion logic too narrow)? Example: :78 instance? Long/Double is a substantive host arm. No problem.\n\n9. Independence of walk B: uses tools.reader + its own select-arms/libspec-deps; shares nothing with tools.namespace (closure.clj uses parse/read-ns-decl + deps-from-ns-decl). The resolution rule (lane-file) is duplicated but that's a design-fixed rule — acceptable, disclosed. Does walk B handle #?@ within ns? select-arms splices ✓ — precisely the r3 defect class. libspec-deps: :as-alias only (no :as/:refer etc.) → not a dep ✓; string libspecs → [] ✓; prefix lists handled ✓. Independence claim holds.\n\n10. Closure tool under-inclusion: read-ns-decl with tools.reader's :read-cond :allow handles splicing natively ✓. strip-nils: postwalk removes nils from vectors/lists within ns decls — wait, danger: strip-nils removes nil from any vector in the ns form… `#?(:cljd nil :clj [x])` reads as nil under cljd features. But legitimately… nil cannot be a libspec so removal is safe. But could it remove nils from metadata or change semantics? Only ns decls, only nil removal — matches the compiler (which ignores nil libspecs). OK. However: on the :cljd lane, features #{:cljd :clj} — `#?(:cljd nil :clj [x])` picks the :cljd arm = nil → stripped → dep dropped. Correct (the cljd compiler does the same).\n\nAlso read-ns-decl reads the first form that looks like an ns decl; if a file has a shebang or comment… no problem.\n\n11. Corpus: 18 files, tests assert exact set and digests ✓, bb script regenerates/checks ✓. SHA-256 vs BLAKE3 rule disclosed.\n\nNext (d) self-verify F2: grep random-uuid in the worktree's src/cljc (should be 27 lines in src/cljc; 21 in closures), grep for things that require dao.await / yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve.\n\n(e) Scope: confirm deps.edn/bb.edn in the host-h0 worktree are unmodified (no :hb alias), nothing else under src/. Quick grep. Also confirm closure output exists.\n\nLet me run these greps:\n- grep \"random-uuid\" in host-h0/src/cljc → count lines.\n- grep \"dao.await\\|dao\\.await\" requires in src → files that require it.\n- grep \":hb\" in host-h0's deps.edn/bb.edn → should not exist.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll verify F2 myself and check scope (deps.edn/bb.edn untouched, requirers of dao.await).\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_3d4529fc4d8c40ae928455f9","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"random-uuid","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld