ething requires it, at which point it\n478: enters the closure and the gate sees it. The five out-of-closure sites are\n479: recorded for the deferred design (§9.1) as reachable only from tests or\n480: not at all. The 21: `dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc:27,185`; `memory_log.cljc:73`;\n481: `ws.cljc:122`; `remote.cljc:1249`; `remote_pair.cljc:180`;\n482: `remote_route.cljc:173`; `journal.cljc:296`; `dao/jing/content/step.cljc:132`;\n483: `dao/lease.cljc:594`; `dao/space/store/fs.cljc:137,351`;\n484: `yin/vm/linker.cljc:1685`; `yin/vm/ucf/custody.cljc:46`;\n485: `yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:1507`; `yin/vm/telemetry.cljc:112`;\n486: `yin/repl.cljc:667,668,733,918`; `yin/repl/dht.cljc:117`.\n487: \n488: Other sources, as the H0 gate resolves them (V): `rand` at\n489: `rpc.cljc:114-116`, `rand-int` at `jing/dht.cljc:373`; secure generators at\n490: `space/dht.cljc:142-151` and `sign.cljc:119-123`, plus `sign.cljc:79`, the\n491: deterministic seed-replay proxy, which matches by name and sits in list 2's\n492: ceiling for that file with a comment (§2.5 rules it internal); `gensym` at\n493: three sites; clocks at `main.cljc:1242,1275,1408,1435,1542` (driver),\n494: `driver.clj:169,206` (JVM lane) and the three ws seams (`ws/jvm.clj:422`,\n495: `ws/node.cljs:249`, `ws/dart.cljd:176`, seam-private); ambient at\n496: `fs.cljc:92,136,271-273`, `repl.cljc:275-277`, `main.cljc`; printing at\n497: `main.cljc`: **13 resolved calls** (`println`, `print`, `flush`,\n498: `js/console.log`; r3's \"19\" counted lines by text, including `*out*`\n499: mentions and docstrings, and is withdrawn); `antlr/repl.cljc:71` is not a\n500: host call (§3.1). Timers the gate sees: `driver.clj:173` (`Thread/sleep`),\n501: `datagram/jvm.clj:70` and the three waitset drivers; `storage.cljc:224-227`\n502: is a promise facade, not a timer, and `main.cljc:1321,1343` construct\n503: threads (driver). All are deferred-scope entries (§9) or seam/driver\n504: sites; none is in an H0-H4 file.\n505: \n506: ### 3.3 Exempt dialect syntax\n507: \n508: Not host contact; the H0 gate exempts them by pattern: `catch` type arms;\n509: `^long`/`^bytes`/`^String` hints; protocol and interface names in `deftype`\n510: bodies and `print-method`; `exists?`; `js-obj`/`(Object.)` opaque sentinels;\n511: require arms whose only purpose is an alias.\n512: \n513: ## 4. The host-implementation contract\n514: \n515: ### 4.1 Stream implementations and their seams (external contact)\n516: \n517: Unchanged from the tree for sockets (V) and listed for completeness; the\n518: storage, entropy and parser rows are deferred (§9).\n519: \n520: +----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n521: | Implementation             | Portable core (V)                          | Seam value a host supplies                            | Status                      |\n522: +============================+============================================+=======================================================+=============================+\n523: | Ring buffer, memory log,   | `dao.stream.ringbuffer`, `.memory_log`,    | None. (They mint identities today, §3.2: deferred.)   | Existing                    |\n524: | remote channel, waitset,   | `.remote_channel`, `.waitset`, `.observe`, |                                                       |                             |\n525: | middleware, apply          | `.middleware`, `.apply`                    |                                                       |                             |\n526: +----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n527: | WebSocket                  | `dao.stream.ws`                            | `{:connect! :bind! :unbind!}` (`host.cljc:20-33`)     | Existing                    |\n528: +----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n529: | Datagram and UDP           | `dao.stream.datagram`, `.udp`              | `bind!` (`datagram.cljc:15-23`)                       | Existing                    |\n530: +----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n531: | Durable journal and the    | `dao.stream.journal` over `dao.jing.file`  | Deferred (§9.2)                                       | Deferred                    |\n532: | storage beneath it         | and `store.fs`                             |                                                       |                             |\n533: +----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n534: | Entropy                    | Deferred                                   | Deferred (§9.1)                                       | Deferred                    |\n535: +----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n536: | Parser stage               | `yang.python.antlr.*`                      | Deferred (§9.3)                                       | Deferred                    |\n537: +----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n538: | wasm import surface        | `dao.stream.wasm.md` §1                    | The seven imports                                     | Existing spec               |\n539: +----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n540: \n541: Seam rule (`abi.md` §6-§7 as acceptance): a seam entry is implementation-\n542: private, called only by the stream implementation that owns it; it takes\n543: host arguments and returns or deposits plain data; it never invokes\n544: application code; it classifies host errors into data; what it cannot do it\n545: answers as a qualified unsupported outcome. A map of functions that portable\n546: application code calls to reach the world is a host service and is rejected\n547: (`abi.md:143-148`); none exists in H0-H4.\n548: \n549: ### 4.2 The primitive profile: exact manifest (P)\n550: \n551: `dao.host.*` (OQ2 adopted) is a namespace family whose files contain only\n552: reader-conditional entries and docstrings stating each entry's law, kind (P\n553: pure, M mutating per §2.4) and oracle. Table A is the profile (76 entries);\n554: table B the portable code replacing host libraries; table C the runtime\n555: prerequisites.\n556: \n557: **Table A: profile entries.**\n558: \n559: +--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n560: | Namespace          | Entries (consolidated from, V)                                                                       | N   | Slice |\n561: +====================+======================================================================================================+=====+=======+\n562: | `dao.host.integer` | From `yin.vm.integer.host` (all 25, P): `big-carrier?`, `exact-integer?`, `safe-native?`,            | 28  | H1    |\n563: |                    | `host-float?`, `nan-float?`, `infinite-float?`, `promote`, `from-native`, `demote`, `to-native`,     |     |       |\n564: |                    | `native->double`, `trunc-native`, `add`, `sub`, `mul`, `quot-trunc`, `rem-trunc`, `compare-big`,     |     |       |\n565: |                    | `bit-and-big`, `bit-or-big`, `bit-xor-big`, `shift-left-big`, `shift-right-big`,                     |     |       |\n566: |     