                |     |       |\n580: +--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n581: | `dao.host.bytes`   | P: `bytes?`, `alloc` (fresh, zeroed), `length`, `get`, `slice` (fresh), `equal?`, `from-vector`      | 10  | H1    |\n582: |                    | (fresh), `to-vector`; M: `set!`, `copy!` (memmove). From `chunks.cljc:6-32`,                         |     |       |\n583: |                    | `jing/dht.cljc:100-121`, `linker.cljc:1232`, `sign.cljc:55-59`, `boring.cljc:46-51`,                 |     |       |\n584: |                    | `datagram.cljc:63-66`, `debruijn.cljc:167`. (`codec.cljc:45` reads it after the codec track's C4,    |     |       |\n585: |                    | §8.3.)                                                                                               |     |       |\n586: +--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n587: | `dao.host.text`    | P: `unit-count`, `code-unit`, `units->string`, `utf8-encode` (fresh bytes; refuses an unpaired       | 6   | H1    |\n588: |                    | surrogate), `utf8-decode` (refuses invalid sequences; never substitutes U+FFFD), `nfc` (Unicode      |     |       |\n589: |                    | 16.0) from `data.cljc:119-173`, `debruijn.cljc:241,310-321`, `jing.cljc:65-71,131-135`,              |     |       |\n590: |                    | `sign.cljc:62-66`.                                                                                   |     |       |"}]}],"meta":{"source":"tool","messageId":"7d211f87-dd68-4338-a3cf-525da5c2aaf6"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"continue reading — the reconciliation of §8.1, §9.1, §10, §14. Selectively read the remaining sections: grep the reconciliation part of the revised §8.1 and §10. First read the §8.1 region. From the r6 layout, §8.1 was