efused by the canonical codec (corpus  | the adopted closure, no executable reference to `MessageDigest`,  |\n808: |       |        | `unpaired-surrogate` class), so no persisted address changes. Base64 made      | `Blake3`, `noble`, `blake3_dart`, `package:crypto`,               |\n809: |       |        | portable (table B; a replacement).                                             | `ed25519_edwards`, `goog.crypt.base64` outside `dao/host/`, and   |\n810: |       |        |                                                                                | for the Ed25519 names outside `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`           |\n811: |       |        |                                                                                | (`generate`); scan errors reported distinctly.                    |\n812: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n813: | H4    | migr.  | Portable Jing CBOR writer over `dao.host.*`; `dao.jing.cbor.boring` and        | Green; `cbor-v1.json` byte-identical on three lanes with the      |\n814: |       |        | `dao.jing.cbor.cljd` deleted; Boring stays for `dao.stream.cbor.boring` and    | errata skips unchanged (`documented-skips-match-the-errata-and-   |\n815: |       |        | the Dart `cbor` package for `dao.stream.cbor.cljd` (OQ4). A measurement:       | leave-no-case-unrun`); fixtures, DHT and linker image goldens     |\n816: |       |        | corpus and one large module image, old writer against new, JVM and Node.       | unchanged; the measurement in the slice report, no threshold      |\n817: |       |        |                                                                                | (OQ7). Slow tier once after landing.                              |\n818: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n819: \n820: Dependencies: H0, H1, H2 in order; H3 and H4 after H2, in either order.\n821: \n822: ### 8.1 List 1: the files permitted non-exempt host arms, baseline and final\n823: \n824: The gate never promises \"no arms across `src/cljc`\", only \"no non-exempt\n825: arms outside list 1\". List 1 is generated at H0 by the gate from the actual\n826: closure (every closure file holding a non-exempt arm, §3.3) and must equal\n827: the **H0 baseline** below, by category, with each file's reason; a\n828: difference either way is an H0 finding to resolve before H1. The baseline\n829: is today's tree: the seven `dao.host.*` files are **planned additions**\n830: (five in H1, two in H3) and are not part of the H0 baseline; they are\n831: marked as such in the table.\n832: \n833: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n834: | Category (reason)          | Files (V, from §1 and the closure)                                                              | After H4                    |\n835: +============================+=================================================================================================+=============================+\n836: | H1-H4 migration sources    | `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`,                  | Removed from list 1 as each |\n837: |                            | `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (the Dart Jing writer; a lane-specific file counted here,    | slice lands; `sign.cljc`    |\n838: |                            | not under seams), `dao/jing.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn.cljc`,           | stays for `generate` only;  |\n839: |                            | `yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc` (table C blocks stay, as  | three of these files are    |\n840: |                            | exempt protocol syntax), `dao/stream/chunks.cljc`, `dao/stream/base64.cljc`,                    | deleted (§8.1 paragraph).   |\n841: |                            | `dao/jing/dht.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker.cljc`, `dao/stream/datagram.cljc` (bytes arms only); and,   |                             |\n842: |                            | from H0's finding (§3.1, profile consumers, H2): `yin/vm.cljc:404`, `dao/space/index.cljc:78`,  |                             |\n843: |                            | `yin/repl/query.cljc:460`, `yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc:32`, `yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:282`,         |                             |\n844: |                            | `yang/php.cljc:95,98`, `yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc:439`,                                |                             |\n845: |                            | `yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc:130`, `yang/antlr/packet.cljc:67`.                       |                             |\n846: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n847: | Profile (the arms belong   | Baseline: `dao/data/arrays.cljc`. Planned additions, not in the H0 baseline:                    | Stay; the seven additions   |\n848: | here by design)            | `dao/host/{integer,float,number,bytes,text,hash,sign}.cljc` (P; five join list 1 at H1, two at  | are on list 1 from the      |\n849: |                            | H3).                                                                                            | slice that creates them.    |\n850: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n851: | Retained runtime           | `dao/data/btree.cljc` (atomic flag `:102-119`, weak and soft references `:212-245`: substantive | Stay, with the table C      |\n852: | prerequisites (table C)    | arms, not protocol syntax, retained by design); `dao/data/btree/storage.cljc` (promise facade,  | reason recorded in the      |\n853: |                            | deferred §9.1); `dao/pretty.cljc` (`StringWriter`/pprint, display only, §3.1).                  | gate's list.                |\n854: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n855: | Codec-track files          | `dao/stream/ws.cljc`, `transit.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`, `cbor/boring.cljc`, `codec.cljc`. (H0:       | Stay; owned by that track;  |\n856: | (untouched by this track)  | `remote_channel.cljc` and `ws_project.cljc` carry only exempt `catch` arms and are not on the   | `codec.cljc:45` after C4.   |\n857: |                            | generated list; `jing/stream.cljc` is not in the closure. All three remain codec-track files    |                             |\n858: |                            | under §8.3; they are simply not list-1 entries.)                                                |                             |\n859: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n860: | Dialect arms (H0 finding,  | `dao/space/query.cljc` (`:808`), `yang/clojure.cljc` (`:375`), `yin/vm/engine.cljc` (`:929`): a | Stay.                       |\n861: | retained)                  | runtime type name in diagnostic text; `yin/repl/adapter.cljc` (`:58`), `yin/repl/dht.cljc`      |                             |\n862: |                            | (`:104`): the dialect's EDN reader under two namespaces; `dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc` (`:168`): |                             |\n863: |                            | the in-memory stream implementation's own host atom test (an implementation-private arm, §4.1). |                             |\n864: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------